      </dt> <dd class="col content" data-v-30f75881><div data-v-30f75881>
          © The Author(s), 2024. Published by Cambridge University Press
        </div></dd></div></dl> <hr aria-hidden="true" class="abstract-divider separator default" data-v-7036083a data-v-30f75881></div> <!----> <div id="content-container" class="content-container content-link-accessible" data-v-efda3ce4><div class="content-box" style="display:;"><div class="article research-article NLM">

<div class="body">
<div class="sec intro" data-magellan-destination="sec1" id="sec1">

<h2 class="A"><span class="label">1</span> Introduction</h2>
<p class="p"> The moduli spaces of stable curves <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline11.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="49" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline11.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> are smooth and proper over the integers, and this implies strong restrictions on the motivic structures, such as <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline12.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="9" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline12.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\ell $
</span></span>
</span>
</span>-adic Galois representations, that can appear in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline13.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="89" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline13.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^*({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Widely believed conjectures regarding analytic continuations and functional equations for <em class="italic">L</em>-functions lead to precise predictions, by Chenevier and Lannes, about which such structures can appear in degrees less than or equal to 22 [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r10"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Chenevier and Lannes</span>10</a>, Theorem F]. These predictions are consistent with all previously known results on <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline14.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="90" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline14.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^*({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Recent work inspired by these predictions confirms their correctness in all degrees less than or equal to 12 [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r4"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Bergström, Faber and Payne</span>4</a>, <a class="xref bibr" href="#r8"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Canning, Larson and Payne</span>8</a>]. Here, we introduce new methods to systematically study the motivic structures in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline15.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="91" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline15.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^k({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline16.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="57" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline16.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$k&gt; 12$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and confirm these predictions in degrees <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline17.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="17" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline17.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$13$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline18.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="18" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline18.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$14$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline19.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="17" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline19.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$15$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
<p class="p"> Throughout, we write <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline20.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="56" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline20.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^*(X)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for the rational singular cohomology of a scheme or Deligne-Mumford stack <em class="italic">X</em> endowed with its associated Hodge structure or <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline21.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="9" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline21.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\ell $
</span></span>
</span>
</span>-adic Galois representation and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline22.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="70" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline22.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^*(X)^{\mathrm {ss}}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for its semi-simplification. Let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline23.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="99" height="23" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline23.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathsf {L} := H^2(\mathbb {P}^1)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline24.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="159" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline24.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathsf {S}}_{12} := H^{11}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,11})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p><div class="statement theorem" data-magellan-destination="theorem1" id="theorem1">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Theorem 1.1.</span> For all <em class="italic">g</em> and <em class="italic">n</em>, we have <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline25.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="205" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline25.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{13}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})^{\mathrm {ss}} \cong \bigoplus \mathsf {L}{\mathsf {S}}_{12}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline26.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="186" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline26.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{14}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})^{\mathrm {ss}} \cong \bigoplus \mathsf {L}^{7}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Moreover, for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline27.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline27.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g \geq 2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, we have <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline28.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="215" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline28.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{15} ({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})^{\mathrm {ss}} \cong \bigoplus {\mathsf {L}}^2 {\mathsf {S}}_{12}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
</div>
<p class="p"> Theorem <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem1">1.1</a> confirms the predictions of Chenevier and Lannes for motivic weights <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline29.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="56" height="17" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline29.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$k \leq 15$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Note that the Hodge structure on the cohomology of a smooth and proper Deligne–Mumford stack such as <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline30.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="49" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline30.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is semi-simple, so the semi-simplification in Theorem <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem1">1.1</a> is relevant only when considering <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline31.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="9" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline31.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\ell $
</span></span>
</span>
</span>-adic Galois representations.</p>
<p class="p"> The proof of Theorem <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem1">1.1</a> uses the inductive structure of the boundary of the moduli space and the maps induced by tautological morphisms between moduli spaces, as do the proofs of the precursor results mentioned above. Recall that the collection of tautological rings <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline32.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="220" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline32.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$RH^*({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n}) \subset H^*({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is the smallest collection of subrings that is closed under pushforward and pullback for the tautological morphisms induced by gluing, forgetting and permuting marked points. For many inductive arguments, including those used here, it suffices to consider the operations that produce cohomology classes on moduli spaces of larger dimension from those on moduli spaces of smaller dimension.</p><div class="statement definition" data-magellan-destination="definition1" id="definition1">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Definition 1.2.</span> A <em class="italic">semi-tautological extension</em> (STE) is a collection of subrings <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline33.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="84" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline33.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$S^*({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline34.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="90" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline34.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^*({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> that contains the tautological subrings <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline35.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="103" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline35.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$RH^*({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and is closed under pullback by forgetting and permuting marked points and under pushforward for gluing marked points.</p>
</div>
<p class="p"> Examples of STEs include the trivial extension <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline36.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="38" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline36.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$RH^*$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, the full cohomology rings <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline37.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="24" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline37.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^*$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and the collection of subrings generated by algebraic cycle classes. Not every STE is closed under the additional tautological operations induced by push-forward for forgetting marked points and pullback for gluing marked points. However, the main examples we study here are indeed closed under all of the tautological operations (see Proposition <a class="xref statement" href="#proposition2">2.4</a>).</p>
<p class="p"> Note that any intersection of STEs is an STE. An STE is <em class="italic">finitely generated</em> if it is the smallest STE that contains a given finite subset (or, equivalently, the union of finitely many <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline38.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="15" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline38.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {Q}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>-vector subspaces) of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline39.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="135" height="28" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline39.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\coprod _{g,n} H^*({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. A finitely generated STE is suitable for combinatorial study via algebraic operations on decorated graphs. See [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r22">22</a>, <a class="xref bibr" href="#r31"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Pixton</span>31</a>] for discussions of the graphical algebra underlying the tautological ring, and [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r24"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Payne and Willwacher</span>24</a>, <a class="xref bibr" href="#r25"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Payne and Willwacher</span>25</a>] for applications of such operadic methods, with not necessarily tautological decorations, to the weight spectral sequence for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline40.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="48" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline40.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{g,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Every STE that we consider is <em class="italic">motivic</em>, meaning that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline41.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="201" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline41.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$S^*({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n}) \subset H^*({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is a sub-Hodge structure and its base change to <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline42.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="23" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline42.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {Q}_\ell $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is preserved by the Galois action.</p><div class="statement theorem" data-magellan-destination="theorem2" id="theorem2">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Theorem 1.3.</span> For any fixed degree <em class="italic">k</em>, the STE generated by </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU1" id="eqnU1">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu1.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="542" height="38" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu1.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}\left\{H^{k'}({\overline{\mathcal{M}}}_{g',n'}) : k' \leq k, g' &lt; \tfrac{3}{2}k' + 1, \ n' \leq k', \ 4g' - 4 + n' \geq k' \right\}\end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">contains <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline43.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="92" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline43.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^k({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for all <em class="italic">g</em> and <em class="italic">n</em>.</p>
</div>
<p class="p"> In particular, there is a finitely generated STE that contains <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline44.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="91" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline44.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^k({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for all <em class="italic">g</em> and <em class="italic">n</em>.</p><div class="statement corollary" data-magellan-destination="corollary1" id="corollary1">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Corollary 1.4.</span> For each <em class="italic">k</em>, there are only finitely many isomorphism classes of simple Hodge structures (respectively, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline45.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="9" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline45.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\ell $
</span></span>
</span>
</span>-adic Galois representations) in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline46.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="158" height="30" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline46.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\bigoplus _{g,n} H^k({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})^{\mathrm {ss}}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
</div>
<p class="p"> We developed the notion of STEs to study nontrivial extensions of tautological rings, such as the STE generated by <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline47.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="102" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline47.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{11}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,11})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, but the same methods also yield new results on the tautological ring itself. We apply the explicit bounds in Theorem <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem2">1.3</a>, together with new tools and results for small <em class="italic">g</em>, <em class="italic">n</em> and <em class="italic">k</em> to prove the following. At the level of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline48.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="15" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline48.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {Q}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>-vector spaces, we identify <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline49.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="91" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline49.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H_k({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> with <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline50.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="138" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline50.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{2d_{g,n} - k}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, where <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline51.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="151" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline51.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$d_{g,n} := 3g-3+n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is the dimension of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline52.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="49" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline52.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Similarly, when <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline53.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="18" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline53.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$S^*$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is an STE, we write <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline54.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="86" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline54.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$S_k({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for the <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline55.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="15" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline55.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {Q}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>-vector space <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline56.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="133" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline56.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$S^{2d_{g,n} - k}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p><div class="statement theorem" data-magellan-destination="theorem3" id="theorem3">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Theorem 1.5.</span> The tautological ring <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline57.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="103" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline57.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$RH^*({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> contains </p><ol class="list number nomark">
<li class="list-item">

<p class="p"><span class="label">1.</span> 
<span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline58.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="95" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline58.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^4({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n}),$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for all <em class="italic">g</em> and <em class="italic">n</em>,</p>
</li>
<li class="list-item">

<p class="p"><span class="label">2.</span> 
<span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline59.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="96" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline59.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^6({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n}),$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline60.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="58" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline60.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g \geq 10$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>,</p>
</li>
<li class="list-item">

<p class="p"><span class="label">3.</span> 
<span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline61.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="97" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline61.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H_{k}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n}),$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for even <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline62.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="57" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline62.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$k \leq 14$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, for all <em class="italic">g</em> and <em class="italic">n</em>.</p>
</li>
</ol>
</div>
<div class="statement theorem" data-magellan-destination="theorem4" id="theorem4">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Theorem 1.6.</span> The STE generated by <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline63.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="102" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline63.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{11}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,11})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> contains <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline64.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="96" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline64.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H_{13}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for all <em class="italic">g</em> and <em class="italic">n</em>.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement theorem" data-magellan-destination="theorem5" id="theorem5">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Theorem 1.7.</span> The STE generated by <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline65.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="102" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline65.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{11}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,11})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline66.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="101" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline66.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{15}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,15})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> contains <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline67.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="97" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline67.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H_{15}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for all <em class="italic">g</em> and <em class="italic">n</em>.</p>
</div>
<p class="p"> Theorem <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem3">1.5</a>(1) confirms a prediction of Arbarello and Cornalba from the 1990s; they proposed that their inductive method used to prove that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline68.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="89" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline68.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^2({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is tautological should also apply in degree 4 [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r1"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Arbarello and Cornalba</span>1</a>, p. 1]. Shortly thereafter, Polito confirmed that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline69.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="90" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline69.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^4({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is tautological for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline70.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline70.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g \geq 8$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r32"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Polito</span>32</a>], but the general case remained open until now. Theorem <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem3">1.5</a>(3) implies that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline71.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="184" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline71.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^k({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n}) \cong \bigoplus \mathsf {L}^{k/2}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for even <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline72.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="57" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline72.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$k \leq 14$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. The work of Chenevier and Lannes predicts that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline73.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="92" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline73.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^k({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> should also be isomorphic to <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline74.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="63" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline74.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\bigoplus \mathsf {L}^{k/2}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline75.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="114" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline75.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$k = 16, 18, 20$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. The Hodge and Tate conjectures then predict that these groups are generated by algebraic cycle classes. However, generation by algebraic cycle classes is an open problem except in the cases where <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline76.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="91" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline76.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^k({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is known to be generated by tautological cycle classes.</p>
<p class="p"> By Theorems <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem4">1.6</a> and <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem5">1.7</a>, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline77.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="97" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline77.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H_{13}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline78.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="96" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline78.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H_{15}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> lie in STEs generated by cohomology from genus <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline79.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="7" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline79.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> moduli spaces. On the other hand, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline80.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="96" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline80.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H_{17}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> requires genus <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline81.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="10" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline81.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> data because <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline82.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="171" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline82.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_{17}H^{17}({\mathcal {M}}_{2,14})\neq 0$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r13"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Faber and Pandharipande</span>13</a>].</p>
<p class="p"> We note that any STE is top-heavy, in the sense that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline83.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="271" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline83.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\dim S^k({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n}) \leq \dim S_k({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline84.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="121" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline84.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$k \leq \dim {\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> (cf. [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r30"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Petersen and Tommasi</span>30</a>]). Moreover, the dimensions in even and odd degrees are unimodal. This is because any STE contains <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline85.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="38" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline85.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$RH^*$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and hence contains an ample class. Multiplication by a suitable power of the ample class gives an injection from <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline86.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="86" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline86.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$S^k({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> to <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline87.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="86" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline87.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$S_k({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
<p class="p"> One could show that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline88.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="91" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline88.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^k({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is generated by tautological cycles in the remaining cases covered by Theorem <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem3">1.5</a>(3) by showing that the pairing on <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline89.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="234" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline89.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$RH^k({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n}) \times RH_k({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is perfect, for example, using <span class="sans-serif">admcycles</span> [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r11"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Delecroix, Schmitt and van Zelm</span>11</a>]. However, computational complexity prevents meaningful progress by brute force. Note that Petersen and Tommasi showed that this pairing is not perfect in general for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline90.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="57" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline90.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$k \geq 22$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r28"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Petersen</span>28</a>, <a class="xref bibr" href="#r30"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Petersen and Tommasi</span>30</a>]. Graber and Pandharipande had previously shown that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline91.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="102" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline91.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{22}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{2,20})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> contains an algebraic cycle class that is not tautological [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r17"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Graber and Pandharipande</span>17</a>].</p><div class="statement conjecture" data-magellan-destination="conjecture1" id="conjecture1">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Conjecture 1.8.</span> The tautological ring <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline92.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="103" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline92.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$RH^*({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> contains <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline93.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="92" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline93.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^k({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for even <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline94.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="57" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline94.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$k \leq 20$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
</div>
<p class="p"> The results above show that Conjecture <a class="xref statement" href="#conjecture1">1.8</a> is true for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline95.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline95.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$k \leq 4$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, and for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline96.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="45" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline96.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$k = 6$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline97.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="57" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline97.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g \geq 10$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. For <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline98.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="57" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline98.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$k \leq 14$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, the conjecture is true if and only if the pairing <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline99.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="234" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline99.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$RH^k({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n}) \times RH_k({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is perfect. The examples of Graber–Pandharipande and Petersen–Tommasi show that the conjectured bound of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline100.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="57" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline100.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$k \leq 20$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is the best possible. As further evidence for Conjecture <a class="xref statement" href="#conjecture1">1.8</a>, we note that the Arbarello–Cornalba induction together with known base cases implies the vanishing of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline101.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="111" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline101.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{16,0}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline102.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="110" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline102.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{18,0}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for all <em class="italic">g</em> and <em class="italic">n</em>, as recently observed by Fontanari [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r15"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Fontanari</span>15</a>].</p>
<p class="p"> The inductive arguments used to study <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline103.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="92" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline103.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{k}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for all <em class="italic">g</em> and <em class="italic">n</em> rely on understanding base cases <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline104.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="104" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline104.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{k'}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g',n'})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, where <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline105.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="17" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline105.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g'$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline106.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="16" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline106.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n'$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> are small relative to <em class="italic">k</em>. As <em class="italic">k</em> grows, more base cases are needed. With the exception of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline107.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="102" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline107.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{11}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,11})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, all base cases required for previous work with <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline108.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="57" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline108.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$k \leq 12$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> have been pure Hodge–Tate [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r1"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Arbarello and Cornalba</span>1</a>, <a class="xref bibr" href="#r4"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Bergström, Faber and Payne</span>4</a>, <a class="xref bibr" href="#r6"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Canning and Larson</span>6</a>]. Substantial work went into establishing these base cases via point counts and other methods. When <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline109.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="56" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline109.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$k \geq 13$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, the problem becomes fundamentally more difficult, as an increasing number of the required base cases are <em class="italic">not</em> pure Hodge–Tate. In particular, previous techniques for handling base cases do not apply.</p>
<p class="p"> The advances presented here depend on a new technique for controlling the pure weight cohomology of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline110.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="49" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline110.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{g,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. A space <em class="italic">X</em> has the <em class="italic">Chow–Künneth generation Property (CKgP)</em> if the tensor product map on Chow groups <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline111.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="250" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline111.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$A_*(X) \otimes A_*(Y) \to A_*(X \times Y)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is surjective for all <em class="italic">Y</em>. If <em class="italic">X</em> is smooth, proper and has the CKgP, then the cycle class map is an isomorphism. However, in several of the base cases needed for our arguments, the smooth and proper moduli space <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline112.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="49" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline112.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> has odd cohomology and hence does not have the CKgP. Nevertheless, we show that the open moduli spaces <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline113.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="48" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline113.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{g,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> do have the CKgP for the relevant pairs <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline114.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="44" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline114.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$(g,n)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. To apply this in the proof of our main results, the key new technical statement is Lemma <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma4">4.3</a>, which says that if <em class="italic">X</em> is smooth and has the CKgP, then <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline115.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="84" height="23" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline115.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_k H^k(X)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is algebraic. This extension of the aforementioned result on the cycle class map to spaces that are not necessarily proper is essential for controlling the motivic structures that appear in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline116.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="91" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline116.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^k({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline117.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="56" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline117.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$k \geq 13$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. For example, using that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline118.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline118.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{3,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> has the CKgP for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline119.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="56" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline119.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n \leq 11$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r5"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Canning and Larson</span>5</a>, Theorem 1.4], we determine the Hodge structures and Galois representations that appear in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline120.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="87" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline120.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^*({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{3,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline121.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="56" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline121.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n \leq 11$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p><div class="statement theorem" data-magellan-destination="theorem6" id="theorem6">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Theorem 1.9.</span> For <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline122.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="56" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline122.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n \leq 11$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline123.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="102" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline123.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^*({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{3,n})^{\mathrm {ss}}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is a polynomial in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline124.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="9" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline124.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathsf {L}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline125.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="27" height="17" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline125.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathsf {S}}_{12}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
</div>
<p class="p"> Bergström and Faber recently used point counting techniques to compute the cohomology of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline126.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline126.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{3,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> as an <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline127.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="21" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline127.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {S}_n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>-equivariant Galois representation for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline128.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="57" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline128.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n \leq 14$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. For <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline129.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline129.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n \geq 9$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, these computations are conditional on the assumption that the only <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline130.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="9" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline130.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\ell $
</span></span>
</span>
</span>-adic Galois representations appearing are those from the list of Chenevier and Lannes [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r3"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Bergström and Faber</span>3</a>]. Theorem <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem6">1.9</a> unconditionally confirms the calculations of Bergström and Faber for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline131.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="45" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline131.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n = 9$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline132.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="18" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline132.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$10$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline133.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="17" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline133.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$11$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
<p class="p"> In order to prove Theorems <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem1">1.1</a>, <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem3">1.5</a>(3) and <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem5">1.7</a>, our inductive arguments require several base cases beyond what was already in the literature. In particular, we prove the following results in genus <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline134.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="10" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline134.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$7$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, which are also of independent interest.</p><div class="statement theorem" data-magellan-destination="theorem7" id="theorem7">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Theorem 1.10.</span> For <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline135.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="46" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline135.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n \leq 3$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, the moduli space <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline136.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline136.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{7,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> has the CKgP and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline137.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="196" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline137.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$R^*({\mathcal {M}}_{7,n}) = A^*({\mathcal {M}}_{7,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
</div>
<p class="p"> Here, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline138.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="21" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline138.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$R^*$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> denotes the subring of the Chow ring <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline139.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="20" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline139.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$A^*$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> generated by tautological cycle classes. Previous results proving that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline140.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="49" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline140.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{g,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> has the CKgP and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline141.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="199" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline141.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$R^*({\mathcal {M}}_{g,n}) = A^*({\mathcal {M}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for small <em class="italic">g</em> and <em class="italic">n</em> have primarily relied on corresponding results for Hurwitz spaces with marked points [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r5"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Canning and Larson</span>5</a>]. Unfortunately, the numerics for degree <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline142.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="9" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline142.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$5$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> covers prevented this technique from working with marked points. Here, we take a new approach to the pentagonal locus, using a modification of Mukai’s construction [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r21"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Mukai</span>21</a>] that includes markings.</p>
</div>
<div class="sec" data-magellan-destination="sec2" id="sec2">

<h2 class="A"><span class="label">2</span> Preliminaries</h2>
<p class="p"> In this section, we establish notation and terminology that we will use throughout the paper and discuss a few basic examples of STEs. We also recall previously known facts about the cohomology groups of moduli spaces, especially in genus 0, 1 and 2, that will be used in the base cases of our inductive arguments.</p>
<div class="sec" data-magellan-destination="sec3" id="sec3">

<h3 class="B"><span class="label">2.1</span> Preliminaries on STEs</h3>
<p class="p"> Recall that an STE is, by definition, closed under the tautological operations given by pushing forward from the boundary or pulling back from moduli spaces with fewer marked points. Let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline143.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="61" height="28" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline143.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\widetilde {\partial \mathcal {M}}_{g,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> denote the normalization of the boundary. The sequence </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU2" id="eqnU2">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu2.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="444" height="28" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu2.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}H^{k-2}(\widetilde{\partial \mathcal{M}}_{g,n}) \to H^{k}({\overline{\mathcal{M}}}_{g,n}) \to W_k H^k({\mathcal{M}}_{g,n})\rightarrow 0\end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">is right exact.</p>
<p class="p"> Let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline144.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="179" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline144.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\pi _i \colon {\mathcal {M}}_{g,n} \to {\mathcal {M}}_{g,n-1}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> be the tautological morphism forgetting the <em class="italic">i</em>th marking, and let </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU3" id="eqnU3">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu3.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="603" height="29" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu3.png" data-zoomable="true">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}\Phi^k_{g,n} := \pi_1^*W_kH^k({\mathcal{M}}_{g,n-1}) + \cdots + \pi_n^*W_kH^k({\mathcal{M}}_{g,n-1}) \subset W_kH^k({\mathcal{M}}_{g,n}). \end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">The following lemma is a cohomological analogue of the “filling criteria” in [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r5"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Canning and Larson</span>5</a>, Section 4].</p>
<p class="p"> We consider the partial order in which <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline145.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="129" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline145.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$(g', n') \prec (g, n)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> if <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline146.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="54" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline146.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g' \leq g$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline147.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="145" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline147.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$2g' + n' \leq 2g + n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline148.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="129" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline148.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$(g',n') \neq (g, n)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. The moduli space <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline149.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="49" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline149.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is stratified according to the topological types of stable curves, and each stratum of the boundary is a finite quotient of a product of moduli spaces <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline150.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="56" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline150.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{g',n'}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, such that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline151.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="129" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline151.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$(g',n') \prec (g,n)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Recall that we write <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline152.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="150" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline152.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$d_{g,n} := 3g - 3 + n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p><div class="statement lemma" data-magellan-destination="lemma1" id="lemma1">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Lemma 2.1.</span> Let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline153.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="18" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline153.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$S^*$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> be an STE, and let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline154.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="122" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline154.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$2g - 2 + n&gt; 0$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. If the canonical map </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqn1" id="eqn1">
<span class="label">(2.1)</span>
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn1.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="485" height="29" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn1.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$ \begin{align} S^{k'}({\overline{\mathcal{M}}}_{g',n'}) \to W_{k'}H^{k'}({\mathcal{M}}_{g',n'})/ \big(\Phi^{k'}_{g',n'} + RH^{k'}({\mathcal{M}}_{g',n'}) \big) \end{align} $$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">is surjective for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline155.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="175" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline155.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$(g',n',k') = (g, n, k)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and all <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline156.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="83" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline156.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$(g', n', k')$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> satisfying </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqn2" id="eqn2">
<span class="label">(2.2)</span>
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn2.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="589" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn2.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$ \begin{align} (g', n') \prec (g, n), \qquad 2d_{g',n'} - k' \leq 2d_{g,n} - k \qquad \text{and} \qquad k' \leq k-2, \end{align} $$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">then <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline157.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="203" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline157.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$S^k({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n}) = H^k({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement other" data-magellan-destination="proof1" id="proof1">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Proof.</span> The proof is by induction on <em class="italic">g</em> and <em class="italic">n</em>. Consider the diagram </p><div class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqn3" id="eqn3">
<span class="label">(2.3)</span>
<div class="figure-thumb"><img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn3.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image" width="556" height="108" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn3.png" data-zoomable="false"></div>
</div>
<p class="p"> Here, we extend <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline158.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="18" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline158.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$S^*$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> to <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline159.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="61" height="28" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline159.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\widetilde {\partial {\mathcal {M}}_{g,n}}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> in the natural way, by summing over components, using the Künneth formula, and taking invariants under automorphisms of the dual graph. We claim that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline160.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="12" height="11" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline160.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\alpha $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is an isomorphism. By the Künneth formula, the domain of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline161.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="12" height="11" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline161.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\alpha $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is a sum of tensor products of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline162.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="85" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline162.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$S^{\ell }({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{\gamma ,\nu })$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> with <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline163.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="79" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline163.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\ell \leq k - 2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline164.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="117" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline164.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$(\gamma , \nu ) \prec (g,n)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Furthermore, by considering dimensions of the cycles involved, we must also have <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline165.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="184" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline165.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$2d_{\gamma ,\nu } - \ell \leq 2d_{g,n} - k$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. This is because we must have <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline166.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="254" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline166.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$k -2- \ell \leq 2(d_{g,n} - 1 - d_{\gamma ,\nu })$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, so that the degree of the other Künneth component does not exceed its real dimension. Now, suppose we are given <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline167.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="84" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline167.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$(g',n',k')$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> that satisfy </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU4" id="eqnU4">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu4.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="587" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu4.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}(g', n') \prec (\gamma,\nu), \qquad 2d_{g',n'} - k' \leq 2d_{\gamma,\nu} - \ell \qquad \text{and} \qquad k' \leq \ell-2.\end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">Then <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline168.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="84" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline168.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$(g',n',k')$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> satisfies (<a class="xref disp-formula" href="#eqn2">2.2</a>), so <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline169.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="202" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline169.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$S^{\ell }({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{\gamma , \nu }) = H^\ell ({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{\gamma ,\nu })$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> by induction. This proves the claim.</p>
<p class="p"> Next, by induction, we have <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline170.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="237" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline170.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^k({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n-1}) = S^k({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n-1})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, so the image of </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU5" id="eqnU5">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu5.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="269" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu5.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}\pi_i^*\colon H^k({\overline{\mathcal{M}}}_{g,n-1}) \to H^k({\overline{\mathcal{M}}}_{g,n})\end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">is contained in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline171.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="86" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline171.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$S^k({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for all <em class="italic">i</em>. Hence, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline172.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="39" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline172.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Phi ^k_{g,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is contained in the image of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline173.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="11" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline173.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\phi $
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. The tautological classes <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline174.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="251" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline174.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$RH^k({\mathcal {M}}_{g,n}) \subseteq W_k H^k({\mathcal {M}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> are also contained in the image of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline175.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="11" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline175.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\phi $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> by definition. Thus, the surjectivity of </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU6" id="eqnU6">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu6.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="435" height="37" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu6.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}S^k({\overline{\mathcal{M}}}_{g,n}) \to W_kH^k({\mathcal{M}}_{g,n})/\left(\Phi^k_{g,n} + RH^k({\mathcal{M}}_{g,n})\right)\end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">implies that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline176.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="11" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline176.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\phi $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is surjective. Hence, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline177.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="13" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline177.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\beta $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is also surjective, as desired.</p>
</div>
<p class="p"> In order to apply Lemma <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma1">2.1</a>, we need results that help us understand generators for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline178.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="315" height="37" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline178.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_kH^k({\mathcal {M}}_{g,n})/\left (\Phi ^k_{g,n} + RH^k({\mathcal {M}}_{g,n})\right )$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. This is the topic of Sections <a class="xref sec" href="#sec7">3</a> and <a class="xref sec" href="#sec8">4</a>.</p>
</div>
<div class="sec" data-magellan-destination="sec4" id="sec4">

<h3 class="B"><span class="label">2.2</span> Pure cohomology in genus 1 and 2</h3>
<p class="p"> On <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline179.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline179.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{0,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, the only nonvanishing pure cohomology is <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline180.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="113" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline180.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_0 H^0({\mathcal {M}}_{0,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Below, we present the complete classification of pure cohomology in genus <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline181.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="7" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline181.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, which is due to Getzler [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r16"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Getzler</span>16</a>]. In genus <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline182.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="10" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline182.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, we present a classification in low cohomological degree, following Petersen [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r27"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Petersen</span>27</a>].</p> 
<div class="sec" data-magellan-destination="sec5" id="sec5">

<h4 class="C"><span class="label">2.2.1</span> Genus 1</h4>
<p class="p"> The following statement appeared in [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r23"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Pandharipande, Zvonkine and Petersen</span>23</a>, Proposition 7]; the proof there is omitted. Here, we include the proof (and corrected statement), which was explained to us by Petersen. Let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline183.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="35" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline183.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathsf {S}}_{k+1}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> denote the weight <em class="italic">k</em> structure associated to the space of cusp forms of weight <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline184.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="41" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline184.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$k+1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline185.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="59" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline185.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {SL}}_2(\mathbb {Z})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline186.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="118" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline186.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\pi \colon E \to {\mathcal {M}}_{1,1}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> be the universal curve, and let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline187.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="15" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline187.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {V}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> be the local system <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline188.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="58" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline188.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$R^1\pi _*\mathbb {Q}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. By the Eichler–Shimura correspondence, we have <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline189.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="238" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline189.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathsf {S}}_{k+1} = W_{k}H^1({\mathcal {M}}_{1,1}, \mathbb {V}^{\otimes {k-1}})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. We will see that the latter is identified with <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline190.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="117" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline190.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_k H^k({\mathcal {M}}_{1,k})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. More generally, we have the following. Given a partition <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline191.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="11" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline191.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\lambda $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> of <em class="italic">n</em>, let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline192.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="20" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline192.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$V_\lambda $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> be the associated Specht module representation of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline193.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="21" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline193.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {S}_n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p><div class="statement proposition" data-magellan-destination="proposition1" id="proposition1">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Proposition 2.2.</span> For <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline194.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="52" height="17" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline194.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n\geq k,$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> a basis for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline195.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="117" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline195.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_kH^k({\mathcal {M}}_{1,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is given by the <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline196.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="37" height="28" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline196.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\binom {n-1}{k-1}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> pullbacks from <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline197.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="119" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline197.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_kH^k({\mathcal {M}}_{1,A})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, where <em class="italic">A</em> runs over all subsets of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline198.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="83" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline198.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\{1,\ldots ,n\}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> of size <em class="italic">k</em>, such that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline199.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="45" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline199.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$1 \in A$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Consequently, there is an <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline200.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="21" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline200.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {S}_n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>-equivariant isomorphism </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU7" id="eqnU7">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu7.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="302" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu7.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}W_k H^k({\mathcal{M}}_{1,n})\cong {\mathsf{S}}_{k+1}\otimes V_{n-k+1,1^{k-1}}. \end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">For <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline201.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline201.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n&lt;k$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, we have <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline202.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="152" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline202.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_k H^k({\mathcal {M}}_{1,n})=0$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement other" data-magellan-destination="proof2" id="proof2">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Proof.</span> Let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline203.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="118" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline203.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\pi \colon E\rightarrow {\mathcal {M}}_{1,1}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> denote the universal elliptic curve, and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline204.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="123" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline204.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\sigma \colon {\mathcal {M}}_{1,1} \to E$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> the section. Associated to the open embedding <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline205.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="124" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline205.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{1,n}\hookrightarrow E^{n-1}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, we have a right exact sequence </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqn4" id="eqn4">
<span class="label">(2.4)</span>
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn4.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="530" height="32" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn4.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$ \begin{align} \bigoplus W_{k-2}H^{k-2}(E^{n-2})\rightarrow W_k H^k(E^{n-1})\rightarrow W_k H^k({\mathcal{M}}_{1,n})\rightarrow 0. \end{align} $$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">Since <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline206.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="146" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline206.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$f\colon E^{n-1}\rightarrow {\mathcal {M}}_{1,1}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is smooth and proper, the Leray spectral sequence degenerates at <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline207.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="21" height="17" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline207.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$E_2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, and by [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r12"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Deligne</span>12</a>, Proposition 2.16], we have a direct sum decomposition </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqn5" id="eqn5">
<span class="label">(2.5)</span>
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn5.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="323" height="49" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn5.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$ \begin{align} H^k(E^{n-1}) = \bigoplus_{p+q = k} H^p({\mathcal{M}}_{1,1}, R^qf_*\mathbb{Q}). \end{align} $$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">By the Künneth formula, we have </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU8" id="eqnU8">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu8.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="361" height="48" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu8.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}R^qf_*\mathbb{Q}= \bigoplus_{i_2 + \cdots + i_{n} = q}R^{i_2}\pi_*\mathbb{Q} \otimes \cdots \otimes R^{i_{n}}\pi_*\mathbb{Q}. \end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">Let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline208.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="102" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline208.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {V}:=R^1\pi _*\mathbb {Q}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, and note that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline209.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="97" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline209.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$R^0\pi _*\mathbb {Q} = \mathbb {Q}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline210.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="135" height="23" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline210.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$R^2\pi _*\mathbb {Q} = \mathbb {Q}(-1)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
<p class="p"> Fix some <em class="italic">p</em> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline211.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="89" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline211.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$(i_2, \ldots , i_{n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> with <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline212.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="165" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline212.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$p + i_2 + \cdots + i_{n} = k$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. If <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline213.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="48" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline213.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$i_j = 2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, then, we claim that </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqn6" id="eqn6">
<span class="label">(2.6)</span>
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn6.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="461" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn6.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$ \begin{align} W_kH^p({\mathcal{M}}_{1,1}, R^{i_2}\pi_*\mathbb{Q} \otimes \cdots \otimes R^{i_{n}}\pi_*\mathbb{Q}) \subset W_kH^k(E^{n-1}) \end{align} $$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">lies in the image of the first map in (<a class="xref disp-formula" href="#eqn4">2.4</a>). More precisely, let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline214.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="151" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline214.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\alpha _{j} \colon E^{n-2} \rightarrow E^{n-1}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> be the locus where the <em class="italic">j</em>th entry in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline215.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="39" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline215.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$E^{n-1}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> agrees with the section <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline216.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="123" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline216.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\sigma \colon {\mathcal {M}}_{1,1} \to E$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. In other words, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline217.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="20" height="17" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline217.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\alpha _j$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is defined by the fiber diagram </p><div class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU9" id="eqnU9">
<div class="figure-thumb"><img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu9.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image" width="159" height="97" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu9.png" data-zoomable="false"></div>
</div>
<p class="p"> If <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline218.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="52" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline218.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$i_j = 2,$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> we have <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline219.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="349" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline219.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$p + i_2 + \cdots + i_{j-1} + i_{j+1} + \cdots + i_{n} = k-2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Therefore, using the Leray spectral sequence for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline220.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="118" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline220.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$E^{n-2} \to {\mathcal {M}}_{1,1}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, there is a corresponding term </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqn7" id="eqn7">
<span class="label">(2.7)</span>
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn7.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="763" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn7.png" data-zoomable="true">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$ \begin{align} \begin{aligned} W_{k-2} H^p({\mathcal{M}}_{1,1}, R^{i_2}\pi_*\mathbb{Q} \otimes \cdots \otimes R^{i_{j-1}}\pi_*\mathbb{Q} \otimes R^{i_{j+1}}\pi_*\mathbb{Q} \otimes \cdots \otimes R^{i_{n}}\pi_*\mathbb{Q}) \subset W_{k-2} H^{k-2}(E^{n-2}). \end{aligned} \end{align} $$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">Then the pushforward <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline221.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="264" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline221.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\alpha _{j*}\colon H^{k-2}(E^{n-2}) \to H^k(E^{n-1})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> sends the subspace on the left of (<a class="xref disp-formula" href="#eqn7">2.7</a>) isomorphically onto the subspace on the left of (<a class="xref disp-formula" href="#eqn6">2.6</a>), which proves the claim.</p>
<p class="p"> It follows that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline222.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="117" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline222.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_kH^k({\mathcal {M}}_{1,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is generated by the terms <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline223.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="322" height="23" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline223.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_k H^p({\mathcal {M}}_{1,1}, R^{i_2} \pi _*\mathbb {Q} \otimes \cdots \otimes R^{i_{n}}\pi _*\mathbb {Q})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline224.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="111" height="23" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline224.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_k H^k(E^{n-1})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, where all <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline225.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="49" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline225.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$i_j \leq 1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. By [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r26"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Petersen</span>26</a>, Section 2], we have <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline226.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="198" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline226.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_k H^p({\mathcal {M}}_{1,1}, \mathbb {V}^{\otimes q}) = 0$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> unless <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline227.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="46" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline227.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$p = 1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline228.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="78" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline228.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$q = k-1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, in which case <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline229.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="238" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline229.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_k H^1({\mathcal {M}}_{1,1}, \mathbb {V}^{\otimes k-1}) = {\mathsf {S}}_{k+1}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> by Eichler–Shimura.</p>
<p class="p"> There are <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline230.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="37" height="28" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline230.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\binom {n-1}{k-1}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> terms of the form <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline231.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="149" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline231.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^1({\mathcal {M}}_{1,1}, \mathbb {V}^{\otimes k-1})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> in (<a class="xref disp-formula" href="#eqn5">2.5</a>) coming from choosing which <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline232.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="42" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline232.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$k-1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> of the <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline233.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="42" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline233.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n-1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> indices have <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline234.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline234.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$i_j =1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Each of these terms is pulled back along the projection map <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline235.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="114" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline235.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$E^{n-1} \to E^{k-1}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, which remembers the <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline236.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="42" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline236.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$k-1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> factors for which <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline237.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline237.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$i_j = 1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Let <em class="italic">A</em> be the collection of indices <em class="italic">j</em>, such that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline238.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline238.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$i_j = 1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> together with <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline239.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="7" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline239.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. There is a commutative diagram </p><div class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU10" id="eqnU10">
<div class="figure-thumb"><img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu10.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image" width="307" height="101" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu10.png" data-zoomable="false"></div>
</div><p class="p continuation">It follows that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline240.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="117" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline240.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_kH^k({\mathcal {M}}_{1,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is generated by the pullbacks from <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline241.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="119" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline241.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_kH^k({\mathcal {M}}_{1,A})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> as <em class="italic">A</em> ranges over all subsets of size <em class="italic">k</em> containing <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline242.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="7" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline242.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Finally, we note that there can be no relations among these <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline243.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="37" height="28" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline243.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\binom {n-1}{k-1}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> copies of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline244.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="238" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline244.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_k H^1({\mathcal {M}}_{1,1}, \mathbb {V}^{\otimes k-1}) = {\mathsf {S}}_{k+1}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> since the image of the left-hand map of (<a class="xref disp-formula" href="#eqn4">2.4</a>) lies in the subspace of type <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline245.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="76" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline245.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathsf {L}^i {\mathsf {S}}_{k+1-2i}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline246.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="40" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline246.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$i \geq 1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
<p class="p"> We have now shown that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline247.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="220" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline247.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_kH^k({\mathcal {M}}_{1,n}) = {\mathsf {S}}_{k+1} \otimes U$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for some <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline248.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="37" height="28" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline248.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\binom {n-1}{k-1}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>-dimensional vector space <em class="italic">U</em>. From the discussion above, it is not difficult to identify <em class="italic">U</em> as an <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline249.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="21" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline249.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {S}_n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>-representation. When <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline250.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="45" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline250.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n = k$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, the <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline251.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="20" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline251.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {S}_k$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> action on <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline252.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="117" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline252.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_kH^k({\mathcal {M}}_{1,k})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is the sign representation. To identify <em class="italic">U</em> for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline253.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline253.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n&gt; k$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline254.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="86" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline254.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {S}_{n-1} \subset \mathbb {S}_n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> be the subgroup that fixes <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline255.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="7" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline255.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Since <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline256.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="117" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline256.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_kH^k({\mathcal {M}}_{1,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is freely generated by the pullbacks from <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline257.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="119" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline257.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_kH^k({\mathcal {M}}_{1,A})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> as <em class="italic">A</em> runs over subsets of size <em class="italic">k</em> containing <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline258.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="7" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline258.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, we have </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU11" id="eqnU11">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu11.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="285" height="31" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu11.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}\mathrm{Res}^{\mathbb{S}_n}_{\mathbb{S}_{n-1}} U = \mathrm{Ind}_{\mathbb{S}_{k-1} \times \mathbb{S}_{n-k}}^{\mathbb{S}_{n-1}}(\mathrm{sgn}\boxtimes \mathbf{1}).\end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">By the Pieri rule, we have </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqn8" id="eqn8">
<span class="label">(2.8)</span>
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn8.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="641" height="31" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn8.png" data-zoomable="true">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$ \begin{align} \mathrm{Ind}_{\mathbb{S}_{k-1} \times \mathbb{S}_{n-k}}^{\mathbb{S}_{n-1}}(\mathrm{sgn}\boxtimes \mathbf{1}) = \mathrm{Ind}_{\mathbb{S}_{k-1} \times \mathbb{S}_{n-k}}^{\mathbb{S}_{n-1}}(V_{1^{k-1}} \boxtimes V_{n-k}) = V_{n-k+1,1^{k-2}} \oplus V_{n-k,1^{k-1}}.\end{align} $$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">By the branching rule, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline259.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="88" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline259.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$V_{n-k+1,1^{k-1}}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is the unique <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline260.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="21" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline260.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {S}_n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> representation whose restriction to <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline261.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="36" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline261.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {S}_{n-1}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is the representation in (<a class="xref disp-formula" href="#eqn8">2.8</a>).</p>
</div>
<p class="p"> Since <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline262.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="61" height="17" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline262.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathsf {S}}_{14} = 0$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, we have the following.</p><div class="statement corollary" data-magellan-destination="corollary2" id="corollary2">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Corollary 2.3.</span> 
<span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline263.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="96" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline263.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{13}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> lies in the STE generated by <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline264.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="101" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline264.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{11}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,11})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for all <em class="italic">n</em>.</p>
</div>
<p class="p"> Let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline265.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="24" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline265.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$S^*_\omega $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> denote the STE generated by <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline266.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="101" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline266.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{11}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,11})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Note that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline267.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="24" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline267.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$S^*_\omega $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is the STE generated by the class <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline268.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="152" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline268.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\omega \in H^{11,0}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,11})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> associated to the weight <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline269.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="18" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline269.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$12$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> cusp form for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline270.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="59" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline270.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {SL}}_2(\mathbb {Z})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>,that is, it is the smallest STE whose complexification contains <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline271.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="14" height="11" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline271.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\omega $
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. In [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r8"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Canning, Larson and Payne</span>8</a>], we showed that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline272.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="25" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline272.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$S^*_\omega $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> contains <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline273.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="98" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline273.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{11}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, and hence <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline274.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="96" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline274.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H_{11}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, for all <em class="italic">g</em> and <em class="italic">n</em>. In this paper, we show that it also contains <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline275.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="97" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline275.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H_{13}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for all <em class="italic">g</em> and <em class="italic">n</em> (Theorem <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem4">1.6</a>). In contrast with the system of tautological rings, an arbitrary STE need not be closed under pushforward along maps forgetting marked points or pullback to the boundary. Nevertheless, we have the following result for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline276.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="90" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline276.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$S_{\omega }^*({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p><div class="statement proposition" data-magellan-destination="proposition2" id="proposition2">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Proposition 2.4.</span> The STE <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline277.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="24" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline277.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$S_{\omega }^*$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is closed under the tautological operations induced by pushforward for forgetting marked points and pullback for gluing marked points.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement other" data-magellan-destination="proof3" id="proof3">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Proof.</span> By [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r26"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Petersen</span>26</a>], all even cohomology in genus <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline278.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="7" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline278.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is represented by boundary strata. Therefore, any product of two odd degree classes can be written as a sum of boundary strata. It follows that every class in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline279.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="90" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline279.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$S_{\omega }^*({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> can be represented as a linear combination of decorated graphs, all of whose nontautological decorations are <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline280.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="30" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline280.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{11}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>-classes on genus 1 vertices.</p>
<p class="p"> The pushforward of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline281.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="96" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline281.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{11}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> along the maps forgetting marked points is zero. Since the tautological rings are closed under pushforward, it follows that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline282.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="25" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline282.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$S_{\omega }^*$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is closed under pushforward.</p>
<p class="p"> By [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r8"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Canning, Larson and Payne</span>8</a>, Lemma 2.2], the image of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline283.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="96" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline283.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{11}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> under pullback to the boundary lies in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline284.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="25" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline284.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$S^*_{\omega }$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. By the excess intersection formula, and using the fact that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline285.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="13" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline285.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\psi $
</span></span>
</span>
</span>-classes in genus 1 are boundary classes, it follows that the pullback of any such decorated graph in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline286.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="25" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline286.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$S_\omega ^*$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> to any boundary stratum is a sum of decorated graphs of the same form. In particular, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline287.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="24" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline287.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$S_{\omega }^*$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is closed under pullback to the boundary, as required.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement remark" data-magellan-destination="remark1" id="remark1">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Remark 2.5.</span> More generally, the Hodge groups <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline288.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="102" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline288.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{k,0}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,k})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> correspond to the space of cusp forms for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline289.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="59" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline289.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {SL}}_2(\mathbb {Z})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> of weight <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline290.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="41" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline290.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$k+1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Essentially the same argument shows that the STE generated by any subset of these cusp form spaces is closed under all of the tautological operations.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="sec" data-magellan-destination="sec6" id="sec6">

<h4 class="C"><span class="label">2.2.2</span> Genus 2</h4>
<p class="p"> Here, we summarize what we need about the pure weight cohomology of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline291.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline291.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{2,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> in low degrees, from [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r28"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Petersen</span>28</a>, <a class="xref bibr" href="#r30"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Petersen and Tommasi</span>30</a>].</p><div class="statement proposition" data-magellan-destination="proposition3" id="proposition3">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Proposition 2.6.</span> Let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline292.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="57" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline292.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$k\leq 10$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Then <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline293.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="269" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline293.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_{2k} H^{2k}({\mathcal {M}}_{2,n})=RH^{2k}({\mathcal {M}}_{2,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement other" data-magellan-destination="proof4" id="proof4">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Proof.</span> When <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline294.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="57" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline294.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n&lt;20$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, we have <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline295.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="235" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline295.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{2k}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{2,n})=RH^{2k}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{2,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> by [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r28"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Petersen</span>28</a>, Theorem 3.8]. Hence, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline296.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="269" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline296.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_{2k} H^{2k}({\mathcal {M}}_{2,n})=RH^{2k}({\mathcal {M}}_{2,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> by restriction. For <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline297.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="55" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline297.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n=20$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline298.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="57" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline298.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$k\leq 10$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, the same result holds (see [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r28"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Petersen</span>28</a>, Remark 3.10]). For <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline299.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="57" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline299.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n&gt;20$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline300.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="57" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline300.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$k \leq 10$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, all of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline301.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="132" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline301.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_{2k} H^{2k}({\mathcal {M}}_{2,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is pulled back from <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline302.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="136" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline302.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_{2k} H^{2k}({\mathcal {M}}_{2,m})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> where <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline303.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="62" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline303.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$m\leq 20$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> (see Lemma <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma2">3.1</a>, below). Because the tautological ring is closed under forgetful pullbacks, the lemma follows.</p>
</div>
<p class="p"> Applying Lemma <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma1">2.1</a> to the STE <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline304.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="38" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline304.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$RH^*$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> immediately implies Conjecture <a class="xref statement" href="#conjecture1">1.8</a> for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline305.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="45" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline305.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g = 2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p><div class="statement corollary" data-magellan-destination="corollary3" id="corollary3">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Corollary 2.7.</span> If <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline306.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="57" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline306.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$k \leq 10$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, then <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline307.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="235" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline307.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{2k}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{2,n}) = RH^{2k}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{2,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for all <em class="italic">n</em>.</p>
</div>
<p class="p"> In odd degrees, there are restrictions on the possible motivic structures coming from the cohomology of local systems on the moduli space of principally polarized abelian surfaces.</p><div class="statement proposition" data-magellan-destination="proposition4" id="proposition4">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Proposition 2.8.</span> In the category of Galois representations, the pure weight cohomology of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline308.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline308.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{2,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> in degrees 13 and 15 is of the form </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU12" id="eqnU12">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu12.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="567" height="32" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu12.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}W_{13}H^{13}({\mathcal{M}}_{2,n})^{\mathrm{ss}} \cong \bigoplus \mathsf{L}{\mathsf{S}}_{12} \ \ \mbox{and} \ \ W_{15}H^{15}({\mathcal{M}}_{2,n})^{\mathrm{ss}} \cong \bigoplus {\mathsf{L}}^2{\mathsf{S}}_{12}. \end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div>
</div>
<div class="statement other" data-magellan-destination="proof5" id="proof5">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Proof.</span> For every <em class="italic">k</em>, the surjection </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU13" id="eqnU13">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu13.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="242" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu13.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}H^k({\overline{\mathcal{M}}}_{2,n})\rightarrow W_{k} H^k({\mathcal{M}}_{2,n}) \end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">factors through <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline309.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="117" height="29" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline309.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_k H^k({\mathcal {M}}_{2,n}^{\operatorname {\mathrm {ct}}})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Here, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline310.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline310.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{2,n}^{\operatorname {\mathrm {ct}}}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is the moduli space of genus <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline311.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="10" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline311.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> curves of compact type with <em class="italic">n</em> markings. By [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r28"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Petersen</span>28</a>, Theorem 2.1(i) and (ii)], </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU14" id="eqnU14">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu14.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="487" height="49" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu14.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}H^k({\mathcal{M}}_{2,n}^{\operatorname{\mathrm{ct}}})\cong \bigoplus_{p+q=k} H^p({\mathcal{M}}_{2}^{\operatorname{\mathrm{ct}}},A^q)\oplus H^p(\operatorname{\mathrm{Sym}}^2 {\mathcal{M}}_{1,1}, B^q), \end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">where <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline312.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="23" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline312.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$A^q$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline313.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="23" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline313.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$B^q$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> are local systems of weight <em class="italic">q</em>, given by direct sums of Tate twists of symplectic local systems. Moreover, the terms <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline314.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="174" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline314.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^p(\operatorname {\mathrm {Sym}}^2 {\mathcal {M}}_{1,1},B^q)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> map to zero under restriction to <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline315.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="90" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline315.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^k({\mathcal {M}}_{2,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> by [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r28"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Petersen</span>28</a>, Lemma 3.3].</p>
<p class="p"> We now consider the terms <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline316.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="115" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline316.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^p({\mathcal {M}}_{2}^{\operatorname {\mathrm {ct}}},A^q)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline317.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="15" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline317.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {V}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> be a Tate twist of a symplectic local system of weight <em class="italic">q</em> on <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline318.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="37" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline318.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_2^{\operatorname {\mathrm {ct}}}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. If <em class="italic">q</em> is odd, then <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline319.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="104" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline319.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^p({\mathcal {M}}_{2}^{\operatorname {\mathrm {ct}}},\mathbb {V})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> vanishes because the hyperelliptic involution acts on the fibers of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline320.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="15" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline320.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {V}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> by <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline321.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="48" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline321.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$(-1)^q$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. When <em class="italic">q</em> is even, the possible Galois representations appearing in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline322.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="119" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline322.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^p({\mathcal {M}}_{2}^{\operatorname {\mathrm {ct}}},\mathbb {V})^{\mathrm {ss}}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> are determined by [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r27"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Petersen</span>27</a>, Theorem 2.1]. When <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline323.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="88" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline323.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$p+q=13$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> (respectively, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline324.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="97" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline324.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$p+q=15)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, the only possibility of pure weight is <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline325.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="37" height="17" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline325.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathsf {L}{\mathsf {S}}_{12}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> (respectively, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline326.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="53" height="23" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline326.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathsf {L}}^2{\mathsf {S}}_{12})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement corollary" data-magellan-destination="corollary4" id="corollary4">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Corollary 2.9.</span> On <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline327.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline327.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{2,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, in the category of Galois representations, we have </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU15" id="eqnU15">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu15.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="502" height="32" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu15.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}H^{13}({\overline{\mathcal{M}}}_{2,n})^{\mathrm{ss}} \cong \bigoplus \mathsf{L}{\mathsf{S}}_{12} \ \ \mbox{and} \ \ H^{15}({\overline{\mathcal{M}}}_{2,n})^{\mathrm{ss}} \cong \bigoplus {\mathsf{L}}^2 {\mathsf{S}}_{12}. \end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div>
</div>
<div class="statement other" data-magellan-destination="proof6" id="proof6">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Proof.</span> For degree 13, consider the right exact sequence </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU16" id="eqnU16">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu16.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="451" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu16.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}H^{11}(\widetilde{\partial {\mathcal{M}}_{2,n}}) \rightarrow H^{13}({\overline{\mathcal{M}}}_{2,n})\rightarrow W_{13}H^{13}({\mathcal{M}}_{2,n})\rightarrow 0. \end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">By [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r8"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Canning, Larson and Payne</span>8</a>], the semi-simplification of the left-hand side is a sum of terms <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline328.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="27" height="17" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline328.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathsf {S}}_{12}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Proposition <a class="xref statement" href="#proposition4">2.8</a> shows that the semi-simplification of the right-hand side consists only of Tate twists of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline329.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="27" height="17" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline329.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathsf {S}}_{12}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Thus, the semi-simplification of the middle term does, too.</p>
<p class="p"> Similarly, for degree <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline330.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="17" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline330.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$15$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, we consider the right exact sequence </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU17" id="eqnU17">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu17.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="451" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu17.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}H^{13}(\widetilde{\partial {\mathcal{M}}_{2,n}}) \rightarrow H^{15}({\overline{\mathcal{M}}}_{2,n})\rightarrow W_{15}H^{15}({\mathcal{M}}_{2,n})\rightarrow 0. \end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">The boundary divisors on <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline331.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="48" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline331.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{2,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> are finite quotients of products of moduli spaces for genus at most <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline332.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="10" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline332.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. In particular, by the Künneth formula and vanishing of odd cohomology in degrees less than or equal to <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline333.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="10" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline333.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$9$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, we see that the left-hand side is a sum of terms of the form <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline334.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="106" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline334.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{13}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g',n'})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> or <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline335.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="238" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline335.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^2({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g_1,n_1}) \otimes H^{11}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g_2,n_2})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, where <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline336.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="110" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline336.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g', g_1, g_2 \leq 2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. By the degree 13 result just proved, the semi-simplification of terms of the first kind is a sum of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline337.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="37" height="17" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline337.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathsf {L}{\mathsf {S}}_{12}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Meanwhile, we know <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline338.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="102" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline338.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^2({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g_1,n_1})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is pure Tate by [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r1"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Arbarello and Cornalba</span>1</a>] and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline339.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="124" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline339.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{11}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g_2, n_2})^{\mathrm {ss}}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is a sum of terms <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline340.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="27" height="17" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline340.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathsf {S}}_{12}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> by [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r8"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Canning, Larson and Payne</span>8</a>]. Hence, the semi-simplification of terms of the second kind is also a sum of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline341.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="37" height="17" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline341.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathsf {L}{\mathsf {S}}_{12}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. To conclude, note that Proposition <a class="xref statement" href="#proposition4">2.8</a> shows that the semi-simplification of the right-hand side consists only of Tate twists of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline342.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="27" height="17" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline342.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathsf {S}}_{12}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, so the semi-simplification of the middle term does too.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement remark" data-magellan-destination="remark2" id="remark2">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Remark 2.10.</span> See Lemma <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma25">8.1</a> for an analogous result in the category of Hodge structures.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="sec" data-magellan-destination="sec7" id="sec7">

<h2 class="A"><span class="label">3</span> Finite generation</h2>
<p class="p"> Let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline343.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="18" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline343.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$S^*$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> be an STE. By Lemma <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma1">2.1</a>, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline344.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="86" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline344.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$S^k({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> contains <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline345.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="92" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline345.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^k({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for all <em class="italic">g</em> and <em class="italic">n</em> if and only if it surjects onto <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline346.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="312" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline346.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_kH^k({\mathcal {M}}_{g,n})/ \big (\Phi ^k_{g,n} + RH^k({\mathcal {M}}_{g,n}) \big )$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for all <em class="italic">g</em> and <em class="italic">n</em>. Below we give a sufficient criterion for the vanishing of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline347.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="174" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline347.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_kH^k({\mathcal {M}}_{g,n})/ \Phi ^k_{g,n}.$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> The argument is similar to the proof of Proposition <a class="xref statement" href="#proposition1">2.2</a>, using the Künneth decomposition of the Leray spectral sequence for the <em class="italic">n</em>-fold fiber product of the universal curve <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline348.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="88" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline348.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {C}^n \to {\mathcal {M}}_g$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
<p class="p"> We are grateful to Petersen for explaining how an earlier version of this lemma could be strengthened to the version presented here. This stronger version will also be useful for controlling some additional base cases in Section <a class="xref sec" href="#sec19">7</a>. To state it, we define the subspace </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU18" id="eqnU18">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu18.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="417" height="29" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu18.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}\Psi_{g,n}^k := \psi_1\Phi^{k-2}_{g,n} + \cdots + \psi_n \Phi^{k-2}_{g,n} \subset W_k H^k({\mathcal{M}}_{g,n}).\end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">In other words, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline349.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="39" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline349.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Psi ^k_{g,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is generated by pullbacks from moduli spaces with fewer markings multiplied with <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline350.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="13" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline350.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\psi $
</span></span>
</span>
</span>-classes. Given a <em class="italic">g</em>-tuple of integers <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline351.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="249" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline351.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\lambda = (\lambda _1 \geq \lambda _2 \geq \cdots \geq \lambda _g \geq 0)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline352.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="24" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline352.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {V}_\lambda $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> be the associated symplectic local system on <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline353.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="33" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline353.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_g$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, as in [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r29"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Petersen, Tavakol and Yin</span>29</a>]. Let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline354.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="150" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline354.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$|\lambda | = \lambda _1 + \cdots + \lambda _g$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, which is the weight of the local system <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline355.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="24" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline355.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {V}_\lambda $
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. When <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline356.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="55" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline356.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$|\lambda | = n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, as in the previous section, we write <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline357.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="20" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline357.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$V_{\lambda }$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for the irreducible <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline358.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="21" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline358.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {S}_n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> representation corresponding to <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline359.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="11" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline359.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\lambda $
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p><div class="statement lemma" data-magellan-destination="lemma2" id="lemma2">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Lemma 3.1.</span> 
<span class="roman">(a)</span> If <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline360.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline360.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g \geq 2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, then </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU19" id="eqnU19">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu19.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="532" height="49" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu19.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}W_kH^k({\mathcal{M}}_{g,n})/(\Phi_{g,n}^k + \Psi_{g,n}^k) \cong \bigoplus_{|\lambda| = n} W_k H^{k - n} ({\mathcal{M}}_g, \mathbb{V}_{\lambda}) \otimes V_{\lambda^T}.\end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">
<span class="roman">(b)</span> Moreover, if <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline361.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="46" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline361.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n&gt; 0$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline362.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="48" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline362.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n \geq k$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, then <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline363.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="183" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline363.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_kH^k({\mathcal {M}}_{g,n}) = \Phi ^k_{g,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement other" data-magellan-destination="proof7" id="proof7">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Proof.</span> (a) Let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline364.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="104" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline364.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\pi \colon \mathcal {C} \to {\mathcal {M}}_g$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> be the universal curve. There is an open inclusion <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline365.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="97" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline365.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{g,n} \subset \mathcal {C}^n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, and hence restriction gives a surjection from <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline366.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="91" height="23" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline366.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_kH^k(\mathcal {C}^n)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> to <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline367.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="118" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline367.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_kH^k({\mathcal {M}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Given a subset <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline368.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="124" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline368.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$A \subset \{1, \ldots , n\}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline369.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="78" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline369.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {C}^n \to \mathcal {C}^A$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> be the projection onto the factors indexed by <em class="italic">A</em>. We consider the following three subspaces of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline370.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="64" height="23" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline370.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^k(\mathcal {C}^n)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>:</p>
<p class="p"> 
</p><ul class="list nomark">
<li class="list-item">

<p class="p"><span class="label">•</span> 
<span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline371.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="15" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline371.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\widetilde {\Phi }$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, the span of the pullbacks of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline372.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="85" height="23" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline372.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^k(\mathcal {C}^{\{i\}^c})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> along projection <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline373.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="96" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline373.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {C}^n \to \mathcal {C}^{\{i\}^c}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span></p>
</li>
<li class="list-item">

<p class="p"><span class="label">•</span> 
<span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline374.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="15" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline374.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\widetilde {\Psi }$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, the span of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline375.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="136" height="23" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline375.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\psi _i \cdot H^{k-2}(\mathcal {C}^{\{i\}^c})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span></p>
</li>
<li class="list-item">

<p class="p"><span class="label">•</span> 
<span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline376.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="14" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline376.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\widetilde {\Delta }$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, the span of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline377.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="159" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline377.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Delta _{ij} \cdot H^{k-2}(\mathcal {C}^{\{i, j\}^c})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, where <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline378.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="27" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline378.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Delta _{ij}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> denotes the pullback of the class of the diagonal in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline379.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="89" height="23" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline379.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^2(\mathcal {C}^{\{i,j\}})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
</li>
</ul><p class="p continuation">Note that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline380.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="14" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline380.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\widetilde {\Delta }$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> lies in the kernel of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline381.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="191" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline381.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^k(\mathcal {C}^n) \to H^k({\mathcal {M}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, and the images of the weight <em class="italic">k</em> parts of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline382.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="15" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline382.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\widetilde {\Phi }$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline383.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="15" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline383.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\widetilde {\Psi }$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> under <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline384.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="244" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline384.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_kH^k(\mathcal {C}^n) \to W_kH^k({\mathcal {M}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> are the subspaces <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline385.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="39" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline385.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Phi ^k_{g,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline386.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="39" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline386.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Psi ^k_{g,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, respectively. To prove part (a), it thus suffices to show that </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqn9" id="eqn9">
<span class="label">(3.1)</span>
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn9.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="439" height="49" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn9.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$ \begin{align} H^k(\mathcal{C}^n)/(\widetilde{\Phi} + \widetilde{\Psi} + \widetilde{\Delta}) \cong \bigoplus_{|\lambda|=n} H^{k-n}({\mathcal{M}}_g, \mathbb{V}_{\lambda}) \otimes V_{\lambda^T}. \end{align} $$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">We explain how (<a class="xref disp-formula" href="#eqn9">3.1</a>) follows from [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r29"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Petersen, Tavakol and Yin</span>29</a>].</p>
<p class="p"> Since <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline387.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="115" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline387.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$f\colon \mathcal {C}^n \to {\mathcal {M}}_g$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is smooth and proper, the Leray spectral sequence degenerates at <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline388.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="21" height="17" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline388.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$E_2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, and by [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r12"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Deligne</span>12</a>, Proposition 2.16], we have a direct sum decomposition </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU20" id="eqnU20">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu20.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="292" height="49" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu20.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}H^k(\mathcal{C}^n) = \bigoplus_{p+q = k}H^p({\mathcal{M}}_g, R^q f_*\mathbb{Q}). \end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">Applying the Künneth formula, we obtain </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqn10" id="eqn10">
<span class="label">(3.2)</span>
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn10.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="465" height="64" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn10.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$ \begin{align} H^k(\mathcal{C}^n) = \bigoplus_{\substack{p + q = k \\i_1 + \ldots+ i_n = q }} H^p\left({\mathcal{M}}_g, R^{i_1} \pi_* \mathbb{Q} \otimes \cdots \otimes R^{i_n} \pi_* \mathbb{Q} \right). \end{align} $$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">As observed in [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r29"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Petersen, Tavakol and Yin</span>29</a>, Section 5.2.2], the subspace <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline389.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="15" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline389.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\widetilde {\Phi }$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> corresponds to the span of the summands where some <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline390.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline390.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$i_s = 0$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Meanwhile, modulo <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline391.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="15" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline391.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\widetilde {\Phi }$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, the subspace <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline392.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="15" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline392.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\widetilde {\Psi }$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> corresponds to the span of summands where some <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline393.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline393.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$i_s = 2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. This follows from the formulas for the projector <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline394.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="20" height="13" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline394.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\pi _2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> (which projects onto such summands) in [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r29"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Petersen, Tavakol and Yin</span>29</a>, Section 5.1]. Quotienting by <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline395.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="52" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline395.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\widetilde {\Phi } + \widetilde {\Psi }$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> thus leaves the term with <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline396.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="135" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline396.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$i_1 = \ldots = i_n = 1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. The local system <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline397.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="93" height="23" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline397.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$(R^1\pi _*\mathbb {Q})^{\otimes n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> corresponds to the <em class="italic">n</em>th tensor power of the standard representation of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline398.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="37" height="23" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline398.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathrm {Sp}_{2g}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. It thus decomposes into a direct sum of irreducible local systems, as in [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r29"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Petersen, Tavakol and Yin</span>29</a>, Section 3.2]. As explained there, we have a natural projection </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqn11" id="eqn11">
<span class="label">(3.3)</span>
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn11.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="251" height="49" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn11.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$ \begin{align} (R^1\pi_*\mathbb{Q})^{\otimes n} \to \bigoplus_{|\lambda| = n} \mathbb{V}_{\lambda} \otimes V_{\lambda^T,} \end{align} $$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">whose kernel is spanned by the image of the <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline399.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="20" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline399.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\binom {n}{2}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> insertion maps </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU21" id="eqnU21">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu21.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="240" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu21.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}(R^1 \pi_* \mathbb{Q})^{\otimes n -2} \to (R^1 \pi_* \mathbb{Q})^{\otimes n}\end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">given by inserting the class of the symplectic form. Modulo other Künneth components, the class of the diagonal <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline400.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="33" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline400.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Delta _{i,j}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is the class of the symplectic form in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline401.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="246" height="23" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline401.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{1}(\mathcal {C}) \otimes H^1(\mathcal {C}) \subset H^2(\mathcal {C}^{\{i,j\}})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Summarizing, we have found </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU22" id="eqnU22">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu22.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="595" height="49" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu22.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}H^k(\mathcal{C}^n)/(\widetilde{\Phi} + \widetilde{\Psi}) \cong H^{k-n}({\mathcal{M}}_g, (R^1\pi_*\mathbb{Q})^{\otimes n}) \to \bigoplus_{|\lambda| =n } H^{k-n}(\mathbb{V}_{\lambda}) \otimes V_{\lambda^T}, \end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">and the kernel is spanned by <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline402.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="14" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline402.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\widetilde {\Delta }$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. This establishes (<a class="xref disp-formula" href="#eqn9">3.1</a>)</p>
<p class="p"> (b) Now assume <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline403.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="48" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline403.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n \geq k$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. If some <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline404.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline404.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$i_s = 2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline405.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="130" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline405.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$i_1 + \cdots + i_n = k$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, we must have some other <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline406.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="52" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline406.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$i_{s'} = 0$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. It follows that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline407.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="57" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline407.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\widetilde {\Psi } \subset \widetilde {\Phi }$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, and hence <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline408.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="105" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline408.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Psi ^k_{g,n} \subset \Phi ^k_{g,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Thus, it suffices to see that the right-hand side of (a) vanishes when <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline409.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="48" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline409.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n \geq k$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline410.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="46" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline410.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n&gt; 0$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. This is immediate when <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline411.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline411.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n&gt; k$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Meanwhile, for the case <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline412.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="45" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline412.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n =k$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, we have <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline413.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="146" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline413.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^0({\mathcal {M}}_g, \mathbb {V}_{\lambda }) = 0$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> since <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline414.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="24" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline414.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {V}_{\lambda }$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is nontrivial.</p>
</div>
<p class="p"> We note a neat consequence of Lemma <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma2">3.1</a>(a) in genus <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline415.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="10" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline415.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, which was also pointed out to us by Petersen.</p>
<p class="p"> 
</p><div class="statement lemma" data-magellan-destination="lemma3" id="lemma3">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Lemma 3.2.</span> Suppose <em class="italic">n</em> is odd. The STE generated by <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline416.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="242" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline416.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^k({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{2,n-1}), H^{k-2}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{2,n-1})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline417.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="111" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline417.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{k-2}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,m})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline418.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="84" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline418.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$m \leq n+2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> contains <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline419.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="90" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline419.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^k({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{2,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement other" data-magellan-destination="proof8" id="proof8">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Proof.</span> The STE generated by <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline420.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="242" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline420.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^k({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{2,n-1}), H^{k-2}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{2,n-1})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline421.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="111" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline421.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{k-2}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,m})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline422.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="84" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline422.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$m \leq n+2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> contains all classes in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline423.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="90" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline423.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{k}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{2,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> that are pushed forward from the boundary, pulled back from less marked points or products of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline424.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="13" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline424.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\psi $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> classes with classes pulled back from less marked points. It, therefore, suffices to show that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline425.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="276" height="29" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline425.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_kH^k({\mathcal {M}}_{2,n})/(\Phi ^k_{2,n} + \Psi ^k_{2,n}) = 0$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. By Lemma <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma2">3.1</a>(a), this quotient is a sum of the pure cohomology of local systems of weight <em class="italic">n</em>. But on <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline426.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="33" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline426.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, the hyperelliptic involution acts on local systems of weight <em class="italic">n</em> by <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline427.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="48" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline427.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$(-1)^n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, so local systems of odd weight have no cohomology.</p>
</div>
<p class="p"> 
</p><div class="statement other" data-magellan-destination="sta1" id="sta1">
<h2 class="B">Proof of Theorem <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem2">1.3</a>.</h2>
<p class="p"> Let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline428.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="19" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline428.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$S^*$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> be the STE generated by the cohomology groups listed in the statement of the theorem. By Lemma <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma1">2.1</a>, it suffices to check that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline429.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="93" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline429.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$S^*({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g',n'})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> surjects onto <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline430.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="355" height="37" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline430.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_{k'}H^{k'}({\mathcal {M}}_{g',n'})/\left (\Phi ^{k'}_{g',n'} + RH^{k'}({\mathcal {M}}_{g',n'})\right )$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for all <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline431.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="83" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline431.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$(g', n', k')$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> with <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline432.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="87" height="17" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline432.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$k' \leq k-2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. By Lemma <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma2">3.1</a>(b), the target vanishes when <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline433.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="60" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline433.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n'&gt; k'$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. By the vcd of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline434.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="56" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline434.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{g',n'}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, it also vanishes when <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline435.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="141" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline435.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$k'&gt; 4g' - 4 + n'$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Finally, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline436.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="104" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline436.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{k'}({\mathcal {M}}_{g',n'})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is tautological for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline437.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="84" height="29" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline437.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$k' \leq \frac {2g'-2}{3}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r35"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Wahl</span>35</a>].</p>
</div>
<div class="statement remark" data-magellan-destination="remark3" id="remark3">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Remark 3.3.</span> One can prove analogues of Theorem <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem2">1.3</a> and Lemma <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma1">2.1</a> for homology. In particular, for each <em class="italic">k</em>, there is a finitely generated STE that contains <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline438.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="90" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline438.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H_k({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for all <em class="italic">g</em> and <em class="italic">n</em>, with explicit bounds on the generators.</p><section><div class="fig-ada" data-magellan-destination="fig1" id="fig1"><div class="caption"><span class="label">Figure 1</span>
<p class="p">The argument in the proof of Theorem <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem2">1.3</a> shows that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline439.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="330" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline439.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_{17}H^{17}({\mathcal {M}}_{g,n})/(\Phi ^{17}_{g,n} + RH^{17}({\mathcal {M}}_{g,n}))$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> vanishes for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline440.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="44" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline440.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$(g,n)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> outside the gray shaded region. Note that this quotient does <em class="italic">not</em> vanish for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline441.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="43" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline441.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$(g,n)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> equal to <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline442.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="53" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline442.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$(1,17)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline443.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="53" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline443.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$(2,14)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, which are pictured by purple dots.</p>
</div>


<div class="figure-thumb"><img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_fig1.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image" width="908" height="690" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_fig1.png" data-zoomable="true"></div>
</div></section>
</div>
</div>
<div class="sec" data-magellan-destination="sec8" id="sec8">

<h2 class="A"><span class="label">4</span> The Chow–Künneth generation Property</h2>
<p class="p"> In this section, we prove a key lemma about the cycle class map for spaces that have the following property.</p><div class="statement definition" data-magellan-destination="definition2" id="definition2">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Definition 4.1.</span> Let <em class="italic">X</em> be a smooth algebraic stack of finite type over a field, stratified by quotient stacks. We say that <em class="italic">X</em> has the CKgP if for all algebraic stacks <em class="italic">Y</em> (of finite type, stratified by quotient stacks), the exterior product </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU23" id="eqnU23">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu23.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="251" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu23.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}A_*(X)\otimes A_*(Y)\rightarrow A_*(X\times Y) \end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">is surjective.</p>
</div>
<p class="p"> For convenience, we record here several properties of the CKgP, all of which are proven in [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r5"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Canning and Larson</span>5</a>, Section 3.1].</p><div class="statement proposition" data-magellan-destination="proposition5" id="proposition5">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Proposition 4.2.</span> Let <em class="italic">X</em> be a smooth algebraic stack of finite type over a field, stratified by quotient stacks. </p><ol class="list number nomark">
<li class="list-item">

<p class="p"><span class="label">1.</span> if <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline444.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="56" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline444.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$U\subset X$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is open and <em class="italic">X</em> has the CKgP, then <em class="italic">U</em> has the CKgP;</p>
</li>
<li class="list-item">

<p class="p"><span class="label">2.</span> if <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline445.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="61" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline445.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$Y\rightarrow X$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is proper, surjective, representable by DM stacks, and <em class="italic">Y</em> has the CKgP, then <em class="italic">X</em> has the CKgP;</p>
</li>
<li class="list-item">

<p class="p"><span class="label">3.</span> if <em class="italic">X</em> admits a finite stratification <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline446.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="105" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline446.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$X=\coprod _{S\in \mathcal {S}} S$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, such that each <em class="italic">S</em> has the CKgP, then <em class="italic">X</em> has the CKgP;</p>
</li>
<li class="list-item">

<p class="p"><span class="label">4.</span> if <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline447.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="62" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline447.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$V\rightarrow X$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is an affine bundle, then <em class="italic">V</em> has the CKgP if and only if <em class="italic">X</em> has the CKgP;</p>
</li>
<li class="list-item">

<p class="p"><span class="label">5.</span> if <em class="italic">X</em> has the CKgP, and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline448.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="63" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline448.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$G\rightarrow X$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is a Grassmann bundle, then <em class="italic">G</em> has the CKgP;</p>
</li>
<li class="list-item">

<p class="p"><span class="label">6.</span> if <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline449.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="147" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline449.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$X = \operatorname {\mathrm {BGL}}_n, \operatorname {\mathrm {BSL}}_n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> or <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline450.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="62" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline450.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {BPGL}}_n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, then <em class="italic">X</em> has the CKgP.</p>
</li>
</ol>
</div>
<p class="p"> If <em class="italic">X</em> is smooth and proper and has the CKgP, then the cycle class map for <em class="italic">X</em> is an isomorphism [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r5"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Canning and Larson</span>5</a>, Lemma 3.11].</p>
<p class="p"> When <em class="italic">X</em> is smooth but not necessarily proper and has the CKgP, the cycle class map is not necessarily an isomorphism. Nevertheless, we have the following useful substitute (cf. [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r20"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Laterveer</span>20</a>, <a class="xref bibr" href="#r33"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Totaro</span>33</a>] for slightly different statements with similar proofs).</p><div class="statement lemma" data-magellan-destination="lemma4" id="lemma4">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Lemma 4.3.</span> Let <em class="italic">X</em> be an open substack of a smooth proper Deligne–Mumford stack <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline451.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="16" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline451.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\overline {X}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> over the complex numbers. If <em class="italic">X</em> has the CKgP, then the cycle class map </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU24" id="eqnU24">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu24.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="281" height="47" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu24.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}\operatorname{\mathrm{cl}}\colon\bigoplus_i A_i(X)\rightarrow \bigoplus_k W_k H^k(X) \end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">is surjective. In particular, if <em class="italic">k</em> is odd, then <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline452.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="120" height="23" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline452.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_kH^k(X)=0$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, and if <em class="italic">k</em> is even, then <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline453.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="84" height="23" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline453.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_k H^k(X)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is pure Hodge–Tate.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement other" data-magellan-destination="proof9" id="proof9">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Proof.</span> Set <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline454.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="92" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline454.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$d:=\dim \overline {X}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline455.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="96" height="23" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline455.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$D:=\overline {X}\smallsetminus X$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline456.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="95" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline456.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Delta \subset \overline {X}\times \overline {X}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> denote the diagonal. Because <em class="italic">X</em> has the CKgP, the exterior product map </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU25" id="eqnU25">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu25.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="318" height="62" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu25.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}\bigoplus_{\ell=0}^{d} A^\ell(\overline{X})\otimes A^{d-\ell}(X)\rightarrow A^d(\overline{X}\times X) \end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">is surjective. We have the excision exact sequence </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU26" id="eqnU26">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu26.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="400" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu26.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}A^d(\overline{X}\times D)\rightarrow A^d(\overline{X}\times \overline{X})\rightarrow A^d(\overline{X}\times X)\rightarrow 0. \end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">It follows that we can write the class of the diagonal in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline457.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="92" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline457.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$A^d(\overline {X} \times \overline {X})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> as </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqn12" id="eqn12">
<span class="label">(4.1)</span>
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn12.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="237" height="23" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn12.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$ \begin{align} \Delta = \Gamma + \Delta^0 + \Delta^1 +\cdots + \Delta^d, \end{align} $$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">where <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline458.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="12" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline458.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Gamma $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is supported on <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline459.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="54" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline459.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\overline {X}\times D$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and each <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline460.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="23" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline460.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Delta ^\ell $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is a linear combination of cycles of the form <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline461.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="91" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline461.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$V_i^\ell \times W_i^{d-\ell }$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, where <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline462.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="22" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline462.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$V_i^{\ell }$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline463.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="46" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline463.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_i^{d-\ell }$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> are subvarieties of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline464.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="17" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline464.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\overline {X}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> of codimension <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline465.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="9" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline465.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\ell $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline466.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="43" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline466.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$d-\ell $
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, respectively.</p>
<p class="p"> Let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline467.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="19" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline467.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$p_1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline468.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="22" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline468.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$p_2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> be the projections of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline469.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="54" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline469.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\overline {X} \times \overline {X}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> to the first and second factors, respectively. Given a class <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline470.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="133" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline470.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Psi \in H^*(\overline {X} \times \overline {X})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, we write <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline471.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="183" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline471.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Psi _*\colon H^*(\overline {X}) \to H^*(\overline {X})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for the associated correspondence, defined by <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline472.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="169" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline472.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Psi _*\alpha = p_{2*}(p_1^*\alpha \cdot \Psi )$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
<p class="p"> Let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline473.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="119" height="23" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline473.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$a\in W_k H^k(X)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline474.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="12" height="11" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline474.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\alpha $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> be a lift of <em class="italic">a</em> in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline475.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="167" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline475.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_k H^k(\overline {X})=H^k(\overline {X})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Then </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU27" id="eqnU27">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu27.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="331" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu27.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}\alpha = \Delta_*\alpha = (\Gamma_* + \Delta^0_* + \Delta^1_* +\cdots + \Delta^d_*)\alpha. \end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">First, we study <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline476.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="183" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline476.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Delta ^\ell _*\alpha = p_{2*}(p_1^*\alpha \cdot \Delta ^{\ell }).$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> Note that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline477.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="73" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline477.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$p_1^*\alpha \cdot \Delta ^{\ell }$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> vanishes for dimension reasons if <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline478.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="99" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline478.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$k+2\ell&gt;2d$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Furthermore, since <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline479.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="22" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline479.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$p_2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is of relative dimension <em class="italic">d</em>, the pushforward by <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline480.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="21" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline480.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$p_2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> of any cycle will vanish if <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline481.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="99" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline481.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$k+2\ell &lt;2d$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Thus, the only nonzero terms occur when <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline482.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="99" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline482.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$k=2d-2\ell $
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Moreover, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline483.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="36" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline483.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Delta ^{\ell }_*\alpha $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is a linear combination of the form <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline484.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="82" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline484.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\sum c_i W_i^{d-\ell }$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, so it lies in the image of the cycle class map.</p>
<p class="p"> Next, we study <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline485.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="32" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline485.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Gamma _*\alpha $
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. It suffices to treat the case that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline486.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="12" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline486.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Gamma $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is the class of a subvariety of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline487.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="55" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline487.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\overline {X}\times \overline {X}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> contained in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline488.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="54" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline488.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\overline {X}\times D$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, as it is a linear combination of such subvarieties. In this case, the map <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline489.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="115" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline489.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$p_2|_{\Gamma }\colon \Gamma \rightarrow \overline {X}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> factors through <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline490.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="66" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline490.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$D\rightarrow \overline {X}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Thus, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline491.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="32" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline491.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Gamma _*\alpha $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> maps to zero under the restriction to <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline492.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="84" height="23" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline492.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_k H^k(X)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> because the correspondence map factors through the cohomology of the boundary <em class="italic">D</em>. Thus, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline493.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="66" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline493.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\alpha |_{X}=a$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is in the image of the cycle class map.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement remark" data-magellan-destination="remark4" id="remark4">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Remark 4.4.</span> Essentially the same argument (only with <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline494.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="23" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline494.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {Q}_\ell $
</span></span>
</span>
</span>-coefficients) gives a similar statement for the cycle class map to <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline495.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="9" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline495.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\ell $
</span></span>
</span>
</span>-adic étale cohomology over an arbitrary field.</p>
</div>
<p class="p"> The first two authors have previously given many examples of moduli spaces <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline496.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="49" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline496.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{g,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> that have the CKgP and also satisfy <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline497.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="198" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline497.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$A^*({\mathcal {M}}_{g,n}) = R^*({\mathcal {M}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r5"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Canning and Larson</span>5</a>, Theorem 1.4]. For the inductive arguments in this paper, we need more base cases in genus <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline498.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="10" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline498.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$7$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. In the next section, we prove that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline499.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline499.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{7,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> has the CKgP and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline500.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="195" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline500.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$A^*({\mathcal {M}}_{7,n}) = R^*({\mathcal {M}}_{7,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline501.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="46" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline501.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n \leq 3$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. The table below records the previously known results from [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r5"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Canning and Larson</span>5</a>, Theorem 1.4] together with Theorem <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem7">1.10</a>.</p>
<p class="p"> The following is a consequence of Lemma <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma4">4.3</a>.</p><div class="statement proposition" data-magellan-destination="proposition6" id="proposition6">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Proposition 4.5.</span> For all <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline502.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline502.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g\leq 7$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline503.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="73" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline503.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n \leq c(g)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> as specified in Table <a class="xref table" href="#tab1">1</a>, we have </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU28" id="eqnU28">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu28.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="255" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu28.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}W_k H^k({\mathcal{M}}_{g,n})=RH^k({\mathcal{M}}_{g,n}). \end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">In particular, if <em class="italic">k</em> is odd and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline504.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="73" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline504.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n \leq c(g)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, then </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU29" id="eqnU29">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu29.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="311" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu29.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}W_k H^k({\mathcal{M}}_{g,n}) = \mathrm{gr}^W_{k} H^{k}_c({\mathcal{M}}_{g,n})=0. \end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div>
<section><div class="table-wrap-ada" data-magellan-destination="tab1" id="tab1"><div class="caption"><span class="label">Table 1</span>
<p class="p">
<span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline505.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="48" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline505.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{g,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> has the CKgP and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline506.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="198" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline506.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$A^*({\mathcal {M}}_{g,n})=R^*({\mathcal {M}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline507.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="73" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline507.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n \leq c(g)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, by [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r5"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Canning and Larson</span>5</a>, Theorem 1.4] and Theorem <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem7">1.10</a>.</p>
</div>




<div class="figure-thumb"><img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_tab1.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image" width="374" height="85" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_tab1.png" data-zoomable="false"></div>

</div></section>
</div>
<div class="statement other" data-magellan-destination="sta2" id="sta2">
<h2 class="B">Proof of Theorem <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem6">1.9</a>, assuming Theorem <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem1">1.1</a>.</h2>
<p class="p"> By the hard Lefschetz theorem, it suffices to prove that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline525.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="104" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline525.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^k({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{3,n})^{\mathrm {ss}}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is a polynomial in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline526.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="9" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline526.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathsf {L}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline527.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="27" height="17" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline527.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathsf {S}}_{12}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for fixed <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline528.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="57" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline528.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$k\leq 17$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline529.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="56" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline529.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n\leq 11$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Consider the right exact sequence </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU30" id="eqnU30">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu30.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="444" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu30.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}H^{k-2}(\widetilde{\partial {\mathcal{M}}_{3,n}})\rightarrow H^k({\overline{\mathcal{M}}}_{3,n})\rightarrow W_k H^k({\mathcal{M}}_{3,n})\rightarrow 0. \end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">By Theorem <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem1">1.1</a> and [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r8"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Canning, Larson and Payne</span>8</a>, Theorems 1.1, 1.2 and Lemma 2.1], for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline530.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="62" height="17" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline530.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$k'\leq 15$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline531.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="118" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline531.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{k'}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g',n'})^{\mathrm {ss}}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is a polynomial in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline532.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="9" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline532.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathsf {L}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline533.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="27" height="17" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline533.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathsf {S}}_{12}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for all <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline534.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="51" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline534.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g'\neq 1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and all <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline535.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="16" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline535.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n'$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> as well as for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline536.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="50" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline536.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g'=1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline537.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="63" height="17" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline537.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n'\leq 13$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Since we assume <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline538.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="56" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline538.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n \leq 11$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, no <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline539.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="50" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline539.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,n'}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> with <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline540.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="63" height="17" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline540.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n' \geq 14$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> appears as a factor in a component of the normalized boundary. It follows that, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline541.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="133" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline541.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{k-2}(\widetilde {\partial {\mathcal {M}}_{3,n}})^{\mathrm {ss}}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is a polynomial in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline542.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="9" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline542.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathsf {L}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline543.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="27" height="17" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline543.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathsf {S}}_{12}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. By [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r5"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Canning and Larson</span>5</a>, Theorem 1.4], <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline544.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline544.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{3,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> has the CKgP and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline545.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="195" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline545.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$A^*({\mathcal {M}}_{3,n}) = R^*({\mathcal {M}}_{3,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline546.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="56" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline546.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n \leq 11$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Thus, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline547.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="246" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline547.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_k H^k({\mathcal {M}}_{3,n})=RH^k({\mathcal {M}}_{3,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> by Lemma <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma4">4.3</a>. Hence, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline548.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="117" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline548.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_k H^k({\mathcal {M}}_{3,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is pure Hodge–Tate, and the theorem follows.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="sec" data-magellan-destination="sec9" id="sec9">

<h2 class="A"><span class="label">5</span> The CKgP in genus 7 with at most three marked points</h2>
<p class="p"> In order to prove Theorems <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem1">1.1</a>, <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem3">1.5</a>(3) for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline549.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="55" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline549.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$k = 14$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem5">1.7</a>, we need more base cases in genus <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline550.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="10" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline550.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$7$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. The required base cases are given by Theorem <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem7">1.10</a>, which we now prove.</p>
<p class="p"> In order to prove Theorem <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem7">1.10</a>, we filter <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline551.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline551.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{7,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> by gonality: </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU31" id="eqnU31">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu31.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="273" height="29" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu31.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}\mathcal{M}^{2}_{7,n}\subset \mathcal{M}^{3}_{7,n}\subset \mathcal{M}^4_{7,n} \subset \mathcal{M}^{5}_{7,n}. \end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">Here, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline552.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="28" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline552.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {M}^{k}_{7,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is the locus parametrizing smooth curves <em class="italic">C</em> with <em class="italic">n</em> marked points that admit a map of degree at most <em class="italic">k</em> to <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline553.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="17" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline553.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {P}^1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Standard results from Brill–Noether theory show that the maximal gonality of a genus <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline554.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="10" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline554.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$7$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> curve is <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline555.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="9" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline555.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$5$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. By Proposition <a class="xref statement" href="#proposition5">4.2</a>(3), to show that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline556.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline556.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{7,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> has the CKgP, it suffices to show that each gonality stratum </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU32" id="eqnU32">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu32.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="116" height="29" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu32.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}\mathcal{M}^k_{7,n}\smallsetminus \mathcal{M}^{k-1}_{7,n} \end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">has the CKgP. Moreover, to show that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline557.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="195" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline557.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$A^*({\mathcal {M}}_{7,n})=R^*({\mathcal {M}}_{7,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, it suffices to show for each <em class="italic">k</em>, that all classes supported on <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline558.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="28" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline558.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {M}^k_{7,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> are tautological up to classes supported on <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline559.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="50" height="28" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline559.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {M}^{k-1}_{7,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. In other words, we must show that every class in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline560.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="155" height="28" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline560.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$A^*({\mathcal {M}}_{7,n}^k \smallsetminus {\mathcal {M}}_{7,n}^{k-1})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> pushes forward to a class in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline561.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="155" height="28" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline561.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$A^*({\mathcal {M}}_{7,n} \smallsetminus \mathcal {M}^{k-1}_ {7,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> that is the restriction of a tautological class on <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline562.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline562.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{7,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
<div class="sec" data-magellan-destination="sec10" id="sec10">

<h3 class="B"><span class="label">5.1</span> Hyperelliptic and trigonal loci</h3>
<p class="p"> By [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r5"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Canning and Larson</span>5</a>, Lemma 9.9], if <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline563.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="57" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline563.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n\leq 14$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, then <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline564.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="28" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline564.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {M}^3_{7,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> has the CKgP and all classes in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline565.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="84" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline565.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$A^*({\mathcal {M}}_{7,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> supported on <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline566.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="28" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline566.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {M}^3_{7,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> are tautological. Note that this includes the hyperelliptic locus.</p>
</div>
<div class="sec" data-magellan-destination="sec11" id="sec11">

<h3 class="B"><span class="label">5.2</span> The tetragonal locus</h3>
<p class="p"> To study the tetragonal locus <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline567.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="113" height="28" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline567.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {M}^4_{7,n}\smallsetminus \mathcal {M}^3_{7,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, we will use the Hurwitz stack <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline568.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="54" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline568.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {H}_{4,g,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> parametrizing degree <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline569.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="10" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline569.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$4$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> covers <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline570.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="92" height="23" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline570.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$f\colon C\rightarrow \mathbb {P}^1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, where <em class="italic">C</em> is a smooth curve of genus <em class="italic">g</em> with <em class="italic">n</em> marked points. There is a forgetful morphism </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU33" id="eqnU33">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu33.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="179" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu33.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}\beta_n\colon\mathcal{H}_{4,g,n}\rightarrow {\mathcal{M}}_{g,n}. \end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">Restricting to curves of gonality exactly <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline571.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="10" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline571.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$4$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, we obtain a proper morphism </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU34" id="eqnU34">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu34.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="441" height="31" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu34.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}\beta_n'\colon\mathcal{H}_{4,g,n}^{\Diamond}:= \mathcal{H}_{4,g,n}\smallsetminus \beta_n^{-1}(\mathcal{M}^3_{g,n})\rightarrow {\mathcal{M}}_{g,n}\smallsetminus \mathcal{M}^3_{g,n} \end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">with image <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline572.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="116" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline572.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{g,n}^4 \smallsetminus {\mathcal {M}}_{g,n}^3$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. To show that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline573.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="113" height="28" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline573.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {M}^4_{7,n}\smallsetminus \mathcal {M}^3_{7,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> has the CKgP, it suffices to show that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline574.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="52" height="29" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline574.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {H}_{4,7,n}^\Diamond $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> has the CKgP by Proposition <a class="xref statement" href="#proposition5">4.2</a>(2). We will do so by further stratifying <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline575.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="52" height="29" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline575.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {H}_{4,7,n}^\Diamond $
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
<p class="p"> In [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r6"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Canning and Larson</span>6</a>, Section 4.4], the first two authors studied a stratification of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline576.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="119" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline576.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {H}_{4,7} := \mathcal {H}_{4,7,0}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> with no markings. Here, we carry out a similar analysis with marked points. The Casnati–Ekedahl structure theorem [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r9"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Casnati and Ekedahl</span>9</a>] associates to a point in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline577.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="38" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline577.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {H}_{4,g}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> a rank <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline578.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="8" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline578.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$3$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> vector bundle <em class="italic">E</em> and a rank <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline579.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="10" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline579.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> vector bundle <em class="italic">F</em> on <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline580.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="17" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline580.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {P}^1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, both of degree <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline581.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="41" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline581.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g+3$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, equipped with a canonical isomorphism <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline582.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="113" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline582.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\det E \cong \det F$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r7"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Canning and Larson</span>7</a>, Section 3]. Let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline583.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="14" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline583.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {B}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> be the moduli stack of pairs of vector bundles <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline584.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="51" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline584.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$(E, F)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> on <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline585.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="18" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline585.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {P}^1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> of degree <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline586.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="41" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline586.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g+3$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, together with an isomorphism of their determinants as in [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r7"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Canning and Larson</span>7</a>, Definition 5.2]. Let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline587.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="89" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline587.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\pi \colon \mathcal {P} \to \mathcal {B}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> be the universal <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline588.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="17" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline588.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {P}^1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>-fibration, and let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline589.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="12" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline589.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {E}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline590.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="18" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline590.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {F}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> be the universal bundles on <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline591.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="16" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline591.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {P}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. There is a natural morphism <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline592.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="87" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline592.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {H}_{4,g} \to \mathcal {B}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> that sends a degree <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline593.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="10" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline593.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$4$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> cover to its associated pair of vector bundles. Moreover, the Casnati–Ekedahl construction gives an embedding of the universal curve <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline594.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="11" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline594.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {C}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> over <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline595.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="38" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline595.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {H}_{4,g}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> into <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline596.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="33" height="17" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline596.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {P} \mathcal {E}^{\vee }$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
<p class="p"> Consider the natural commutative diagram </p><div class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqn13" id="eqn13">
<span class="label">(5.1)</span>
<div class="figure-thumb"><img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn13.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image" width="289" height="99" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn13.png" data-zoomable="false"></div>
</div><p class="p continuation">where <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline597.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="20" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline597.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {C}_n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is the universal curve over <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline598.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="54" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline598.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {H}_{4,g,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. For each <em class="italic">i</em>, the map <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline599.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="80" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline599.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$a \circ b \circ \sigma _i$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> sends a pointed curve to the image of the <em class="italic">i</em>th marking under the Casnati–Ekedahl embedding. Taking the product of these maps for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline600.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="95" height="17" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline600.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$i = 1, \ldots , n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, we obtain a commutative diagram </p><div class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqn14" id="eqn14">
<span class="label">(5.2)</span>
<div class="figure-thumb"><img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn14.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image" width="308" height="112" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn14.png" data-zoomable="false"></div>
</div>
<div class="statement lemma" data-magellan-destination="lemma5" id="lemma5">

<h4 class="C"><span class="label">Lemma 5.1</span> (Lemma 10.5 of [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r5"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Canning and Larson</span>5</a>]).</h4>
<p class="p"> Suppose <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline601.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="127" height="30" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline601.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$x \in A^*(\mathcal {H}_{4,g,n}^\Diamond )$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> lies in the image of the map <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline602.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="225" height="30" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline602.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$A^*((\mathbb {P} \mathcal {E}^\vee )^n) \to A^*(\mathcal {H}_{4,g,n}^\Diamond )$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Then <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline603.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="40" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline603.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\beta ^{\prime }_{n*}x$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is tautological on <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline604.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="116" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline604.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{g,n} \smallsetminus {\mathcal {M}}_{g,n}^3$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
</div>
<p class="p"> The splitting types of the Casnati–Ekedahl bundles <em class="italic">E</em> and <em class="italic">F</em> induce a stratification on <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline605.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="37" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline605.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {H}_{4,7}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. We write <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline606.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="127" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline606.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$E = (e_1, e_2, e_3)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline607.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="98" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline607.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$F = (f_1, f_2)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> to indicate that the bundles have splitting types </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU35" id="eqnU35">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu35.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="527" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu35.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}E=\mathcal{O}(e_1)\oplus \mathcal{O}(e_2)\oplus \mathcal{O}(e_3) \qquad \text{and} \qquad F=\mathcal{O}(f_1)\oplus \mathcal{O}(f_2).\end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">We will consider a stratification into three pieces </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU36" id="eqnU36">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu36.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="193" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu36.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}\mathcal{H}_{4,7,n}=X_n\sqcup Y_n \sqcup Z_n. \end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">The three strata correspond to unions of splitting types of <em class="italic">E</em> and <em class="italic">F</em>. The possible splitting types are recorded in [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r6"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Canning and Larson</span>6</a>, Section 4.4]. The locus <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline608.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="21" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline608.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$Z_n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is the set of covers with maximally unbalanced splitting types, and parametrizes hyperelliptic curves [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r6"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Canning and Larson</span>6</a>, Equation 4.5]. Its image in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline609.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline609.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{7,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is contained in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline610.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="28" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline610.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{7,n}^3$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, which has the CKgP when <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline611.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="57" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline611.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n\leq 14$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, as noted above. We will show that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline612.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="23" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline612.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$X_n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline613.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="19" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline613.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$Y_n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> have the CKgP and that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline614.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="99" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline614.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$A^*((\mathbb {P} \mathcal {E}^{\vee })^n)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> surjects onto the Chow ring of their union, which is <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline615.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="52" height="29" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline615.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {H}_{4,7,n}^\Diamond $
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. We start with <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline616.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="23" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline616.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$X_n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
<p class="p"> Let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline617.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="102" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline617.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$X_n\subset \mathcal {H}_{4,7,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> denote the locus of covers with splitting types <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline618.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="101" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline618.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$E = (3, 3, 4)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline619.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="82" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline619.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$F = (5,5)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, or <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline620.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="101" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline620.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$E = (3, 3, 4)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline621.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="82" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline621.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$F = (4, 6)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p><div class="statement lemma" data-magellan-destination="lemma6" id="lemma6">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Lemma 5.2.</span> If <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline622.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="46" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline622.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n \leq 3$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, then <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline623.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="23" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline623.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$X_n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> has the CKgP and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline624.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="195" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline624.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$A^*((\mathbb {P} \mathcal {E}^\vee )^n) \to A^*(X_n)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is surjective.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement other" data-magellan-destination="proof10" id="proof10">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Proof.</span> Taking <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline625.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="46" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline625.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$f =4$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> in [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r5"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Canning and Larson</span>5</a>, Definition 10.8], we have <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline626.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="100" height="28" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline626.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$X_n = \mathcal {H}_{4,7,n}^4$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. The result then follows from [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r5"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Canning and Larson</span>5</a>, Lemmas 10.11 and 10.12] with <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline627.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="45" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline627.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g = 7$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline628.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="88" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline628.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$f = f_1 = 4$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
</div>
<p class="p"> Now let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline629.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="98" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline629.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$Y_n\subset \mathcal {H}_{4,7,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> be the union </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU37" id="eqnU37">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu37.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="143" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu37.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}Y_n = \Sigma_{2,n}\sqcup \Sigma_{3,n}, \end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">where <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline630.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="35" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline630.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Sigma _{2,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> parametrizes covers with splitting types <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline631.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="101" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline631.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$E = (2, 4, 4)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline632.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="82" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline632.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$F = (4,6)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline633.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="35" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline633.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Sigma _{3,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> parametrizes covers with splitting types <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline634.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="101" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline634.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$E = (2, 3, 5)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline635.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="82" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline635.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$F = (4,6)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
<p class="p"> Recall that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline636.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="89" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline636.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\pi \colon \mathcal {P} \rightarrow \mathcal {B}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is the structure map for the <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline637.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="17" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline637.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {P}^1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> bundle <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline638.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="16" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline638.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {P}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline639.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="111" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline639.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\gamma \colon \mathbb {P} \mathcal {E}^\vee \to \mathcal {P}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> denote the structure map and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline640.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="160" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline640.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\eta _i\colon (\mathbb {P} \mathcal {E}^\vee )^n \to \mathbb {P} \mathcal {E}^\vee $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> denote the <em class="italic">i</em>th projection. Define </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU38" id="eqnU38">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu38.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="415" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu38.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}z_i := \eta_i^* \gamma^* c_1(\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{P}}(1)) \ \ \mbox{and} \ \ \zeta_i := \eta_i^* c_1(\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P} \mathcal{E}^\vee}(1)).\end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">Then <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline641.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="13" height="13" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline641.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$z_i$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline642.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="14" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline642.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\zeta _i$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> generate <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline643.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="99" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline643.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$A^*((\mathbb {P} \mathcal {E}^\vee )^n)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> as an algebra over <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline644.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="51" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline644.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$A^*(\mathcal {B})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Write <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline645.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="86" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline645.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Sigma _{\ell } := \Sigma _{\ell , 0}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p><div class="statement lemma" data-magellan-destination="lemma7" id="lemma7">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Lemma 5.3.</span> For <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline646.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="61" height="17" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline646.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\ell = 2,3$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline647.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="46" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline647.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n \leq 3$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, there is a surjection </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU39" id="eqnU39">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu39.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="361" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu39.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}A^*(\Sigma_{\ell})[z_1, \ldots, z_n, \zeta_1, \ldots, \zeta_n] \to A^*(\Sigma_{\ell,n})\end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">induced by <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline648.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="90" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline648.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Sigma _{\ell ,n}\rightarrow \Sigma _\ell $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and restriction from <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline649.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="59" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline649.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$(\mathbb {P} \mathcal {E}^{\vee })^n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Moreover, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline650.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="36" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline650.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Sigma _{\ell ,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> has the CKgP.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement other" data-magellan-destination="proof11" id="proof11">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Proof.</span> Let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline651.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="11" height="17" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline651.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\vec {e}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline652.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="14" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline652.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\vec {f}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> be the splitting types associated to <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline653.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="21" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline653.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Sigma _{\ell }$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, and let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline654.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="81" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline654.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {B}_{\vec {e}, \vec {f}} \subset \mathcal {B}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> be the locally closed substack that parametrizes pairs of bundles <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline655.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="51" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline655.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$(E, F)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> with locally constant splitting types <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline656.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="11" height="17" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline656.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\vec {e}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline657.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="14" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline657.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\vec {f}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. We write <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline658.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="249" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline658.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {O}(\vec {e}) := \mathcal {O}(e_1) \oplus \cdots \oplus \mathcal {O}(e_k)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. By construction, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline659.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="35" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline659.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Sigma _{\ell ,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is the preimage of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline660.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="39" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline660.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {B}_{\vec {e}, \vec {f}}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> along <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline661.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="100" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline661.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {H}_{4,7,n} \to \mathcal {B}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. We, therefore, study the base change of (<a class="xref disp-formula" href="#eqn14">5.2</a>) along <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline662.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="87" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline662.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {B}_{\vec {e}, \vec {f}} \to \mathcal {B}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>: </p><div class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqn15" id="eqn15">
<span class="label">(5.3)</span>
<div class="figure-thumb"><img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn15.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image" width="205" height="107" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn15.png" data-zoomable="false"></div>
</div>
<p class="p"> We now recall the description of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline663.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="21" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline663.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Sigma _\ell $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> as an open substack of a vector bundle on <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline664.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="39" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline664.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {B}_{\vec {e}, \vec {f}}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, as in [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r6"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Canning and Larson</span>6</a>, Lemma 3.10]. Let </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU40" id="eqnU40">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu40.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="624" height="28" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu40.png" data-zoomable="true">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}U \subset H^0(\mathbb{P}^1,\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})^\vee \otimes \operatorname{\mathrm{Sym}}^2 \mathcal{O}(\vec{e})) = H^0(\mathbb{P} \mathcal{O}(\vec{e})^\vee, \gamma^*\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})^\vee \otimes \mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P} \mathcal{O}(\vec{e})^\vee}(2))\end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">be the open subset of equations that define a smooth curve, as in [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r6"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Canning and Larson</span>6</a>, Lemma 3.10]. Then </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU41" id="eqnU41">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu41.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="433" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu41.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}\Sigma_\ell = [(U \times \mathbb{G}_m)/\operatorname{\mathrm{SL}}_2 \ltimes (\operatorname{\mathrm{Aut}}(\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})) \times \operatorname{\mathrm{Aut}}(\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})))].\end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">The stack <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline665.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="39" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline665.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {B}_{\vec {e}, \vec {f}}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is the part obtained by forgetting <em class="italic">U</em>: </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU42" id="eqnU42">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu42.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="397" height="32" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu42.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e}, \vec{f}} = [\mathbb{G}_m/\operatorname{\mathrm{SL}}_2 \ltimes (\operatorname{\mathrm{Aut}}(\mathcal{O}(\vec{e})) \times \operatorname{\mathrm{Aut}}(\mathcal{O}(\vec{f})))].\end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">As explained in [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r6"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Canning and Larson</span>6</a>, Equation 3.1], there is a product of stacks <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline666.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="51" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline666.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {BGL}}_n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> which is an affine bundle over <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline667.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="103" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline667.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathrm {B}\!\operatorname {\mathrm {Aut}}(\mathcal {O}(\vec {e}))$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. As such, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline668.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="39" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline668.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {B}_{\vec {e}, \vec {f}}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> has the CKgP by Proposition <a class="xref statement" href="#proposition5">4.2</a>(4) and (5). It follows that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline669.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="21" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline669.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Sigma _{\ell }$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> also has the CKgP by Proposition <a class="xref statement" href="#proposition5">4.2</a>(1) and (4).</p>
<p class="p"> Let us define the rank <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline670.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="10" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline670.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> vector bundle <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline671.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="193" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline671.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {W} := \gamma ^*\mathcal {F}^\vee \otimes \mathcal {O}_{\mathbb {P} \mathcal {E}^\vee }(2)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> on <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline672.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="33" height="17" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline672.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {P} \mathcal {E}^\vee $
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Write <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline673.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="45" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline673.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {W}_{\vec {e},\vec {f}}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for the restriction of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline674.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="22" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline674.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {W}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> to <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline675.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="71" height="28" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline675.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {P} \mathcal {E}^\vee |_{\mathcal {B}_{\vec {e},\vec {f}}}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. The discussion above says that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline676.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="21" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline676.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Sigma _{\ell }$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is an open substack of the vector bundle <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline677.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="110" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline677.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$(\pi \circ \gamma )_*\mathcal {W}_{\vec {e},\vec {f}}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> on <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline678.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="39" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline678.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {B}_{\vec {e},\vec {f}}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
<p class="p"> Next, we give a similar description with marked points. Consider the evaluation map </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU43" id="eqnU43">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu43.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="265" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu43.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}(\pi\circ\gamma)^*(\pi\circ\gamma)_*\mathcal{W}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}} \rightarrow \mathcal{W}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}. \end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">Pulling back to the fiber product <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline679.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="98" height="28" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline679.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$(\mathbb {P} \mathcal {E}^\vee |_{\mathcal {B}_{\vec {e},\vec {f}}})^n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, we obtain </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqn16" id="eqn16">
<span class="label">(5.4)</span>
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn16.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="345" height="57" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn16.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$ \begin{align} \eta_j^*(\pi\circ\gamma)^*(\pi\circ\gamma)_*\mathcal{W}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}\rightarrow \bigoplus_{i=1}^n\eta_i^*\mathcal{W}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}. \end{align} $$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">Note that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline680.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="201" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline680.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\eta _j^*(\pi \circ \gamma )^*(\pi \circ \gamma )_*\mathcal {W}_{\vec {e},\vec {f}}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is independent of <em class="italic">j</em>. The kernel <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline681.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="15" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline681.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {Y}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> of (<a class="xref disp-formula" href="#eqn16">5.4</a>) parametrizes tuples of <em class="italic">n</em> points on <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline682.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="65" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline682.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {P} \mathcal {O}(\vec {e})^\vee $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> together with a section of </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU44" id="eqnU44">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu44.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="314" height="28" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu44.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}H^0(\mathbb{P} \mathcal{O}(\vec{e})^\vee, \gamma^* \mathcal{O}(\vec{f})^\vee \otimes \mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P} \mathcal{O}(\vec{e})^\vee}(2))\end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">that vanishes on the points. There is, therefore, a natural map <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline683.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="88" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline683.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Sigma _{\ell ,n} \hookrightarrow \mathcal {Y}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> defined by sending a pointed curve to the images of the points on <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline684.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="65" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline684.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {P} \mathcal {O}(\vec {e})^\vee $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and the defining section of the curve. The kernel <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline685.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="15" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline685.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {Y}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is not locally free. Nevertheless, its restriction to the open substack <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline686.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="150" height="28" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline686.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$U_n \subset (\mathbb {P} \mathcal {E}^\vee |_{\mathcal {B}_{\vec {e},\vec {f}}})^n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> where (<a class="xref disp-formula" href="#eqn16">5.4</a>) is surjective is locally free.</p>
<p class="p"> We claim that the map <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline687.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="84" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline687.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Sigma _{\ell ,n} \to \mathcal {Y}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> factors through <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline688.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="39" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline688.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {Y}|_{U_n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. To see this, suppose <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline689.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="104" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline689.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$C \subset \mathbb {P} \mathcal {O}(\vec {e})^\vee $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is the vanishing of a section of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline690.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="196" height="28" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline690.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\gamma ^* \mathcal {O}(\vec {f})^\vee \otimes \mathcal {O}_{\mathbb {P} \mathcal {O}(\vec {e})^\vee }(2)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <em class="italic">C</em> is smooth and irreducible. By [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r5"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Canning and Larson</span>5</a>, Lemma 10.6], if <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline691.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="46" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline691.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n\leq 3$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, the evaluation map (<a class="xref disp-formula" href="#eqn16">5.4</a>) is surjective at any tuple of <em class="italic">n</em> distinct points on <em class="italic">C</em>. It follows that the image of the composition <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline692.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="218" height="28" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline692.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Sigma _{\ell ,n} \rightarrow \mathcal {Y} \rightarrow (\mathbb {P} \mathcal {E}^\vee |_{\mathcal {B}_{\vec {e},\vec {f}}})^n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is contained in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline693.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="23" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline693.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$U_n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Hence, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline694.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="112" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline694.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Sigma _{\ell ,n} \hookrightarrow \mathcal {Y}|_{U_n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
<p class="p"> In summary, we have a sequence of maps </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU45" id="eqnU45">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu45.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="501" height="30" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu45.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}\Sigma_{\ell,n} \hookrightarrow \mathcal{Y}|_{U_n} \rightarrow U_n \hookrightarrow (\mathbb{P} \mathcal{E}^\vee|_{\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}})^n \rightarrow (\mathcal{P}|_{\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}})^n \rightarrow \mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}}, \end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">each of which is an open inclusion, vector bundle or product of projective bundles. Since <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline695.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="39" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline695.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {B}_{\vec {e},\vec {f}}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> has the CKgP, it follows that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline696.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="36" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline696.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Sigma _{\ell ,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> also has the CKgP by Proposition <a class="xref statement" href="#proposition5">4.2</a>(1), (4) and (<a class="xref sec" href="#sec9">5</a>). Moreover, we see that </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU46" id="eqnU46">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu46.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="379" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu46.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}A^*(\mathcal{B}_{\vec{e},\vec{f}})[z_1, \ldots, z_n, \zeta_1, \ldots, \zeta_n] \to A^*(\Sigma_{\ell,n})\end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">is surjective. Finally, note that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline697.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="108" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline697.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Sigma _{\ell ,n} \to \mathcal {B}_{\vec {e},\vec {f}}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> factors through <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline698.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="21" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline698.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Sigma _\ell $
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, so <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline699.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="186" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline699.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$A^*(\mathcal {B}_{\vec {e},\vec {f}}) \to A^*(\Sigma _{\ell ,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> factors through <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline700.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="59" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline700.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$A^*(\Sigma _{\ell })$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. This proves the claim.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement corollary" data-magellan-destination="corollary5" id="corollary5">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Corollary 5.4.</span> For <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline701.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="46" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline701.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n \leq 3$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline702.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="52" height="29" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline702.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {H}_{4,7,n}^\Diamond $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> has the CKgP. Hence, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline703.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="28" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline703.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {M}^4_{7,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> has the CKgP.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement other" data-magellan-destination="proof12" id="proof12">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Proof.</span> We have <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline704.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="143" height="29" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline704.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {H}_{4,7,n}^\Diamond = X_n \sqcup Y_n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. By Lemmas <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma6">5.2</a> and <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma7">5.3</a>, each of these pieces has the CKgP. Note that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline705.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="52" height="29" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline705.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {H}^{\Diamond }_{4,7,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> maps properly onto <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline706.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="113" height="28" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline706.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {M}^4_{7,n}\smallsetminus \mathcal {M}^3_{7,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline707.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="28" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline707.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{7,n}^3$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> has the CKgP. Thus, the result follows by Proposition <a class="xref statement" href="#proposition5">4.2</a>(2)–(3).</p>
</div>
<p class="p"> The next step is to show that all classes in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline708.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="73" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline708.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$A^*(\Sigma _{\ell ,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> are restrictions from <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline709.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="59" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline709.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$(\mathbb {P} \mathcal {E}^{\vee })^n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p><div class="statement lemma" data-magellan-destination="lemma8" id="lemma8">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Lemma 5.5.</span> For <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline710.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="61" height="17" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline710.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\ell = 2,3$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline711.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="46" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline711.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n \leq 3$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, the restriction <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline712.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="207" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline712.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$A^*((\mathbb {P} \mathcal {E}^{\vee })^n) \to A^*(\Sigma _{\ell ,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is surjective.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement other" data-magellan-destination="proof13" id="proof13">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Proof.</span> Consider the following diagram: </p><div class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqn17" id="eqn17">
<span class="label">(5.5)</span>
<div class="figure-thumb"><img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn17.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image" width="572" height="95" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn17.png" data-zoomable="false"></div>
</div><p class="p continuation">The map <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline713.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="145" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline713.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$A^*(\mathcal {B}) \to A^*(\Sigma _{\ell })$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is surjective by [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r6"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Canning and Larson</span>6</a>, Lemma 4.2] for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline714.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="43" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline714.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\ell =2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, and by [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r6"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Canning and Larson</span>6</a>, Lemma 4.3(1)] for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline715.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="42" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline715.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\ell = 3$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Therefore, the bottom horizontal arrow is surjective. By Lemma <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma7">5.3</a>, the right vertical arrow is also surjective. Hence, the top horizontal arrow is surjective.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement lemma" data-magellan-destination="lemma9" id="lemma9">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Lemma 5.6.</span> For <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline716.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="46" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline716.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n \leq 3$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, the pullback map <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline717.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="224" height="29" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline717.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$A^*((\mathbb {P} \mathcal {E}^\vee )^n) \to A^*(\mathcal {H}_{4,7,n}^\Diamond )$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is surjective.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement other" data-magellan-destination="proof14" id="proof14">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Proof.</span> First, we fix some notation. Let </p><div class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU47" id="eqnU47">
<div class="figure-thumb"><img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu47.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image" width="176" height="33" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu47.png" data-zoomable="false"></div>
</div><p class="p continuation">denote the natural closed inclusion maps. Let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline718.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="174" height="29" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline718.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\phi \colon \mathcal {H}_{4,7,n}^\Diamond \to (\mathbb {P} \mathcal {E}^\vee )^n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> be the map from the top left to top right in diagram (<a class="xref disp-formula" href="#eqn14">5.2</a>). We let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline719.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="153" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline719.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\phi ':X_n\rightarrow (\mathbb {P} \mathcal {E}^{\vee })^n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> be the composite of the open inclusion <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline720.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="113" height="29" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline720.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$X_n \hookrightarrow \mathcal {H}_{4,7,n}^{\Diamond }$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline721.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="11" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline721.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\phi $
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline722.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="82" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline722.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\psi :=\phi \circ \iota $
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, and let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline723.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="19" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline723.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\psi '$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> be the composite of the open inclusion <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline724.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="92" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline724.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Sigma _{2,n}\hookrightarrow Y_n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline725.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="13" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline725.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\psi $
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
<p class="p"> Consider the following commutative diagram, where the bottom row is exact </p><div class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqn18" id="eqn18">
<span class="label">(5.6)</span>
<div class="figure-thumb"><img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn18.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image" width="461" height="102" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn18.png" data-zoomable="false"></div>
</div><p class="p continuation">By Lemma <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma6">5.2</a>, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline726.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="27" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline726.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\phi ^{\prime }*$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is surjective. It thus suffices to show that the image of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline727.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="13" height="11" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline727.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\iota _*$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is contained in the image of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline728.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="18" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline728.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\phi ^*$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. To do so, we consider another commutative diagram where the bottom row is exact </p><div class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqn19" id="eqn19">
<span class="label">(5.7)</span>
<div class="figure-thumb"><img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn19.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image" width="489" height="98" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn19.png" data-zoomable="false"></div>
</div><p class="p continuation">By Lemma <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma8">5.5</a>, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline729.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="29" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline729.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\psi ^{\prime }*$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is surjective. Moreover, by the projection formula and Lemma <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma8">5.5</a>, the image of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline730.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="8" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline730.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\jmath $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is generated as an <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline731.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="99" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline731.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$A^*((\mathbb {P} \mathcal {E}^{\vee })^n)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> module by the fundamental class <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline732.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="132" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline732.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$[\Sigma _{3,n}]\in A^*(Y_n)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Therefore, any class <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline733.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="94" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline733.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\alpha \in A^*(Y_n)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> can be written as </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU48" id="eqnU48">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu48.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="410" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu48.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}\alpha = \psi^*\alpha_0+[\Sigma_{3,n}]\psi^*\alpha_1=\iota^*\phi^*\alpha_0+[\Sigma_{3,n}]\iota^*\phi^*\alpha_1, \end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">where <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline734.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="142" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline734.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\alpha _i\in A^*((\mathbb {P} \mathcal {E}^\vee )^n)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. By the projection formula, </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU49" id="eqnU49">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu49.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="249" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu49.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}\iota_*\alpha=[Y_n]\phi^*\alpha_0+[\Sigma_{3,n}]\phi^*\alpha_1, \end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">where now the fundamental class <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline735.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="48" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline735.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$[\Sigma _{3,n}]$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is a class on <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline736.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="52" height="29" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline736.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {H}^{\Diamond }_{4,7,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. It thus suffices to show that the classes <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline737.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="32" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline737.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$[Y_n]$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline738.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="48" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline738.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$[\Sigma _{3,n}]$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> are in the image of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline739.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="18" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline739.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\phi ^*$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
<p class="p"> By [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r6"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Canning and Larson</span>6</a>, Lemma 4.8], <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline740.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="34" height="23" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline740.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$[\overline {\Sigma _{\ell }}]$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is in the image of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline741.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="162" height="29" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline741.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$A^*(\mathcal {B}) \to A^*(\mathcal {H}_{4,7}^\Diamond )$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Because <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline742.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="48" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline742.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$[\Sigma _{3,n}]$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is the pullback of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline743.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="34" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline743.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$[\Sigma _3]$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> along <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline744.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="200" height="29" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline744.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$A^*(\mathcal {H}_{4,7}^{\Diamond }) \to A^*(\mathcal {H}_{4,7,n}^{\Diamond })$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline745.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="32" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline745.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$[Y_n]$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is the pullback of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline746.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="33" height="23" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline746.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$[\overline {\Sigma _{2}}]$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, both <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline747.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="48" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline747.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$[\Sigma _{3,n}]$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline748.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="32" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline748.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$[Y_n]$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> are in the image of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline749.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="176" height="29" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline749.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$A^*(\mathcal {B})\to A^*(\mathcal {H}_{4,7,n}^{\Diamond })$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Hence, they are in the image of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline750.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="19" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline750.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\phi ^*$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
</div>
<p class="p"> Recall that proper, surjective maps induce surjective maps on rational Chow groups. Since the map <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline751.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="237" height="29" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline751.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\beta _n'\colon \mathcal {H}_{4,7,n}^\Diamond \to {\mathcal {M}}_{7,n} \smallsetminus {\mathcal {M}}_{7,n}^3$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is proper with image <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline752.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="113" height="28" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline752.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{7,n}^4 \smallsetminus {\mathcal {M}}_{7,n}^3$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, every class supported on the tetragonal locus is the pushforward of a class from <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline753.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="52" height="29" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline753.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {H}_{4,7,n}^\Diamond $
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Combining Lemmas <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma5">5.1</a> and <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma9">5.6</a>, therefore, proves the following.</p><div class="statement lemma" data-magellan-destination="lemma10" id="lemma10">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Lemma 5.7.</span> If <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline754.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="46" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline754.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n \leq 3$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, then all classes supported on <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline755.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="113" height="28" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline755.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{7,n}^4 \smallsetminus {\mathcal {M}}_{7,n}^3$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> are tautological.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="sec" data-magellan-destination="sec12" id="sec12">

<h3 class="B"><span class="label">5.3</span> The pentagonal locus</h3>
<p class="p"> It remains to study the locus <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline756.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="185" height="28" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline756.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{7,n}^\circ = {\mathcal {M}}_{7,n} \smallsetminus {\mathcal {M}}_{7,n}^4$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> of curves of gonality exactly <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline757.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="9" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline757.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$5$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Mukai showed that every curve in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline758.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="32" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline758.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{7}^{\circ }$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is realized as a linear section of the orthogonal Grassmannian in its spinor embedding <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline759.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="149" height="23" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline759.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(5,10) \hookrightarrow \mathbb {P}^{15}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r21"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Mukai</span>21</a>]. To take advantage of this construction, we first develop a few lemmas about the orthogonal Grassmannian.</p>
<div class="sec" data-magellan-destination="sec13" id="sec13">

<h4 class="C"><span class="label">5.3.1</span> The orthogonal Grassmannian</h4>
<p class="p"> Let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline760.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="14" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline760.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {V}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> be the universal rank <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline761.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="18" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline761.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$10$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> bundle on <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline762.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="56" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline762.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {BSO}}_{10}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. The universal orthogonal Grassmannian is the quotient stack <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline763.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="151" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline763.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$[\operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(5, 10)/\mathrm {SO}_{10}]$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, which we think of as the orthogonal Grassmann bundle with structure map <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline764.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="200" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline764.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\pi \colon \operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(5,\mathcal {V}) \to \operatorname {\mathrm {BSO}}_{10}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. By construction, the pullback of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline765.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="14" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline765.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {V}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> along <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline766.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="11" height="11" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline766.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\pi $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> satisfies <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline767.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="120" height="17" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline767.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\pi ^* \mathcal {V} = \mathcal {U} \oplus \mathcal {U}^{\vee }$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> where <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline768.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="16" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline768.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {U}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is the universal rank <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline769.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="9" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline769.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$5$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> subbundle on <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline770.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="78" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline770.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(5, \mathcal {V})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p><div class="statement lemma" data-magellan-destination="lemma11" id="lemma11">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Lemma 5.8.</span> The stack </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU50" id="eqnU50">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu50.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="259" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu50.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}\operatorname{\mathrm{OG}}(5,\mathcal{V}) \cong [\operatorname{\mathrm{OG}}(5, 10)/\mathrm{SO}_{10}]\end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">has the CKgP. Moreover, its Chow ring is freely generated by the Chern classes of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline771.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="16" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline771.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {U}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement other" data-magellan-destination="proof15" id="proof15">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Proof.</span> Let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline772.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="185" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline772.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$V = \mathrm {span}\{e_1, \ldots , e_{10}\}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> be a fixed <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline773.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="18" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline773.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$10$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>-dimensional vector space with quadratic form </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU51" id="eqnU51">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu51.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="108" height="51" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu51.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}Q = \left(\begin{matrix} 0 &amp; I_5 \\ I_5 &amp; 0 \end{matrix}\right).\end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">Let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline774.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="178" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline774.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$U = \mathrm {span}\{e_1, \ldots , e_5\}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, which is an isotropic subspace. The stabilizer of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline775.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="41" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline775.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathrm {SO}_{10}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> acting on <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline776.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="85" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline776.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(5,10)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> at <em class="italic">U</em> is </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU52" id="eqnU52">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu52.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="396" height="52" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu52.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}\mathrm{Stab}_U = \left\{M = \left(\begin{matrix} A &amp; B \\ 0 &amp; D \end{matrix}\right) : M^TQM =Q\right\} \subset \mathrm{SO}_{10}. \end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">Expanding, we have </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU53" id="eqnU53">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu53.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="515" height="51" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu53.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}M^T Q M = \left(\begin{matrix} A^T &amp; 0 \\ B^T &amp; D^T \end{matrix}\right)\left(\begin{matrix} 0 &amp; I_5 \\ I_5 &amp; 0 \end{matrix}\right)\left(\begin{matrix} A &amp; B \\ 0 &amp; D \end{matrix}\right) = \left( \begin{matrix} 0 &amp; A^TD \\ D^TA &amp; B^TD + D^TB \end{matrix}\right).\end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">Thus, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline777.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="48" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline777.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathrm {Stab}_U$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is defined by the conditions <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline778.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="100" height="23" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline778.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$D = (A^T)^{-1}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline779.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="142" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline779.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$B^TD + D^TB = 0$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
<p class="p"> Note that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline780.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="48" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline780.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathrm {Stab}_U$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is a maximal parabolic subgroup and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline781.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="212" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline781.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(5, 10) = \mathrm {SO}_{10}/\mathrm {Stab}_U$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. As such, the quotient <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline782.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="151" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline782.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$[\operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(5,10)/\mathrm {SO}_{10}]$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is equivalent to the classifying stack <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline783.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="63" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline783.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathrm {BStab}_U$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. To gain a better understanding of the latter, consider the group homomorphism </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU54" id="eqnU54">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu54.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="333" height="51" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu54.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}\operatorname{\mathrm{GL}}_5 \hookrightarrow \mathrm{Stab}_U, \qquad A\mapsto \left(\begin{matrix} A &amp; 0 \\ 0 &amp; (A^T)^{-1}\end{matrix}\right).\end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">For fixed <em class="italic">D</em>, the condition <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline784.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="142" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline784.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$B^TD + D^TB = 0$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is linear in <em class="italic">B</em>. Specifically, it says that <em class="italic">B</em> lies in the <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline785.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="60" height="23" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline785.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$(D^{T})^{-1}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> translation of the <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline786.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="31" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline786.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {A}^{10}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> of skew symmetric <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline787.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="42" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline787.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$5 \times 5$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> matrices. In particular, the cosets of the subgroup <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline788.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="122" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline788.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {GL}}_5 \hookrightarrow \mathrm {Stab}_U$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> are isomorphic to affine spaces <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline789.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="31" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline789.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {A}^{10}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. In other words, the induced map on classifying spaces <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline790.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="252" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline790.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {BGL}}_5 \to \mathrm {BStab}_U \cong \operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(5, \mathcal {V})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is an affine bundle. It follows that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline791.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="78" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline791.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(5, \mathcal {V})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> has the CKgP by Proposition <a class="xref statement" href="#proposition5">4.2</a>(4) and (5).</p>
<p class="p"> Furthermore, by construction, the tautological subbundle <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline792.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="16" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline792.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {U}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> on <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline793.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="78" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline793.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(5, \mathcal {V})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> pulls back to the tautological rank <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline794.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="9" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline794.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$5$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> bundle on <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline795.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="48" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline795.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {BGL}}_5$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. It follows that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline796.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="217" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline796.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$A^*(\mathrm {BStab}_U) \cong A^*(\mathrm {BGL}_5)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and is freely generated by the Chern classes of the tautological bundle.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement remark" data-magellan-destination="remark5" id="remark5">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Remark 5.9.</span> There is also a natural map <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline797.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="117" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline797.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathrm {Stab}_U \to \operatorname {\mathrm {GL}}_5$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> that sends <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline798.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="54" height="51" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline798.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\left (\begin {matrix} A &amp; B \\ 0 &amp; D \end {matrix}\right )$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> to <em class="italic">A</em>. The kernel of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline799.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="117" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline799.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathrm {Stab}_U \to \operatorname {\mathrm {GL}}_5$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is the subgroup <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline800.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="99" height="23" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline800.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$G \cong (\mathbb {G}_a)^{10}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, where <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline801.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="119" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline801.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$A = I_5, D = I_5$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline802.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="95" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline802.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$B + B^T = 0$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. This shows that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline803.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="48" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline803.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathrm {Stab}_U$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is actually a semi-direct product <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline804.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="72" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline804.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$G \rtimes \operatorname {\mathrm {GL}}_5$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. The map <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline805.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="146" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline805.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathrm {BStab}_U \to \operatorname {\mathrm {BGL}}_5$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is a <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline806.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="29" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline806.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathrm {B}G$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>-banded gerbe.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement lemma" data-magellan-destination="lemma12" id="lemma12">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Lemma 5.10.</span> Let <em class="italic">V</em> be a rank <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline807.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="21" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline807.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$2\nu $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> vector bundle with quadratic form on <em class="italic">X</em>. </p><ol class="list number nomark">
<li class="list-item">

<p class="p"><span class="label">1.</span> The rational Chow ring of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline808.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="78" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline808.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(\nu , V)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is generated over the Chow ring of <em class="italic">X</em> by the Chern classes of the tautological subbundle.</p>
</li>
<li class="list-item">

<p class="p"><span class="label">2.</span> If <em class="italic">X</em> has the CKgP, then <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline809.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="78" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline809.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(\nu , V)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> has the CKgP.</p>
</li>
</ol>
</div>
<div class="statement other" data-magellan-destination="proof16" id="proof16">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Proof.</span> The argument is very similar to that for Grassmannians in type A.</p>
<p class="p"> First consider the case when <em class="italic">X</em> is a point. The orthogonal Grassmannian <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline810.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="85" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline810.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(\nu , 2\nu )$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is stratified by Schubert cells, each of which is isomorphic to an affine space. By Proposition <a class="xref statement" href="#proposition5">4.2</a>(3), it follows that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline811.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="85" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline811.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(\nu , 2\nu )$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> has the CKgP. Moreover, the fundamental classes of these cells are expressed in terms of the Chern classes of the tautological quotient or subbundle via a Giambelli formula [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r19"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Kresch and Tamvakis</span>19</a>, p. 1–2]. Note that this formula involves dividing by <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline812.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="10" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline812.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, so it is important that we work with rational coefficients for this claim. In conclusion, the Chern classes of the tautological subbundle generate the Chow ring of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline813.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="85" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline813.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(\nu , 2\nu )$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
<p class="p"> More generally, for a fiber bundle <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline814.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="158" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline814.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$f\colon \operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(\nu , V) \to X$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, to prove (1), we stratify <em class="italic">X</em> into locally closed subsets <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline815.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="19" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline815.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$X_i$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> over which <em class="italic">V</em> is trivial, such that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline816.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="69" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline816.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\overline X_i \supset X_j$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline817.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="41" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline817.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$i \leq j$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline818.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="19" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline818.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$X_i$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> has codimension at least <em class="italic">i</em>. To check that the desired classes generate <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline819.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="119" height="23" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline819.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$A^k(\operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(\nu , V))$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for a given <em class="italic">k</em>, it suffices to show that they generate <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline820.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="248" height="23" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline820.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$A^k(f^{-1}(X_0 \cup X_1 \cup \cdots \cup X_k))$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
<p class="p"> Over each piece of the stratification, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline821.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="219" height="23" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline821.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$f^{-1}(X_i) = X_i \times \operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(\nu , 2\nu )$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Since <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline822.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="85" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline822.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(\nu ,2\nu )$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> has the CKgP, the Chow ring of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline823.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="219" height="23" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline823.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$f^{-1}(X_i) = X_i \times \operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(\nu , 2\nu )$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is generated by <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline824.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="57" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline824.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$A^*(X_i)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and restrictions of the Chern classes from the tautological subbundle on <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline825.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="78" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline825.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(\nu , V)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. By excision and the push-pull formula, the Chow ring of any finite union <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline826.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="302" height="23" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline826.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$f^{-1}(X_0) \cup f^{-1}(X_1) \cup \cdots \cup f^{-1}(X_k)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is generated by the desired classes.</p>
<p class="p"> Finally, (2) follows from (1) exactly as in [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r5"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Canning and Larson</span>5</a>, Lemma 3.7].</p>
</div>
<div class="statement corollary" data-magellan-destination="corollary6" id="corollary6">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Corollary 5.11.</span> For any <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline827.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="46" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline827.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n \geq 1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, the <em class="italic">n</em>-fold fiber product </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU55" id="eqnU55">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu55.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="433" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu55.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}\operatorname{\mathrm{OG}}(5, \mathcal{V})^n := \operatorname{\mathrm{OG}}(5, \mathcal{V}) \times_{\operatorname{\mathrm{BSO}}_{10}} \cdots \times_{\operatorname{\mathrm{BSO}}_{10}} \operatorname{\mathrm{OG}}(5, \mathcal{V}) \end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">has the CKgP, and its Chow ring is generated by the Chern classes of the tautological subbundles <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline828.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="91" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline828.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {U}_1, \ldots , \mathcal {U}_n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> pulled back from each factor.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement other" data-magellan-destination="proof17" id="proof17">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Proof.</span> The case <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline829.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="44" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline829.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n = 1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> follows from Lemma <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma11">5.8</a>. For <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline830.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="45" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline830.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n&gt; 1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, the <em class="italic">n</em>-fold fiber product is an orthogonal Grassmann bundle over the <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline831.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="56" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline831.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$(n-1)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>-fold fiber product, so the claim follows from Lemma <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma12">5.10</a>.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement remark" data-magellan-destination="remark6" id="remark6">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Remark 5.12.</span> By Proposition <a class="xref statement" href="#proposition5">4.2</a>(2), the fact that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline832.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="78" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline832.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(5, \mathcal {V})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> has the CKgP implies that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline833.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="56" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline833.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {BSO}}_{10}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> also has the CKgP. It should be possible to show that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline834.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="56" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline834.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {BSO}}_{10}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> has the CKgP (with integral coefficients as well) using the calculation of its Chow ring by Field [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r14"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Field</span>14</a>]. If the calculation there holds over any field, it would show that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline835.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="56" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline835.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {BSO}}_{10}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> has Totaro’s “weak Chow–Künneth Property,” which is equivalent to the CKgP by the proof of [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r34"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Totaro</span>34</a>, Theorem 4.1].</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="sec" data-magellan-destination="sec14" id="sec14">

<h4 class="C"><span class="label">5.3.2</span> Review of the Mukai construction</h4>
<p class="p"> We first review Mukai’s construction and then explain how to modify it for pointed curves. The canonical model of a pentagonal genus <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline836.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="10" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline836.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$7$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> curve <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline837.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="59" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline837.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$C \subset \mathbb {P}^6$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> lies on a <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline838.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="18" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline838.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$10$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>-dimensional space of quadrics. The vector space <em class="italic">W</em> of these quadrics is defined by the exact sequence </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqn20" id="eqn20">
<span class="label">(5.8)</span>
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn20.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="419" height="28" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn20.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$ \begin{align} 0 \rightarrow W \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathrm{Sym}}^2 H^0(C, \omega_C) \to H^0(C, \omega_C^{\otimes 2}) \rightarrow 0. \end{align} $$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">For each <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline839.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="52" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline839.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$p \in C$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, the subspace <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline840.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="73" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline840.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_p \subset W$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> of quadrics that are singular at <em class="italic">p</em> is <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline841.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="9" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline841.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$5$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>-dimensional. It appears in the exact sequence (see [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r21"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Mukai</span>21</a>, Section 3]) </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqn21" id="eqn21">
<span class="label">(5.9)</span>
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn21.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="529" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn21.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$ \begin{align} 0 \rightarrow W_p \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathrm{Sym}}^2 H^0(C, \omega_C(-p)) \to H^0(C,\omega_C(-p)^{\otimes 2}) \rightarrow 0. \end{align} $$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">Mukai shows that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline842.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="28" height="17" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline842.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W^\vee $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> has a canonical quadratic form and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline843.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="29" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline843.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_p^\perp $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is an isotropic subspace, so one obtains a map <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline844.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="140" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline844.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$C \to \operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(5, W^\vee )$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> via <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline845.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="210" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline845.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$p \mapsto [W_p^\perp ] \in \operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(5, W^\vee )$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r21"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Mukai</span>21</a>, Theorem 0.4].</p>
<p class="p"> Let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline846.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="155" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline846.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(5, 10) \hookrightarrow \mathbb {P} S^+$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> be the spinor embedding, as in [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r21"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Mukai</span>21</a>, Section 1]. The composition </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU56" id="eqnU56">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu56.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="323" height="23" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu56.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}C \to \operatorname{\mathrm{OG}}(5, W^\vee) \cong \operatorname{\mathrm{OG}}(5, 10) \hookrightarrow \mathbb{P} S^+\end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">realizes <em class="italic">C</em> as a linear section <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline847.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="225" height="23" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline847.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$C = \operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(5,10) \cap \mathbb {P}^6 \subset \mathbb {P} S^+$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline848.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="59" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline848.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$C \subset \mathbb {P}^6$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is canonically embedded [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r21"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Mukai</span>21</a>, Theorem 0.4]. Conversely, if a linear section <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline849.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="128" height="23" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline849.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {P}^6 \cap \operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(5, 10)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is a smooth curve, then it is a canonically embedded pentagonal genus <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline850.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="10" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline850.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$7$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> curve [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r21"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Mukai</span>21</a>, Proposition 2.2]. This construction works in families, and Mukai proves that there is an equivalence of stacks </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqn22" id="eqn22">
<span class="label">(5.10)</span>
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn22.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="263" height="23" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn22.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$ \begin{align} {\mathcal{M}}_{7}^\circ \cong [(\operatorname{\mathrm{Gr}}(7, S^+) \smallsetminus \Delta)/\mathrm{SO}_{10}], \end{align} $$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">where <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline851.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="118" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline851.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Delta \subset \operatorname {\mathrm {Gr}}(7, S^+)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is the closed locus of linear subspaces <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline852.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="78" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline852.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {P}^6 \subset \mathbb {P} S^+$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> whose intersection with <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline853.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="85" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline853.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(5, 10)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is not a smooth curve [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r21"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Mukai</span>21</a>, Section 5].</p>
<p class="p"> The spinor representation of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline854.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="41" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline854.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathrm {SO}_{10}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> corresponds to a rank <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline855.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="18" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline855.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$16$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> vector bundle <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline856.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="23" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline856.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {S}^+$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> on the classifying stack <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline857.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="56" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline857.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {BSO}}_{10}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Then, the equivalence (<a class="xref disp-formula" href="#eqn22">5.10</a>) shows that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline858.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="32" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline858.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_7^\circ $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is an open substack of the Grassmann bundle <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline859.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="80" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline859.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {Gr}}(7, \mathcal {S}^+)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> over <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline860.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="56" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline860.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {BSO}}_{10}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>: </p><div class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqn23" id="eqn23">
<span class="label">(5.11)</span>
<div class="figure-thumb"><img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn23.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image" width="182" height="99" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn23.png" data-zoomable="false"></div>
</div><p class="p continuation">We note that the tautological subbundle <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline861.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="12" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline861.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {E}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> on <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline862.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="80" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline862.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {Gr}}(7, \mathcal {S}^+)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> restricts to the dual of the Hodge bundle on <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline863.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="32" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline863.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_7^\circ $
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. In other words, if <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline864.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="104" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline864.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$f\colon \mathcal {C} \to {\mathcal {M}}_7^{\circ }$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is the universal curve, then <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline865.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="130" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline865.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\alpha _0^*\mathcal {E} = (f_*\omega _f)^\vee $
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. The universal version of the Mukai construction furnishes a map <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline866.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="123" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline866.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {C} \to \operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(5, \mathcal {V})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> over <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline867.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="56" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline867.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {BSO}}_{10}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="sec" data-magellan-destination="sec15" id="sec15">

<h4 class="C"><span class="label">5.3.3</span> The Mukai construction with markings</h4>
<p class="p"> For <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline868.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline868.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n \leq 4$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, we describe <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline869.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline869.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{7,n}^{\circ }$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> in a similar fashion to (<a class="xref disp-formula" href="#eqn23">5.11</a>) but this time as an open substack of a Grassmann bundle over <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline870.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="90" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline870.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(5,\mathcal {V})^n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. To do so, let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline871.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="176" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline871.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\iota \colon \operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(5, \mathcal {V}) \hookrightarrow \mathbb {P} \mathcal {S}^+$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> be the universal spinor embedding, and let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline872.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="141" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline872.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {L} := \iota ^*\mathcal {O}_{\mathbb {P} \mathcal {S}^+}(-1)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. The embedding <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline873.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="6" height="10" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline873.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\iota $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is determined by an inclusion of vector bundles <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline874.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="94" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline874.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {L} \hookrightarrow \pi ^*\mathcal {S}^+$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> on <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline875.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="78" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline875.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(5, \mathcal {V})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. On the <em class="italic">n</em>-fold fiber product <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline876.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="90" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline876.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(5, \mathcal {V})^n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline877.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="19" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline877.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {L}_i$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline878.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="19" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline878.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {U}_i$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> denote the pullbacks of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline879.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="14" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline879.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {L}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline880.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="16" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline880.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {U}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, respectively, from the <em class="italic">i</em>th factor. Let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline881.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="219" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline881.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\pi _n \colon \operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(5, \mathcal {V})^n \to \operatorname {\mathrm {BSO}}_{10}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> be the structure map. Consider the sum of the inclusions </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqn24" id="eqn24">
<span class="label">(5.12)</span>
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn24.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="152" height="57" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn24.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$ \begin{align} \bigoplus_{i=1}^n \mathcal{L}_i \xrightarrow{\phi_n} \pi_n^* \mathcal{S}^+. \end{align} $$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">Let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline882.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="138" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline882.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$Z_n \subset \operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(5,\mathcal {V})^n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> be the open substack where <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline883.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="21" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline883.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\phi _n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> has rank <em class="italic">n</em>. In other words, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline884.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="21" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline884.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$Z_n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is the locus where the <em class="italic">n</em> points on <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline885.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="78" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline885.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(5, \mathcal {V})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> have independent image under the spinor embedding.</p>
<p class="p"> Let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline886.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="24" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline886.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {Q}_n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> be the cokernel of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline887.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="44" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline887.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\phi _n|_{Z_n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, which is a rank <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline888.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="51" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline888.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$16 - n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> vector bundle on <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline889.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="21" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline889.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$Z_n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. The fiber of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline890.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="116" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline890.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {Gr}}(7 - n, \mathcal {Q}_n)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> over <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline891.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="218" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline891.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$(p_1, \ldots , p_n) \in \operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(5, \mathcal {V})^n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> parametrizes linear spaces <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline892.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="78" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline892.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {P}^6 \subset \mathbb {P} S^+$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> that contain the <em class="italic">n</em> points <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline893.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="18" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline893.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$p_i$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Thus, we can identify <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline894.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="116" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline894.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {Gr}}(7-n,\mathcal {Q}_n)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> with the locally closed substack </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqn25" id="eqn25">
<span class="label">(5.13)</span>
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn25.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="668" height="23" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn25.png" data-zoomable="true">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$ \begin{align} \left\{(p_1, \ldots, p_n, \Lambda) : p_i \in \mathbb{P} \Lambda \text{ and}\ p_i\ \text{independent} \right\} \subset \operatorname{\mathrm{OG}}(5, \mathcal{V})^n \times_{\operatorname{\mathrm{BSO}}_{10}} \operatorname{\mathrm{Gr}}(7, \mathcal{S}^+). \end{align} $$
</span></span>
</span>
</div>
<div class="statement lemma" data-magellan-destination="lemma13" id="lemma13">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Lemma 5.13.</span> For <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline895.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline895.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n \leq 4$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, there is an open embedding <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline896.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="22" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline896.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\alpha _n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline897.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline897.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{7,n}^\circ $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> in the Grassmann bundle </p><div class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU57" id="eqnU57">
<div class="figure-thumb"><img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu57.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image" width="397" height="102" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu57.png" data-zoomable="false"></div>
</div><p class="p continuation">Hence, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline898.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline898.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{7,n}^{\circ }$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> has the CKgP.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement other" data-magellan-destination="proof18" id="proof18">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Proof.</span> Let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline899.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="119" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline899.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$f\colon \mathcal {C} \to {\mathcal {M}}_{7,n}^{\circ }$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> be the universal curve, and let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline900.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="126" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline900.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\sigma _i\colon {\mathcal {M}}_{7,n}^{\circ } \to \mathcal {C}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> be the <em class="italic">i</em>th section. The universal version of the Mukai construction gives a morphism <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline901.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="123" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline901.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {C} \to \operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(5, \mathcal {V})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Precomposing with each of the sections <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline902.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="18" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline902.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\sigma _i$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> defines a map <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline903.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="170" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline903.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{7, n}^{\circ } \to \operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(5,\mathcal {V})^n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> over <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline904.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="56" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline904.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {BSO}}_{10}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. We claim that, for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline905.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline905.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n \leq 4$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, the images of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline906.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="90" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline906.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\sigma _1, \ldots , \sigma _n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> must be independent. Indeed, suppose the images of the sections in a fiber, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline907.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="128" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline907.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$p_1, \ldots , p_n \in C$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, are dependent under the canonical embedding. Then <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline908.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="110" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline908.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$p_1 + \cdots + p_n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> would give a <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline909.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="20" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline909.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g^1_n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> on <em class="italic">C</em>, but curves in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline910.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline910.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{7,n}^{\circ }$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> have no <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline911.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="20" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline911.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g^1_n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline912.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline912.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n \leq 4$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> by definition.</p>
<p class="p"> We also have the map <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline913.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="227" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline913.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{7,n}^{\circ } \to {\mathcal {M}}_7^\circ \to \operatorname {\mathrm {Gr}}(7, \mathcal {S}^+)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> that sends a curve to its span under the spinor embedding. Taking the product of these maps over <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline914.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="56" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline914.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {BSO}}_{10}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> yields a map </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU58" id="eqnU58">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu58.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="323" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu58.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}{\mathcal{M}}_{7,n}^\circ \to \operatorname{\mathrm{OG}}(5, \mathcal{V})^n \times_{\operatorname{\mathrm{BSO}}_{10}} \operatorname{\mathrm{Gr}}(7, \mathcal{S}^+).\end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">This map sends a family of pointed curves <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline915.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="126" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline915.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$(C, p_1, \ldots , p_n)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> over a scheme <em class="italic">T</em> to the data of sections <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline916.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="221" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline916.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$p_i\colon T \to C \to \operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(5, W^\vee )$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and the subbundle of the spinor representation of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline917.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="28" height="17" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline917.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W^\vee $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> determined by the span of the fibers of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline918.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="193" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline918.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$C \subset \operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(5, W^\vee ) \subset \mathbb {P} S^+$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> over <em class="italic">T</em>. The map evidently factors through the locally closed locus in (<a class="xref disp-formula" href="#eqn25">5.13</a>), which we identified with <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline919.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="116" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline919.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {Gr}}(7 - n, \mathcal {Q}_n)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. In fact, the image is precisely <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline920.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="150" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline920.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {Gr}}(7 - n, \mathcal {Q}_n) \smallsetminus \Delta $
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, where <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline921.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="13" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline921.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Delta $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is the closed locus, such that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline922.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="142" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline922.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {P} \Lambda \cap \operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(5, W^\vee )$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is not a family of smooth curves. Indeed, on the complement of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline923.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="13" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline923.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Delta $
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, an inverse map <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline924.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="232" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline924.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {Gr}}(7 - n, \mathcal {Q}_n) \smallsetminus \Delta \to {\mathcal {M}}_{7,n}^{\circ }$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is defined by sending <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline925.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="126" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline925.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$(p_1, \ldots , p_n, \Lambda )$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> to the curve <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline926.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="180" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline926.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$C = \mathbb {P} \Lambda \cap \operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(5, W^\vee )$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> together with the sections <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline927.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="227" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline927.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$p_i \in \mathbb {P} \Lambda \cap \operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(5, W^\vee ) = C$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
<p class="p"> By Corollary <a class="xref statement" href="#corollary6">5.11</a>, we know <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline928.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="90" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline928.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(5, \mathcal {V})^n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> has the CKgP. To complete the proof, apply Proposition <a class="xref statement" href="#proposition5">4.2</a>(1) and (<a class="xref sec" href="#sec9">5</a>).</p>
</div>
<p class="p"> We now identify the restrictions of the universal bundles on <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline929.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="90" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline929.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(5, \mathcal {V})^n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline930.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="116" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline930.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {Gr}}(7 - n, \mathcal {Q}_n)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> to <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline931.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline931.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{7,n}^{\circ }$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> along <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline932.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="22" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline932.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\alpha _n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p><div class="statement lemma" data-magellan-destination="lemma14" id="lemma14">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Lemma 5.14.</span> Let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline933.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="119" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline933.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$f\colon \mathcal {C} \to {\mathcal {M}}_{7,n}^{\circ }$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> be the universal curve, and let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline934.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="18" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline934.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\sigma _i$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> denote the image of the <em class="italic">i</em>th section. The vector bundle <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline935.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="44" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline935.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\alpha _n^*\, \mathcal {U}_i$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> sits in an exact sequence </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqn26" id="eqn26">
<span class="label">(5.14)</span>
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn26.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="513" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn26.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$ \begin{align} 0 \rightarrow \alpha_n^* \, \mathcal{U}_i \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathrm{Sym}}^2 f_*(\omega_f(-\sigma_i)) \rightarrow f_*((\omega_f(-\sigma_i))^{\otimes 2}) \rightarrow 0. \end{align} $$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">In particular, all classes pulled back from <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline936.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="90" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline936.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(5, \mathcal {V})^n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> to <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline937.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline937.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{7,n}^\circ $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> are tautological.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement other" data-magellan-destination="proof19" id="proof19">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Proof.</span> The composition of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline938.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="22" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline938.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\alpha _n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> with projection onto the <em class="italic">i</em>th factor of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline939.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="21" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline939.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$Z_n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is the map that sends a pointed curve <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline940.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="126" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline940.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$(C, p_1, \ldots , p_n)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> to the image of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline941.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="18" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline941.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$p_i$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> under the canonical map from <em class="italic">C</em> to <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline942.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="206" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline942.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(5, W^\vee ) \cong \operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(5, 10)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. By construction, the fiber at <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline943.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="18" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline943.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$p_i$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> of the universal rank <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline944.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="9" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline944.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$5$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> bundle on <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline945.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="85" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline945.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(5,10)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline946.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="29" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline946.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_p^\perp $
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Equation (<a class="xref disp-formula" href="#eqn26">5.14</a>) is the relative version of (<a class="xref disp-formula" href="#eqn21">5.9</a>). By Grothendieck–Riemann–Roch, the middle and right terms in (<a class="xref disp-formula" href="#eqn26">5.14</a>) have tautological Chern classes. It follows that the Chern classes of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline947.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="41" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline947.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\alpha _n^*\mathcal {U}_i$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> are also tautological. The last claim now follows from Corollary <a class="xref statement" href="#corollary6">5.11</a>.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement lemma" data-magellan-destination="lemma15" id="lemma15">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Lemma 5.15.</span> We have <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline948.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="134" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline948.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$c_1(\alpha _n^*\mathcal {L}_i) = -\psi _i$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline949.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="85" height="28" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline949.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$A^1({\mathcal {M}}_{7,n}^{\circ })$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement other" data-magellan-destination="proof20" id="proof20">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Proof.</span> Let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline950.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="119" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline950.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$f\colon \mathcal {C} \to {\mathcal {M}}_{7,n}^{\circ }$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> be the universal curve. The line bundle <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline951.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="40" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline951.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\alpha ^*\mathcal {L}_i$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is the pullback of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline952.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="82" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline952.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {O}_{\mathbb {P} \mathcal {S}^+}(-1)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> along the composition </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU59" id="eqnU59">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu59.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="284" height="30" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu59.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}{\mathcal{M}}_{7,n}^{\circ} \xrightarrow{\sigma_i} \mathcal{C} \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathrm{OG}}(5, \mathcal{V}) \xrightarrow{\iota} \mathbb{P} \mathcal{S}^+.\end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">But the above composition also factors as </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU60" id="eqnU60">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu60.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="317" height="36" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu60.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}{\mathcal{M}}_{7,n}^{\circ} \xrightarrow{\sigma_i} \mathcal{C} \xrightarrow{|\omega_f|} \mathbb{P} (f_* \omega_f)^\vee \to \mathbb{P} \mathcal{S}^+,\end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline953.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="82" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline953.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {O}_{\mathbb {P} \mathcal {S}^+}(-1)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> restricts to <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline954.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="122" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline954.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {O}_{\mathbb {P} (f_* \omega _f)^\vee }(-1)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Hence, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline955.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="42" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline955.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\alpha _n^*\mathcal {L}_i$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline956.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="249" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline956.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\sigma _i^* \mathcal {O}_{\mathbb {P} (f_* \omega _f)^\vee }(-1) = (\sigma _i^*\omega _f)^\vee $
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement lemma" data-magellan-destination="lemma16" id="lemma16">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Lemma 5.16.</span> Let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline957.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="20" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline957.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {E}_n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> be the tautological rank <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline958.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="43" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline958.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$7 - n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> subbundle on <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline959.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="116" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline959.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {Gr}}(7 - n, \mathcal {Q}_n)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. The pullback <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline960.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="43" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline960.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\alpha _n^*\mathcal {E}_n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> sits in an exact sequence </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqn27" id="eqn27">
<span class="label">(5.15)</span>
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn27.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="355" height="57" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn27.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$ \begin{align} 0 \rightarrow \bigoplus_{i=1}^n \alpha_n^*\mathcal{L}_i \rightarrow (f_*\omega_f)^\vee \rightarrow \alpha_n^*\mathcal{E}_n \rightarrow 0. \end{align} $$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">In particular, the Chern classes of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline961.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="43" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline961.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\alpha _n^* \mathcal {E}_n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> are tautological.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement other" data-magellan-destination="proof21" id="proof21">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Proof.</span> Recall that we defined <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline962.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="24" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline962.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {Q}_n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> as the cokernel of (<a class="xref disp-formula" href="#eqn24">5.12</a>). The map onto the second factor in (<a class="xref disp-formula" href="#eqn25">5.13</a>), <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline963.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="263" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline963.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$p\colon \operatorname {\mathrm {Gr}}(7 - n, \mathcal {Q}_n) \to \operatorname {\mathrm {Gr}}(7, \mathcal {S}^+)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, sends a <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline964.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="43" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline964.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$7 - n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> dimensional subspace to its preimage under the quotient map <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline965.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="83" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline965.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {S}^+ \to \mathcal {Q}_n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Hence, there is an exact sequence on <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline966.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="116" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline966.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {Gr}}(7 - n, \mathcal {Q}_n)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU61" id="eqnU61">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu61.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="271" height="57" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu61.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}0 \rightarrow \bigoplus_{i=1}^n \mathcal{L}_i \to p^* \mathcal{E} \to \mathcal{E}_n \rightarrow 0.\end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">Then note that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline967.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="55" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline967.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\alpha _n^*p^*\mathcal {E}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is the same as the pullback of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline968.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="12" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline968.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {E}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> along <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline969.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="227" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline969.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{7,n}^\circ \to {\mathcal {M}}_{7}^\circ \to \operatorname {\mathrm {Gr}}(7, \mathcal {S}^+)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, which is the dual of the Hodge bundle. The last claim follows by combining the exact sequence (<a class="xref disp-formula" href="#eqn27">5.15</a>) with Lemma <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma15">5.15</a>.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement lemma" data-magellan-destination="lemma17" id="lemma17">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Lemma 5.17.</span> The Chow ring of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline970.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline970.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{7,n}^{\circ }$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is generated by tautological classes.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement other" data-magellan-destination="proof22" id="proof22">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Proof.</span> By Lemma <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma13">5.13</a>, we know that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline971.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline971.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{7,n}^\circ $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is an open substack of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline972.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="116" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline972.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {Gr}}(7 - n, \mathcal {Q}_n)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. The Chow ring of the latter is generated by pullbacks of classes from <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline973.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="90" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline973.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {OG}}(5, \mathcal {V})^n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and by the Chern classes of the tautological subbundle <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline974.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="20" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline974.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathcal {E}_n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. By Lemmas <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma14">5.14</a> and <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma16">5.16</a>, respectively, both of these collections of classes restrict to tautological classes on <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline975.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline975.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{7,n}^\circ $
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="sec" data-magellan-destination="sec16" id="sec16">

<h2 class="A"><span class="label">6</span> Applications to even cohomology</h2>
<p class="p"> Here, we use the results from Sections <a class="xref sec" href="#sec7">3</a>, <a class="xref sec" href="#sec8">4</a> and <a class="xref sec" href="#sec9">5</a> to prove Theorem <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem3">1.5</a>.</p>
<div class="sec" data-magellan-destination="sec17" id="sec17">

<h3 class="B"><span class="label">6.1</span> The degree 4 cohomology of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline976.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="49" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline976.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is tautological</h3>
<p class="p"> 
</p><div class="statement other" data-magellan-destination="sta3" id="sta3">
<h2 class="C">Proof of Theorem <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem3">1.5</a>(1).</h2>
<p class="p"> By [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r1"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Arbarello and Cornalba</span>1</a>], we know that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline977.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="91" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline977.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^k({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is tautological for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline978.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="46" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline978.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$k \leq 3$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Therefore, using Theorem <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem2">1.3</a>, we deduce that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline979.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="89" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline979.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^4({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is contained in the STE generated by <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline980.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="99" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline980.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^4({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g',n'})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline981.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="53" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline981.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g' &lt; 7$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline982.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="53" height="17" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline982.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n' \leq 4$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. By Proposition <a class="xref statement" href="#proposition6">4.5</a>, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline983.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="124" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline983.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_4H^4({\mathcal {M}}_{g',n'})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is tautological for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline984.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="17" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline984.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g'$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline985.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="16" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline985.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n'$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> in this range, and it follows that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline986.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="90" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline986.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^4({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is tautological.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement other" data-magellan-destination="sta4" id="sta4">
<h2 class="C">Proof of Theorem <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem3">1.5</a>(2).</h2>
<p class="p"> By Theorem <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem3">1.5</a>(1) and [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r1"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Arbarello and Cornalba</span>1</a>], all classes in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline987.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="89" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline987.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^6({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> that are pushed forward from the boundary are tautological. Also, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline988.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="90" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline988.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^6({\mathcal {M}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is stable and hence tautological for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline989.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="58" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline989.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g \geq 10$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r35"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Wahl</span>35</a>]. It follows that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline990.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="90" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline990.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^6({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is tautological for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline991.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="58" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline991.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g \geq 10$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement remark" data-magellan-destination="remark7" id="remark7">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Remark 6.1.</span> By Lemma <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma2">3.1</a>, to show that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline992.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="90" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline992.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^6({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is tautological for all <em class="italic">g</em> and <em class="italic">n</em>, it would suffice to show this for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline993.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline993.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g\leq 9$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline994.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="17" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline994.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n\leq 6$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. In principle, this can be checked computationally as follows. By Theorem <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem3">1.5</a>(3), we know that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline995.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="88" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline995.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H_6({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is tautological for all <em class="italic">g</em> and <em class="italic">n</em>. Thus, if the intersection pairing </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU62" id="eqnU62">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu62.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="280" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu62.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}RH^6({\overline{\mathcal{M}}}_{g,n})\times RH_6({\overline{\mathcal{M}}}_{g,n})\rightarrow \mathbb{Q} \end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">is perfect for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline996.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline996.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g\leq 9$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline997.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="17" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline997.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n\leq 6$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, then <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline998.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="89" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline998.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^6({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is tautological. In principle, one could compute this pairing using the Sage package admcycles [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r11"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Delecroix, Schmitt and van Zelm</span>11</a>]. In practice, however, this computation is too memory intensive to carry out.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="sec" data-magellan-destination="sec18" id="sec18">

<h3 class="B"><span class="label">6.2</span> The low degree even homology of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline999.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="49" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline999.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is tautological</h3>
<p class="p"> Let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1000.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="44" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1000.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H_k^{BM}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> denote Borel–Moore homology with coefficients in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1001.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="15" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1001.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {Q}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> or <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1002.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="23" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1002.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {Q}_{\ell }$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, together with its mixed Hodge structure or Galois action. From the long exact sequence in Borel–Moore homology, we have a right exact sequence </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqn28" id="eqn28">
<span class="label">(6.1)</span>
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn28.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="454" height="28" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn28.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$ \begin{align} H_k(\widetilde{\partial {\mathcal{M}}_{g,n}})\rightarrow H_k({\overline{\mathcal{M}}}_{g,n})\rightarrow W_{-k} H_k^{BM}({\mathcal{M}}_{g,n})\rightarrow 0 \end{align} $$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">for all <em class="italic">k</em>.</p><div class="statement other" data-magellan-destination="sta5" id="sta5">
<h2 class="C">Proof of Theorem <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem3">1.5</a>(3).</h2>
<p class="p"> We now show that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1003.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="90" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1003.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H_k({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is tautological for even <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1004.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="57" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1004.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$k \geq 14$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. For <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1005.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="45" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1005.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g=0$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, we have <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1006.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="216" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1006.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^*({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{0,n}) = RH^*({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{0,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>[<a class="xref bibr" href="#r18"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Keel</span>18</a>]. For <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1007.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="46" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1007.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g \geq 1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, by [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r4"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Bergström, Faber and Payne</span>4</a>, Proposition 2.1] and the duality between <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1008.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="45" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1008.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H_k^{BM}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1009.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="25" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1009.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^k_c$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, we have: </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU63" id="eqnU63">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu63.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="413" height="63" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu63.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$ \begin{align*} H_k^{BM}({\mathcal{M}}_{g,n})=0 \text{ for } \begin{cases} k&lt;2g \text{ and } n=0,1; \\ k&lt;2g-2+n \text{ and } n\geq 2. \end{cases} \end{align*} $$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">Combining this with the exact sequence (<a class="xref disp-formula" href="#eqn28">6.1</a>), we reduce inductively to the finitely many cases <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1010.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="57" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1010.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$k\geq 2g$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1011.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="63" height="17" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1011.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n=0,1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> or <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1012.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="122" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1012.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$k\geq 2g-2+n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1013.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1013.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n\geq 2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. When <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1014.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="46" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1014.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g\geq 3$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, in all of these cases, with <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1015.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="57" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1015.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$k\leq 14$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, we know that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1016.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="49" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1016.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{g,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> has the CKgP and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1017.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="198" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1017.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$A^*({\mathcal {M}}_{g,n})=R^*({\mathcal {M}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> (see Table <a class="xref table" href="#tab1">1</a>). By Proposition <a class="xref statement" href="#proposition6">4.5</a>, it follows that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1018.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="147" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1018.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_{-k}H^{BM}_k({\mathcal {M}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is tautological, so again, by induction and the exact sequence (<a class="xref disp-formula" href="#eqn28">6.1</a>), we reduce to the cases of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1019.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="64" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1019.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g=1,2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. When <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1020.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="44" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1020.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g=1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, all even cohomology is tautological [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r26"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Petersen</span>26</a>]. When <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1021.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="45" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1021.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g=2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, we apply Corollary <a class="xref statement" href="#corollary3">2.7</a>.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement corollary" data-magellan-destination="corollary7" id="corollary7">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Corollary 6.2.</span> As Hodge structures or Galois representations, we have </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU64" id="eqnU64">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu64.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="286" height="32" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu64.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}H^{2d_{g,n}-14}({\overline{\mathcal{M}}}_{g,n})^{\mathrm{ss}}\cong \bigoplus \mathsf{L}^{d_{g,n}-7.} \end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div>
</div>
<div class="statement other" data-magellan-destination="proof23" id="proof23">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Proof.</span> We proved <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1022.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="97" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1022.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H_{14}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is tautological and hence algebraic. Applying Poincaré duality yields the corollary.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="sec" data-magellan-destination="sec19" id="sec19">

<h2 class="A"><span class="label">7</span> The 13th and 15th homology of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1023.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="49" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1023.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>
</h2>
<p class="p"> In this section, we prove Theorems <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem4">1.6</a> and <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem5">1.7</a>. As a corollary, we obtain restrictions on the Hodge structures and Galois representations appearing in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1024.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="97" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1024.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H_{13}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1025.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="96" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1025.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H_{15}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
<div class="sec" data-magellan-destination="sec20" id="sec20">

<h3 class="B"><span class="label">7.1</span> 13th homology</h3>
<p class="p"> As usual, we argue by induction on <em class="italic">g</em> and <em class="italic">n</em>. First, we must treat one extra base case.</p><div class="statement lemma" data-magellan-destination="lemma18" id="lemma18">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Lemma 7.1.</span> The group <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1026.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="102" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1026.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{13}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{2,11})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is in the STE generated by <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1027.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="101" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1027.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{11}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,11})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement other" data-magellan-destination="proof24" id="proof24">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Proof.</span> We showed in [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r8"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Canning, Larson and Payne</span>8</a>] that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1028.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="98" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1028.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{11}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is in the STE generated by <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1029.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="101" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1029.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{11}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,11})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for all <em class="italic">g</em> and <em class="italic">n</em>. Next, we note that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1030.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="53" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1030.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{2,10}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> has the CKgP (see Table <a class="xref table" href="#tab1">1</a>), so <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1031.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="101" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1031.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{13}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{2,10})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> consists of classes pushed forward from the boundary by Proposition <a class="xref statement" href="#proposition6">4.5</a>. In particular, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1032.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="102" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1032.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{13}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{2,10})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> also lies in this STE. The claim then follows from Lemma <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma3">3.2</a>.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement other" data-magellan-destination="sta6" id="sta6">
<h2 class="C">Proof of Theorem <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem4">1.6</a>.</h2>
<p class="p"> The proof is similar to that of Theorem <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem3">1.5</a>(3). When <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1033.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="45" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1033.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g=0$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, all odd cohomology vanishes [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r18"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Keel</span>18</a>], so we can assume <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1034.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="46" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1034.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g\geq 1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. By [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r4"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Bergström, Faber and Payne</span>4</a>, Proposition 2.1] and the duality between <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1035.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="44" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1035.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H_{13}^{BM}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1036.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="32" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1036.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{13}_c$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, we have that for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1037.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="46" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1037.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g\geq 1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU65" id="eqnU65">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu65.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="421" height="63" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu65.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$ \begin{align*} H^{BM}_{13}({\mathcal{M}}_{g,n})=0 \text{ for } \begin{cases} 13&lt;2g \text{ and } n=0,1 \\ 13&lt;2g-2+n \text{ and } n\geq 2. \end{cases} \end{align*} $$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">Combining this with the exact sequence (<a class="xref disp-formula" href="#eqn28">6.1</a>), we reduce inductively to the finitely many cases where <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1038.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="65" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1038.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$13\geq 2g$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1039.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="63" height="17" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1039.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n=0,1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> or <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1040.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="130" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1040.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$13\geq 2g-2+n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1041.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1041.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n\geq 2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. All such cases except for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1042.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="44" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1042.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$(g,n)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1043.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="308" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1043.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$Z = \{ (2,11), (1,11),(1,12),(1,13)\}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> have the CKgP (see Table <a class="xref table" href="#tab1">1</a>). By Proposition <a class="xref statement" href="#proposition6">4.5</a>, it follows that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1044.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="189" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1044.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_{-13}H_{13}^{BM}({\mathcal {M}}_{g,n})=0$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1045.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="82" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1045.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$(g,n) \not \in Z$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. By induction and the exact sequence (<a class="xref disp-formula" href="#eqn28">6.1</a>), we reduce to the exceptional cases of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1046.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="83" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1046.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$(g,n) \in Z$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. The case <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1047.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="124" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1047.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$(g,n)=(2,11)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> follows from Lemma <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma18">7.1</a> and hard Lefschetz. The cases where <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1048.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="44" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1048.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g=1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> follow from Proposition <a class="xref statement" href="#proposition1">2.2</a> and induction on <em class="italic">n</em>.</p>
</div>
<p class="p"> Following the proof strategy above, we obtain the following corollary.</p><div class="statement corollary" data-magellan-destination="corollary8" id="corollary8">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Corollary 7.2.</span> As Hodge structures or Galois representations, we have </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU66" id="eqnU66">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu66.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="318" height="32" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu66.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}H^{2d_{g,n}-13}({\overline{\mathcal{M}}}_{g,n})^{\mathrm{ss}}\cong \bigoplus\mathsf{L}^{d_{g,n}-12}{\mathsf{S}}_{12} \end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">for all <em class="italic">g</em> and <em class="italic">n</em>.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement other" data-magellan-destination="proof25" id="proof25">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Proof.</span> From the proof above, we see that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1049.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="189" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1049.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W_{-13}H_{13}^{BM}({\mathcal {M}}_{g,n})=0$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1050.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="82" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1050.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$(g,n)\notin Z$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, and so </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU67" id="eqnU67">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu67.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="239" height="28" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu67.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}H_{13}(\widetilde{\partial {\mathcal{M}}_{g,n}})\rightarrow H_{13}({\overline{\mathcal{M}}}_{g,n}) \end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">is surjective. Noting that pushforward along a gluing map just induces a Tate twist, by induction on <em class="italic">g</em> and <em class="italic">n</em>, we reduce to the cases <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1051.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="83" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1051.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$(g, n) \in Z$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. The case <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1052.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="124" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1052.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$(g,n)=(2,11)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> follows from Lemma <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma18">7.1</a> and hard Lefschetz. The cases where <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1053.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="44" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1053.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g=1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> follow from Proposition <a class="xref statement" href="#proposition1">2.2</a> and induction on <em class="italic">n</em>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="sec" data-magellan-destination="sec21" id="sec21">

<h3 class="B"><span class="label">7.2</span> 15th homology</h3>
<p class="p"> Again, we will argue by induction on <em class="italic">g</em> and <em class="italic">n</em>. We first need to treat two additional base cases in genus <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1054.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="10" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1054.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. The difficult one is with <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1055.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="18" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1055.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$12$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> markings.</p><div class="statement lemma" data-magellan-destination="lemma19" id="lemma19">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Lemma 7.3.</span> 
<span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1056.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="101" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1056.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{15}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{2,12})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is generated by classes pushed forward from the boundary. Hence, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1057.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="102" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1057.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{15}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{2,12})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is contained in the STE generated by <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1058.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="101" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1058.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{11}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,11})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
</div>
<p class="p"> The proof of Lemma <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma19">7.3</a> involves calculating intersection pairings via decorated graphs. In order to simplify pictures for and language surrounding decorated graphs, we use the following conventions: </p><ol class="list number nomark">
<li class="list-item">

<p class="p"><span class="label">1.</span> A white circle <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1059.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="8" height="9" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1059.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\circ $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is a vertex of genus <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1060.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="7" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1060.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span></p>
</li>
<li class="list-item">

<p class="p"><span class="label">2.</span> A black circle <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1061.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="8" height="9" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1061.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\bullet $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is a vertex of genus <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1062.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="10" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1062.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$0$
</span></span>
</span>
</span></p>
</li>
<li class="list-item">

<p class="p"><span class="label">3.</span> All markings that are not drawn elsewhere are understood to be on the leftmost genus <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1063.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="7" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1063.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> vertex</p>
</li>
<li class="list-item">

<p class="p"><span class="label">4.</span> The decoration <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1064.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="20" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1064.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\omega _i$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> on a genus <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1065.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="7" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1065.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> vertex is shorthand for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1066.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="34" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1066.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$f_i^*\omega $
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, where <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1067.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="168" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1067.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$f_i\colon {\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,12} \to {\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,11}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> forgets the <em class="italic">i</em>th marking and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1068.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="140" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1068.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\omega \in H^{11}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,11})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Similarly, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1069.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="27" height="17" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1069.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\omega _{ij}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is shorthand for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1070.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="37" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1070.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$f_{ij}^*\omega $
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, where <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1071.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="175" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1071.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$f_{ij} \colon {\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,13} \to {\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,11}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> forgets the <em class="italic">i</em>th and <em class="italic">j</em>th markings.</p>
</li>
<li class="list-item">

<p class="p"><span class="label">5.</span> As we vary the decoration <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1072.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="14" height="11" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1072.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\omega $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> over <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1073.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="158" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1073.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{11}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,11}) \cong {\mathsf {S}}_{12}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, pushforward along a map that glues <em class="italic">e</em> pairs of marked points determines a morphism <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1074.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="201" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1074.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathsf {L}^e {\mathsf {S}}_{12} \to H^{11+2e}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. We say that a collection of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1075.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="14" height="11" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1075.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\omega $
</span></span>
</span>
</span>-decorated graphs “is a basis for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1076.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="91" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1076.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^k({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>” if the corresponding morphisms <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1077.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="171" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1077.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathsf {L}^e {\mathsf {S}}_{12} \to H^{k}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> form a basis for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1078.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="207" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1078.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\operatorname {\mathrm {Hom}}(\mathsf {L}^e{\mathsf {S}}_{12}, H^{k}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n}))$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and we have <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1079.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="400" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1079.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^k({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n}) \cong \operatorname {\mathrm {Hom}}(\mathsf {L}^e{\mathsf {S}}_{12}, H^{k}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})) \otimes \mathsf {L}^e {\mathsf {S}}_{12}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p class="p"> Bergström and Faber’s implementation [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r2"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Bergström</span>2</a>] of the Getzler–Kapranov formula in genus <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1080.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="10" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1080.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> shows that, viewed as Galois representations, </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqn29" id="eqn29">
<span class="label">(7.1)</span>
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn29.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="226" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn29.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$ \begin{align} H^{15}({\overline{\mathcal{M}}}_{2,12})^{\mathrm{ss}} = 836 \, {\mathsf{L}}^2{\mathsf{S}}_{12.} \end{align} $$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">In fact, we will produce <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1081.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="30" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1081.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$836$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> independent maps <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1082.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="181" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1082.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathsf {L}}^2{\mathsf {S}}_{12} \to H^{15}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{2,12})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> that arise through pushforward from the boundary. From this, we will conclude that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1083.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="101" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1083.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{15}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{2,12})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is semi-simple and decomposes as a sum of these <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1084.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="30" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1084.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$836$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> copies of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1085.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="46" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1085.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathsf {L}}^2{\mathsf {S}}_{12}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
<p class="p"> As discussed above, an <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1086.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="14" height="11" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1086.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\omega $
</span></span>
</span>
</span>-decorated graph with <em class="italic">e</em> edges represents a morphism <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1087.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="201" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1087.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathsf {L}^e {\mathsf {S}}_{12} \to H^{11 + 2e}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. In Figure <a class="xref fig" href="#fig2">2</a>, we list <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1088.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="29" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1088.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$891$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> such decorated graphs for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1089.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="101" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1089.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{15}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{2,12})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and record particular Künneth components of their pullbacks to boundary divisors. We then argue that there are <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1090.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="19" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1090.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$55$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> relations among these graphs, which allow us to conclude that there are <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1091.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="30" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1091.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$836$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> independent graphs among them.</p><section><div class="fig-ada" data-magellan-destination="fig2" id="fig2"><div class="caption"><span class="label">Figure 2</span>
<p class="p">Selected Künneth components of pullbacks of the <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1092.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="29" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1092.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$891$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> classes to boundary divisors. In the chart, each row represents several rows of a block matrix. The number of rows in each group is listed to its left. The two half-edges glued to make a boundary divisor (pictured across the top) are labeled <em class="italic">q</em> on the left vertex and <em class="italic">p</em> on the right vertex.</p>
</div>


<div class="figure-thumb"><img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_fig2.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image" width="1417" height="1431" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_fig2.png" data-zoomable="true"></div>
</div></section>
<p class="p"> Before proving Lemma <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma19">7.3</a>, we require some explicit bases for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1093.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="97" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1093.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{13}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for small <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1094.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="30" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1094.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g, n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Recall that Getzler [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r16"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Getzler</span>16</a>] showed that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1095.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="202" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1095.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{13}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,n})^{\mathrm {ss}} = \bigoplus \mathsf {L}{\mathsf {S}}_{12}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for all <em class="italic">n</em>.</p><div class="statement lemma" data-magellan-destination="lemma20" id="lemma20">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Lemma 7.4.</span> The following <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1096.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="38" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1096.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$11\ \omega $
</span></span>
</span>
</span>-decorated graphs form a basis for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1097.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="101" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1097.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{13}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,12})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> </p><div class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU68" id="eqnU68">
<div class="figure-thumb"><img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu68.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image" width="103" height="53" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu68.png" data-zoomable="false"></div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="statement other" data-magellan-destination="proof26" id="proof26">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Proof.</span> Consider the block diagonal pairing against the basis for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1098.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="101" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1098.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{11}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,12})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> given by the set of genus <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1099.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="7" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1099.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> vertices decorated by <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1100.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="99" height="13" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1100.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\omega _2, \ldots , \omega _{12}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement lemma" data-magellan-destination="lemma21" id="lemma21">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Lemma 7.5.</span> The following <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1101.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="50" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1101.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$429\ \omega $
</span></span>
</span>
</span>-decorated graphs form a basis for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1102.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="101" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1102.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{13}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,13})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> </p><div class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU69" id="eqnU69">
<div class="figure-thumb"><img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu69.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image" width="513" height="127" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu69.png" data-zoomable="false"></div>
</div><p class="p continuation">Above, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1103.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="30" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1103.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$x, y$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> are any two markings. In the last group of classes, <em class="italic">i</em> or <em class="italic">j</em> can be equal to <em class="italic">y</em>.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement other" data-magellan-destination="proof27" id="proof27">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Proof.</span> Getzler [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r16"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Getzler</span>16</a>] proved that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1104.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="214" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1104.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{13}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,13})^{\mathrm {ss}} = 429 \, \mathsf {L}{\mathsf {S}}_{12}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, so it suffices to show that the images of these maps span. We know that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1105.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="101" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1105.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{13}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,13})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is pushed forward from the boundary by Proposition <a class="xref statement" href="#proposition1">2.2</a>. Modulo classes of the first kind, the second two kinds are pulled back from <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1106.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="102" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1106.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{13}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,12})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Pulling back the relations from <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1107.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="101" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1107.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{13}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,12})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, we can ensure that a fixed marking, such as <em class="italic">y</em> in the first case or <em class="italic">x</em> in the next case, is on the genus <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1108.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="10" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1108.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$0$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> vertex.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement lemma" data-magellan-destination="lemma22" id="lemma22">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Lemma 7.6.</span> Let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1109.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="132" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1109.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\{x, y, 1, \ldots , 12\}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> be a set of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1110.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="18" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1110.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$14$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> markings. The following <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1111.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="70" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1111.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$6,006\ \omega $
</span></span>
</span>
</span>-decorated graphs form a basis for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1112.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="102" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1112.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{13}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,14})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> </p><div class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU70" id="eqnU70">
<div class="figure-thumb"><img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu70.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image" width="712" height="126" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu70.png" data-zoomable="true"></div>
</div><p class="p continuation">In the last grouping above, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1113.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="24" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1113.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$i, j$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> or <em class="italic">k</em> can equal <em class="italic">y</em>.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement other" data-magellan-destination="proof28" id="proof28">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Proof.</span> Getzler [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r16"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Getzler</span>16</a>] proved that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1114.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="223" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1114.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{13}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,14})^{\mathrm {ss}}=6006\,\mathsf {L}{\mathsf {S}}_{12}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, so it suffices to show that the images of these maps span. Modulo classes of the first and second kinds above, the last three kinds are pulled back from <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1115.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="54" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1115.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,12}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Thus, using the relations on <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1116.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="101" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1116.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{13}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,12})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, we can ensure that a fixed marking among those <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1117.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="18" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1117.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$12$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is on the genus <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1118.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="10" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1118.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$0$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> vertex.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement lemma" data-magellan-destination="lemma23" id="lemma23">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Lemma 7.7.</span> The following <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1119.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="50" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1119.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$264\ \omega $
</span></span>
</span>
</span>-decorated graphs form a basis for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1120.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="101" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1120.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{13}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{2,12})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> </p><div class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU71" id="eqnU71">
<div class="figure-thumb"><img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu71.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image" width="509" height="108" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu71.png" data-zoomable="false"></div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="statement other" data-magellan-destination="proof29" id="proof29">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Proof.</span> Bergström and Faber’s implementation [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r2"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Bergström</span>2</a>] of the Getzler–Kapranov formula in genus <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1121.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="10" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1121.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> shows that, as Galois representations, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1122.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="214" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1122.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{13}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{2,12})^{\mathrm {ss}} = 264 \, \mathsf {L}{\mathsf {S}}_{12}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Thus, it suffices to show that the above <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1123.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="31" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1123.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$264$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> maps are independent. We verify this by computing their pullbacks to <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1124.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="102" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1124.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{13}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,14})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and using Lemma <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma22">7.6</a> to see that those maps are independent. Indeed, the pullback is given by the graph that replaces the rightmost genus <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1125.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="7" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1125.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> vertex with a genus <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1126.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="10" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1126.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$0$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> vertex and adds two markings labeled <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1127.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="30" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1127.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$x, y$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> to that vertex.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement remark" data-magellan-destination="remark8" id="remark8">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Remark 7.8.</span> Theorem <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem4">1.6</a> says that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1128.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="97" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1128.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H_{13}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is contained in the STE generated by <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1129.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="101" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1129.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{11}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,11})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Thus, it has a graphical presentation in which the generators are graphs of the sort appearing in Lemmas <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma20">7.4</a>–<a class="xref statement" href="#lemma23">7.7</a>. In forthcoming work, we will show that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1130.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="98" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1130.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{13}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is also contained in this STE. There, we take a more systematic approach and provide a complete list of relations among the corresponding decorated graph generators.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement other" data-magellan-destination="sta7" id="sta7">
<h2 class="C">Proof of Lemma <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma19">7.3</a>.</h2>
<p class="p"> Figure <a class="xref fig" href="#fig2">2</a> represents a matrix with <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1131.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="29" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1131.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$891$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> rows. We first show that the matrix has rank <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1132.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="29" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1132.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$825$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and describe the <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1133.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="20" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1133.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$66$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> relations among the rows.</p>
<p class="p"> First, notice that the rows in A1 are the only rows with nonzero entries in the first column. Next, rows in A2, A3 and A4 have entries in column 2 that are independent from the other entries that appear in that column for later rows (by Lemma <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma21">7.5</a>). This shows that the rows in A1 through A4 are independent and independent from the remaining five rows. Meanwhile, the bottom four rows are block upper triangular. This shows that the rank of the matrix is at least <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1134.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="29" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1134.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$825$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
<p class="p"> Meanwhile, it is not hard to check that the following <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1135.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="20" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1135.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$66$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> relations exist among the rows: </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU72" id="eqnU72">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu72.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="547" height="42" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu72.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}R_1(ij) + \frac{1}{24}R_2(ij) + R_3[i,j] + R_3[j,i] - R_4(ij) + \frac{1}{12} R_5(ij) = 0.\end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">To verify these relations, one needs to make use of known relations among tautological classes in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1136.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="86" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1136.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^4({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,3})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1137.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="87" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1137.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^2({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,2})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1138.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="86" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1138.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^2({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,1})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
<p class="p"> Now, let </p><div class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU73" id="eqnU73">
<div class="figure-thumb"><img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu73.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image" width="686" height="72" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu73.png" data-zoomable="true"></div>
</div><p class="p continuation">We claim <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1139.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="67" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1139.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$M_{ij} \neq 0$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. To see this, consider the intersection of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1140.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="31" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1140.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$M_{ij}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> with <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1141.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="55" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1141.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$R_5(ik)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1142.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="45" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1142.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$k \neq j$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. The intersection of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1143.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="55" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1143.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$R_5(ik)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> with the first five terms in the above equation vanish, since there is no <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1144.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="31" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1144.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{11}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> on a genus <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1145.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="7" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1145.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> vertex with less than <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1146.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="17" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1146.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$11$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> markings. Meanwhile, the intersection <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1147.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="125" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1147.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$R_5(ij) \cdot R_5(ik)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is nonzero using the usual rules for intersecting decorated graphs, as in [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r17"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Graber and Pandharipande</span>17</a>]. To see this, one should take the <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1148.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="14" height="11" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1148.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\omega $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> decoration on the <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1149.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="51" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1149.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,11}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> vertex in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1150.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="53" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1150.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$R_5(ij)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> to be dual to the decoration used on the <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1151.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="51" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1151.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,11}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> vertex in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1152.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="55" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1152.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$R_5(ik)$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
<p class="p"> Finally, the <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1153.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="27" height="17" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1153.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {S}_{12}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> action on the symbols <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1154.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="31" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1154.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$M_{ij}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1155.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="229" height="32" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1155.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathrm {Ind}_{\mathbb {S}_{10}}^{\mathbb {S}_{12}}(V_{1^{10}}) = V_{2,1^{10}} \oplus V_{3,1^9}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, which is a sum of irreducible representations of dimension <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1156.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="17" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1156.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$11$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1157.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="19" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1157.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$55$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. It follows that there are either <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1158.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="17" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1158.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$11$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> or <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1159.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="19" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1159.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$55$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> relations among the <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1160.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="31" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1160.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$M_{ij}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. There cannot be only <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1161.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="17" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1161.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$11$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> relations among the <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1162.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="31" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1162.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$M_{ij}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> because then there would be more than <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1163.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="30" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1163.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$836$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> independent copies of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1164.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="46" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1164.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathsf {L}}^2{\mathsf {S}}_{12}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1165.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="101" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1165.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{15}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{2,12})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, violating the dimension count (<a class="xref disp-formula" href="#eqn29">7.1</a>). Hence, there must be exactly <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1166.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="19" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1166.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$55$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> relations among the <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1167.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="31" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1167.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$M_{ij}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. This shows that the <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1168.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="29" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1168.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$891$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> copies of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1169.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="46" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1169.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathsf {L}}^2{\mathsf {S}}_{12}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> listed on the left of the table generate an <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1170.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="30" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1170.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$836$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>-dimensional space, so they span all of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1171.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="101" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1171.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{15}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{2,12})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement remark" data-magellan-destination="remark9" id="remark9">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Remark 7.9.</span> One could instead prove that the <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1172.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="29" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1172.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$891$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> classes span a space of rank <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1173.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="30" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1173.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$836$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> by computing the pairing of this space against itself. By the argument above, the pairing must have rank <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1174.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="30" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1174.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$836$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
</div>
<p class="p"> Finally, applying Lemma <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma3">3.2</a>(a) together with Lemmas <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma19">7.3</a> and <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma23">7.7</a>, and Corollary <a class="xref statement" href="#corollary2">2.3</a>, we obtain one more base case.</p><div class="statement lemma" data-magellan-destination="lemma24" id="lemma24">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Lemma 7.10.</span> 
<span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1175.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="101" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1175.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{15}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{2,13})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> lies in the STE generated by <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1176.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="102" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1176.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{11}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,11})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement other" data-magellan-destination="sta8" id="sta8">
<h2 class="C">Proof of Theorem <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem5">1.7</a>.</h2>
<p class="p"> The proof is similar to that of Theorem <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem4">1.6</a>. When <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1177.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="45" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1177.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g=0$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, all odd cohomology vanishes [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r18"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Keel</span>18</a>], so we can assume <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1178.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="46" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1178.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g\geq 1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. By [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r4"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Bergström, Faber and Payne</span>4</a>, Proposition 2.1] and the duality between <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1179.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="44" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1179.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H_{15}^{BM}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1180.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="32" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1180.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{15}_c$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, we have that for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1181.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="46" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1181.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g\geq 1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU74" id="eqnU74">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu74.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="421" height="63" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu74.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$ \begin{align*} H^{BM}_{15}({\mathcal{M}}_{g,n})=0 \text{ for } \begin{cases} 15&lt;2g \text{ and } n=0,1 \\ 15&lt;2g-2+n \text{ and } n\geq 2. \end{cases} \end{align*} $$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">Combining this with the exact sequence (<a class="xref disp-formula" href="#eqn28">6.1</a>), we reduce inductively to the finitely many cases <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1182.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="65" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1182.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$15\geq 2g$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1183.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="63" height="17" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1183.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n=0,1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> or <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1184.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="130" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1184.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$15\geq 2g-2+n$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1185.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1185.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n\geq 2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. In such cases, when <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1186.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="46" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1186.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g\geq 3$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1187.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="48" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1187.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{g,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> has the CKgP, and so by induction and the exact sequence (<a class="xref disp-formula" href="#eqn28">6.1</a>), we reduce to the cases where <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1188.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="44" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1188.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g=1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1189.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="102" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1189.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$11\leq n \leq 14$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, or <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1190.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="45" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1190.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g=2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1191.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="101" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1191.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$11\leq n\leq 13$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. When <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1192.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="45" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1192.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g=2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1193.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="54" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1193.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$n=11$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, the result follows from hard Lefschetz and Lemma <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma18">7.1</a>. When <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1194.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="45" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1194.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g=2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1195.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="101" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1195.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$12\leq n\leq 13$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, the result follows from Lemmas <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma19">7.3</a> and <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma24">7.10</a>. For <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1196.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="44" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1196.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g = 1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, the claim follows from Proposition <a class="xref statement" href="#proposition1">2.2</a>.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement corollary" data-magellan-destination="corollary9" id="corollary9">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Corollary 7.11.</span> As Hodge structures or Galois representations, we have </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU75" id="eqnU75">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu75.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="475" height="32" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu75.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}H^{2d_{g,n}-15}({\overline{\mathcal{M}}}_{g,n})^{\mathrm{ss}}\cong \bigoplus\mathsf{L}^{d_{g,n}-13}{\mathsf{S}}_{12}\oplus \bigoplus \mathsf{L}^{d_{g,n}-15}{\mathsf{S}}_{16} \end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">for all <em class="italic">g</em> and <em class="italic">n</em>.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement other" data-magellan-destination="proof30" id="proof30">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Proof.</span> The proof is similar to that of Corollary <a class="xref statement" href="#corollary8">7.2</a>, using the additional input that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1197.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="307" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1197.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{15}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,15})^{\mathrm {ss}} \cong {\mathsf {S}}_{16} \oplus 186263\, {\mathsf {L}}^2{\mathsf {S}}_{12}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> by [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r16"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Getzler</span>16</a>, p. 491].</p>
</div>
<p class="p"> We expect that Theorem <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem5">1.7</a> can be improved as follows.</p><div class="statement conjecture" data-magellan-destination="conjecture2" id="conjecture2">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Conjecture 7.12.</span> The STE generated by <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1198.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="102" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1198.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{11}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,11})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> contains <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1199.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="97" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1199.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{15}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1200.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1200.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g \geq 2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
</div>
<p class="p"> The proof of Theorem <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem1">1.1</a> in the next section shows that for <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1201.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1201.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g\geq 2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1202.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="112" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1202.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{15}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})^{\mathrm {ss}}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> contains no copies of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1203.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="27" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1203.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathsf {S}}_{16}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Conjecture <a class="xref statement" href="#conjecture2">7.12</a> is, therefore, equivalent to the assertion that the STE generated by <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1204.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="102" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1204.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{11}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,11})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1205.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="101" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1205.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{15}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,15})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> contains <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1206.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="98" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1206.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{15}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for all <em class="italic">g</em> and <em class="italic">n</em>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="sec" data-magellan-destination="sec22" id="sec22">

<h2 class="A"><span class="label">8</span> Proof of Theorem <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem1">1.1</a>
</h2>
<p class="p"> The first two statements of Theorem <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem1">1.1</a> follow immediately from Corollaries <a class="xref statement" href="#corollary7">6.2</a> and <a class="xref statement" href="#corollary8">7.2</a> by Poincaré duality. From Corollary <a class="xref statement" href="#corollary9">7.11</a>, we can similarly conclude that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1207.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="111" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1207.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{15}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})^{\mathrm {ss}}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is a direct sum of copies of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1208.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="46" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1208.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathsf {L}}^2 {\mathsf {S}}_{12}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1209.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="27" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1209.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathsf {S}}_{16}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. To finish, it suffices to show that when <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1210.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1210.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g\geq 2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, no copies of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1211.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="27" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1211.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathsf {S}}_{16}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> appear.</p><div class="statement lemma" data-magellan-destination="lemma25" id="lemma25">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Lemma 8.1.</span> The STE generated by <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1212.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="102" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1212.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{11}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,11})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> contains <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1213.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="94" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1213.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H_{15}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{2,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> for all <em class="italic">n</em>. Hence, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1214.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="214" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1214.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{15}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{2,n})^{\mathrm {ss}} \cong \bigoplus {\mathsf {L}}^2{\mathsf {S}}_{12}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, as Galois representations or Hodge structures.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement other" data-magellan-destination="proof31" id="proof31">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Proof.</span> When <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1215.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="45" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1215.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g=2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, as Galois representations, there are no copies of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1216.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="27" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1216.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathsf {S}}_{16}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> in <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1217.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="109" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1217.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{15}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{2,n})^{\mathrm {ss}}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> by Corollary <a class="xref statement" href="#corollary4">2.9</a>. This shows that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1218.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="109" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1218.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H_{15}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{2,n})^{\mathrm {ss}}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is a direct sum of copies of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1219.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="91" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1219.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathsf {L}^{d_{2,n} - 13} {\mathsf {S}}_{12}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> in the category of Galois representations. But we know that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1220.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="97" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1220.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H_{15}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> lies in the STE generated by <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1221.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="101" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1221.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{11}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,11})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1222.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="102" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1222.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{15}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,15})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> by Theorem <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem5">1.7</a>. By considering the Galois representations involved, it follows that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1223.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="94" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1223.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H_{15}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{2,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> lies in the STE generated by <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1224.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="102" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1224.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{11}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,11})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. In particular, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1225.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="108" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1225.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H_{15}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{2,n})^{\mathrm {ss}}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is a direct sum of copies of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1226.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="91" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1226.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathsf {L}^{d_{2,n} - 13} {\mathsf {S}}_{12}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, either as Galois representations or Hodge structures. The second statement follows by Poincaré duality.</p>
</div>
<p class="p"> To show there are no copies of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1227.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="27" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1227.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathsf {S}}_{16}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> when <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1228.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="46" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1228.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g\geq 3$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, we will use a similar strategy to that of [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r8"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Canning, Larson and Payne</span>8</a>]. We study the first two maps in the weight <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1229.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="17" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1229.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$15$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> complex: </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqn30" id="eqn30">
<span class="label">(8.1)</span>
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn30.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="675" height="49" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn30.png" data-zoomable="true">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$ \begin{align} H^{15}({\overline{\mathcal{M}}}_{g,n})\xrightarrow{\alpha} \bigoplus_{|E(\Gamma)| = 1} H^{15}({\overline{\mathcal{M}}}_{\Gamma})^{\operatorname{\mathrm{Aut}}(\Gamma)} \rightarrow \bigoplus_{|E(\Gamma)| = 2} (H^{15}\big({\overline{\mathcal{M}}}_{\Gamma}) \otimes \det E(\Gamma)\big)^{\operatorname{\mathrm{Aut}}(\Gamma)}. \end{align} $$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">Here, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1230.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="12" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1230.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Gamma $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is a stable graph of genus <em class="italic">g</em> with <em class="italic">n</em> legs. The first map is the pullback to the normalization of the boundary <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1231.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="61" height="28" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1231.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\widetilde {\partial {\mathcal {M}}_{g,n}}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. The second map is explicitly described in [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r8"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Canning, Larson and Payne</span>8</a>, Section 4.1].</p><div class="statement lemma" data-magellan-destination="lemma26" id="lemma26">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Lemma 8.2.</span> If <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1232.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="46" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1232.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g\geq 3$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, then the pullback map <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1233.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="12" height="11" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1233.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\alpha $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> in (<a class="xref disp-formula" href="#eqn30">8.1</a>) is injective.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement other" data-magellan-destination="proof32" id="proof32">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Proof.</span> The map <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1234.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="12" height="11" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1234.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\alpha $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is injective when <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1235.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="169" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1235.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathrm {gr}^W_{15}H^{15}_c({\mathcal {M}}_{g,n})=0$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. By [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r4"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Bergström, Faber and Payne</span>4</a>, Proposition 2.1], this holds whenever <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1236.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="131" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1236.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$2g-2+n&gt;15$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. When <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1237.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="131" height="20" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1237.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$2g-2+n\leq 15$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1238.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="49" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1238.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
${\mathcal {M}}_{g,n}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> has the CKgP (see Table <a class="xref table" href="#tab1">1</a>). The result follows from Proposition <a class="xref statement" href="#proposition6">4.5</a>.</p>
</div>
<p class="p"> We now assume <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1239.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="46" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1239.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g\geq 3$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, and we study the second map in (<a class="xref disp-formula" href="#eqn30">8.1</a>) as a morphism of Hodge structures. In particular, we consider the <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1240.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="45" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1240.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{15,0}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> part: </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqn31" id="eqn31">
<span class="label">(8.2)</span>
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn31.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="578" height="53" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn31.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$ \begin{align} \bigoplus_{|E(\Gamma)| = 1} H^{15,0}({\overline{\mathcal{M}}}_{\Gamma})^{\operatorname{\mathrm{Aut}}(\Gamma)} \xrightarrow{ \ \beta \ } \bigoplus_{|E(\Gamma)| = 2} \big(H^{15,0}({\overline{\mathcal{M}}}_{\Gamma}) \otimes \det E(\Gamma)\big)^{\operatorname{\mathrm{Aut}}(\Gamma)}. \end{align} $$
</span></span>
</span>
</div>
<p class="p"> By Lemma <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma26">8.2</a>, to prove the theorem in the category of Hodge structures, it suffices to show that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1241.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="13" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1241.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\beta $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> is injective. The domain is a direct sum over graphs with one edge. If <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1242.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="12" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1242.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Gamma $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> has one vertex and a loop, then <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1243.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="300" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1243.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{15,0}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{\Gamma })=H^{15,0}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g-1,n+2})=0$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> by induction on <em class="italic">g</em>. If <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1244.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="12" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1244.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Gamma $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> has two vertices with an edge connecting them, then by the Künneth formula, we have </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU76" id="eqnU76">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu76.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="427" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu76.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}H^{15,0}({\overline{\mathcal{M}}}_{\Gamma})=H^{15,0}({\overline{\mathcal{M}}}_{a,A\cup p})\oplus H^{15,0}({\overline{\mathcal{M}}}_{b,A^c\cup q}). \end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">Assume <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1245.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="48" height="16" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1245.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$a\geq b$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. By induction, the above is nonvanishing only if <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1246.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="43" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1246.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$b=1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1247.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="80" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1247.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$|A^c|\geq 14$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Because <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1248.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="46" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1248.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g\geq 3$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, it follows that <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1249.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="260" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1249.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{15,0}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{\Gamma })=H^{15,0}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,A^c\cup q})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> in this case. Let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1250.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="19" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1250.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Gamma '$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> be the graph obtained from <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1251.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="12" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1251.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Gamma $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> by adding a loop on the genus <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1252.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="43" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1252.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g-1$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> vertex and decreasing the genus accordingly, as in Figure <a class="xref fig" href="#fig3">3</a>. Then <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1253.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="101" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1253.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{15,0}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{\Gamma '})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> has a summand <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1254.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="138" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1254.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{15,0}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,A^c\cup q})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, and the map <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1255.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="232" height="24" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1255.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{15,0}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{\Gamma })\rightarrow H^{15,0}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{\Gamma '})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> injects into that summand. This completes the proof of Theorem <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem1">1.1</a> in the category of Hodge structures.</p><section><div class="fig-ada" data-magellan-destination="fig3" id="fig3"><div class="caption"><span class="label">Figure 3</span>
<p class="p">The graph <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1256.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="12" height="14" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1256.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Gamma $
</span></span>
</span>
</span> on the left and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1257.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="19" height="15" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1257.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\Gamma '$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> on the right.</p>
</div>


<div class="figure-thumb"><img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_fig3.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image" width="955" height="228" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_fig3.png" data-zoomable="true"></div>
</div></section>
<p class="p"> Finally, we explain how to deduce the result in the category of Galois representations from the result in the category of Hodge structures. To do so, we need one more lemma.</p><div class="statement lemma" data-magellan-destination="lemma27" id="lemma27">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Lemma 8.3.</span> Let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1258.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="141" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1258.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$V \subset H^{15}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,15})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> be the subspace of classes pushed forward from the boundary, and let <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1259.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="146" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1259.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W \subset H^{15}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,15})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> be the image of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1260.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="238" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1260.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{15}_c({\mathcal {M}}_{1,15}) \to H^{15}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,15})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. Then there is a direct sum decomposition <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1261.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="184" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1261.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{15}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,15}) = V \oplus W$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, as Hodge structures or as Galois representations. Moreover, we have <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1262.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="73" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1262.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W \cong {\mathsf {S}}_{16}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1263.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="165" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1263.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$V^{\mathrm {ss}} \cong 186263\, {\mathsf {L}}^2{\mathsf {S}}_{12}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="statement other" data-magellan-destination="proof33" id="proof33">

<p class="p"><span class="label">Proof.</span> There is an exact sequence </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU77" id="eqnU77">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu77.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="409" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu77.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}0 \rightarrow V \rightarrow H^{15}({\overline{\mathcal{M}}}_{1,15}) \rightarrow W_{15}H^{15}({\mathcal{M}}_{1,15}) \rightarrow 0.\end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">It thus suffices to show that the composition </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqn32" id="eqn32">
<span class="label">(8.3)</span>
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn32.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="378" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn32.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$ \begin{align} W \to H^{15}({\overline{\mathcal{M}}}_{1,15}) \to W_{15} H^{15}({\mathcal{M}}_{1,15}) \cong {\mathsf{S}}_{16} \end{align} $$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">is an isomorphism. The pairing <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1264.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="277" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1264.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{15}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,15}) \times H^{15}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,15}) \to \mathbb {Q}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> equips <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1265.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="102" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1265.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{15}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,15})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> with a nondegenerate bilinear form, under which the inclusion of <em class="italic">W</em> is dual to the quotient <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1266.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="271" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1266.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{15}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,15}) \to W_{15} H^{15}({\mathcal {M}}_{1,15})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>. To show (<a class="xref disp-formula" href="#eqn32">8.3</a>) is an isomorphism is, therefore, equivalent to showing that the restriction of the pairing to <em class="italic">W</em> with itself is full rank. This becomes clear in the category of Hodge structures: Since <em class="italic">V</em> has type <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1267.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="114" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1267.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{13,2} \oplus H^{2,13}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> and <em class="italic">W</em> has type <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1268.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="113" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1268.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{15,0} \oplus H^{0,15}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, the pairing between <em class="italic">V</em> and <em class="italic">W</em> is trivial, so <em class="italic">W</em> must be full rank on itself. This claim holds at the level of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1269.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="15" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1269.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {Q}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>-vector spaces. Since all the maps above are also maps of Galois representations, we have a direct sum decomposition as Galois representations too.</p>
<p class="p"> The identification of the remainder <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1270.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="163" height="21" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1270.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$V^{\mathrm {ss}} = 186263\, {\mathsf {L}}^2{\mathsf {S}}_{12}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> follows from [<a class="xref bibr" href="#r16"><span class="show-for-sr">Reference Getzler</span>16</a>, p. 491].</p>
</div>
<p class="p"> By Poincaré duality, to prove Theorem <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem1">1.1</a>, it suffices to show that when <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1271.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="47" height="19" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1271.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$g \geq 2$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, there are no copies of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1272.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="93" height="22" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1272.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathsf {L}^{d_{g,n}-15} {\mathsf {S}}_{16}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> in the right-hand side of Corollary <a class="xref statement" href="#corollary9">7.11</a>. The proof of Theorem <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem5">1.7</a> exhibits <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1273.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="145" height="26" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1273.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$H^{2d_{g,n} - 15}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span> as a quotient of a direct sum of the form </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqnU78" id="eqnU78">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu78.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="668" height="32" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu78.png" data-zoomable="true">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$\begin{align*}\bigoplus \mathsf{L}^{d_{g,n}-13} \otimes H^{11}({\overline{\mathcal{M}}}_{1,11})\oplus \bigoplus \mathsf{L}^{d_{g,n}-15} \otimes H^{15}({\overline{\mathcal{M}}}_{1,15}) \twoheadrightarrow H^{2d_{g,n} - 15}({\overline{\mathcal{M}}}_{g,n}), \end{align*}$$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">where the map from each summand on the left is a composition of a forgetful pullback with a gluing pushforward. By Lemma <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma27">8.3</a>, it suffices to show that, for each of these maps, the composition with the inclusion of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1274.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="146" height="25" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1274.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$W \subset H^{15}({\overline {\mathcal {M}}}_{1,15})$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>, </p><div data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="disp-formula" data-magellan-destination="eqn33" id="eqn33">
<span class="label">(8.4)</span>
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn33.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="516" height="27" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn33.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$$ \begin{align} \mathsf{L}^{d_{g,n}-15} \otimes W \rightarrow \mathsf{L}^{d_{g,n}-15} \otimes H^{15}({\overline{\mathcal{M}}}_{1,15}) \to H^{2d_{g,n} - 15}({\overline{\mathcal{M}}}_{g,n}), \end{align} $$
</span></span>
</span>
</div><p class="p continuation">vanishes. When we view (<a class="xref disp-formula" href="#eqn33">8.4</a>) as a map of Hodge structures, we see that it vanishes, since we have already proved Theorem <a class="xref statement" href="#theorem1">1.1</a> in the category of Hodge structures. Thus, (<a class="xref disp-formula" href="#eqn33">8.4</a>) vanishes as a map of <span data-mathjax-status="texmath alt-graphic" class="inline-formula">
<span class="alternatives">
<img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==" data-src="https://static.cambridge.org/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1275.png?pub-status=live" class="aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off" width="15" height="18" data-original-image="/binary/version/id/urn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1275.png" data-zoomable="false">
<span class="mathjax-tex-wrapper" data-mathjax-type="texmath"><span class="tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on">
$\mathbb {Q}$
</span></span>
</span>
</span>-vector spaces, and so also as a map of Galois representations.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="back">
<div class="ack">
<h2 class="A"> Acknowledgements</h2>
<p class="p"> We thank Jonas Bergström, Carel Faber, Rahul Pandharipande, Dan Petersen, Kartik Prasanna, Burt Totaro and Thomas Willwacher for helpful conversations related to this work. We especially thank Dan Petersen for his comments that led to an improved version of Lemma <a class="xref statement" href="#lemma2">3.1</a>. S.C. was supported by a Hermann-Weyl-Instructorship from the Forschungsinstitut für Mathematik at ETH Zürich. This research was partially conducted during the period H.L. served as a Clay Research Fellow and as a guest of the Forschungsinstitut für Mathematik at ETH Zürich. S.P. was supported in part by National Science Foundation grants DMS–2302475 and DMS–2053261.</p>
</div>
<div class="sec coi-statement" data-magellan-destination="sec23" id="sec23">
<h2 class="A"> Competing interests</h2>
<p class="p"> The authors have no competing interest to declare.</p>
</div>

