wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$n \\geq 9$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, these computations are conditional on the assumption that the only \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline130.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"9\" height=\"15\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline130.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\ell $\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E-adic Galois representations appearing are those from the list of Chenevier and Lannes [\u003Ca class=\"xref bibr\" href=\"#r3\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"show-for-sr\"\u003EReference Bergström and Faber\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E3\u003C\u002Fa\u003E]. Theorem \u003Ca class=\"xref statement\" href=\"#theorem6\"\u003E1.9\u003C\u002Fa\u003E unconditionally confirms the calculations of Bergström and Faber for \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline131.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline131.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$n = 9$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline132.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline132.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$10$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E and \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline133.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline133.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$11$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E In order to prove Theorems \u003Ca class=\"xref statement\" href=\"#theorem1\"\u003E1.1\u003C\u002Fa\u003E, \u003Ca class=\"xref statement\" href=\"#theorem3\"\u003E1.5\u003C\u002Fa\u003E(3) and \u003Ca class=\"xref statement\" href=\"#theorem5\"\u003E1.7\u003C\u002Fa\u003E, our inductive arguments require several base cases beyond what was already in the literature. In particular, we prove the following results in genus \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline134.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"10\" height=\"15\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline134.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$7$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, which are also of independent interest.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\"statement theorem\" data-magellan-destination=\"theorem7\" id=\"theorem7\"\u003E\n\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003ETheorem 1.10.\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E For \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline135.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline135.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$n \\leq 3$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, the moduli space \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline136.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"47\" height=\"21\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline136.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n${\\mathcal {M}}_{7,n}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E has the CKgP and \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline137.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"196\" height=\"21\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline137.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$R^*({\\mathcal {M}}_{7,n}) = A^*({\\mathcal {M}}_{7,n})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E Here, \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline138.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline138.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$R^*$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E denotes the subring of the Chow ring \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline139.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline139.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$A^*$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E generated by tautological cycle classes. Previous results proving that \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline140.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"49\" height=\"22\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline140.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n${\\mathcal {M}}_{g,n}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E has the CKgP and \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline141.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"199\" height=\"22\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline141.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$R^*({\\mathcal {M}}_{g,n}) = A^*({\\mathcal {M}}_{g,n})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E for small \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003Eg\u003C\u002Fem\u003E and \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003En\u003C\u002Fem\u003E have primarily relied on corresponding results for Hurwitz spaces with marked points [\u003Ca class=\"xref bibr\" href=\"#r5\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"show-for-sr\"\u003EReference Canning and Larson\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E5\u003C\u002Fa\u003E]. Unfortunately, the numerics for degree \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline142.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"9\" height=\"16\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline142.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$5$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E covers prevented this technique from working with marked points. Here, we take a new approach to the pentagonal locus, using a modification of Mukai’s construction [\u003Ca class=\"xref bibr\" href=\"#r21\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"show-for-sr\"\u003EReference Mukai\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E21\u003C\u002Fa\u003E] that includes markings.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003Cdiv class=\"sec\" data-magellan-destination=\"sec2\" id=\"sec2\"\u003E\n\n\u003Ch2 class=\"A\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003E2\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E Preliminaries\u003C\u002Fh2\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E In this section, we establish notation and terminology that we will use throughout the paper and discuss a few basic examples of STEs. We also recall previously known facts about the cohomology groups of moduli spaces, especially in genus 0, 1 and 2, that will be used in the base cases of our inductive arguments.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003Cdiv class=\"sec\" data-magellan-destination=\"sec3\" id=\"sec3\"\u003E\n\n\u003Ch3 class=\"B\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003E2.1\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E Preliminaries on STEs\u003C\u002Fh3\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E Recall that an STE is, by definition, closed under the tautological operations given by pushing forward from the boundary or pulling back from moduli spaces with fewer marked points. Let \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline143.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"61\" height=\"28\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline143.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\widetilde {\\partial \\mathcal {M}}_{g,n}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E denote the normalization of the boundary. The sequence \u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"disp-formula\" data-magellan-destination=\"eqnU2\" id=\"eqnU2\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu2.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"444\" height=\"28\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu2.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$$\\begin{align*}H^{k-2}(\\widetilde{\\partial \\mathcal{M}}_{g,n}) \\to H^{k}({\\overline{\\mathcal{M}}}_{g,n}) \\to W_k H^k({\\mathcal{M}}_{g,n})\\rightarrow 0\\end{align*}$$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\u003Cp class=\"p continuation\"\u003Eis right exact.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E Let \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline144.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"179\" height=\"22\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline144.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\pi _i \\colon {\\mathcal {M}}_{g,n} \\to {\\mathcal {M}}_{g,n-1}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E be the tautological morphism forgetting the \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003Ei\u003C\u002Fem\u003Eth marking, and let \u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"disp-formula\" data-magellan-destination=\"eqnU3\" id=\"eqnU3\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu3.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"603\" height=\"29\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu3.png\" data-zoomable=\"true\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Phi^k_{g,n} := \\pi_1^*W_kH^k({\\mathcal{M}}_{g,n-1}) + \\cdots + \\pi_n^*W_kH^k({\\mathcal{M}}_{g,n-1}) \\subset W_kH^k({\\mathcal{M}}_{g,n}). \\end{align*}$$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\u003Cp class=\"p continuation\"\u003EThe following lemma is a cohomological analogue of the “filling criteria” in [\u003Ca class=\"xref bibr\" href=\"#r5\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"show-for-sr\"\u003EReference Canning and Larson\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E5\u003C\u002Fa\u003E, Section 4].\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E We consider the partial order in which \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline145.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"129\" height=\"20\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline145.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$(g', n') \\prec (g, n)$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E if \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline146.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"54\" height=\"20\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline146.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$g' \\leq g$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline147.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"145\" height=\"20\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline147.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$2g' + n' \\leq 2g + n$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E and \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline148.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"129\" height=\"20\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline148.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$(g',n') \\neq (g, n)$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. The moduli space \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline149.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"49\" height=\"26\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline149.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n${\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E is stratified according to the topological types of stable curves, and each stratum of the boundary is a finite quotient of a product of moduli spaces \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline150.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"56\" height=\"22\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline150.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n${\\mathcal {M}}_{g',n'}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, such that \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline151.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"129\" height=\"20\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline151.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$(g',n') \\prec (g,n)$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. Recall that we write \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline152.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"150\" height=\"21\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline152.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$d_{g,n} := 3g - 3 + n$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\"statement lemma\" data-magellan-destination=\"lemma1\" id=\"lemma1\"\u003E\n\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003ELemma 2.1.\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E Let \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline153.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline153.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$S^*$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E be an STE, and let \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline154.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"122\" height=\"19\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline154.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$2g - 2 + n&gt; 0$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. If the canonical map \u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"disp-formula\" data-magellan-destination=\"eqn1\" id=\"eqn1\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003E(2.1)\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn1.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"485\" height=\"29\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn1.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$$ \\begin{align} S^{k'}({\\overline{\\mathcal{M}}}_{g',n'}) \\to W_{k'}H^{k'}({\\mathcal{M}}_{g',n'})\u002F \\big(\\Phi^{k'}_{g',n'} + RH^{k'}({\\mathcal{M}}_{g',n'}) \\big) \\end{align} $$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\u003Cp class=\"p continuation\"\u003Eis surjective for \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline155.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"175\" height=\"20\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline155.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$(g',n',k') = (g, n, k)$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E and all \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline156.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline156.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$(g', n', k')$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E satisfying \u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"disp-formula\" data-magellan-destination=\"eqn2\" id=\"eqn2\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003E(2.2)\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn2.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"589\" height=\"24\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn2.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$$ \\begin{align} (g', n') \\prec (g, n), \\qquad 2d_{g',n'} - k' \\leq 2d_{g,n} - k \\qquad \\text{and} \\qquad k' \\leq k-2, \\end{align} $$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\u003Cp class=\"p continuation\"\u003Ethen \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline157.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"203\" height=\"26\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline157.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$S^k({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n}) = H^k({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003Cdiv class=\"statement other\" data-magellan-destination=\"proof1\" id=\"proof1\"\u003E\n\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003EProof.\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E The proof is by induction on \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003Eg\u003C\u002Fem\u003E and \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003En\u003C\u002Fem\u003E. Consider the diagram \u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\"disp-formula\" data-magellan-destination=\"eqn3\" id=\"eqn3\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003E(2.3)\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003Cdiv class=\"figure-thumb\"\u003E\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn3.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image\" width=\"556\" height=\"108\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn3.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E Here, we extend \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline158.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline158.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$S^*$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E to \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline159.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"61\" height=\"28\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline159.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\widetilde {\\partial {\\mathcal {M}}_{g,n}}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E in the natural way, by summing over components, using the Künneth formula, and taking invariants under automorphisms of the dual graph. We claim that \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline160.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"12\" height=\"11\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline160.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\alpha $\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E is an isomorphism. By the Künneth formula, the domain of \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline161.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"12\" height=\"11\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline161.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\alpha $\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E is a sum of tensor products of \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline162.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"85\" height=\"26\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline162.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$S^{\\ell }({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{\\gamma ,\\nu })$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E with \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline163.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline163.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\ell \\leq k - 2$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E and \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline164.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"117\" height=\"20\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline164.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$(\\gamma , \\nu ) \\prec (g,n)$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. Furthermore, by considering dimensions of the cycles involved, we must also have \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline165.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"184\" height=\"21\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline165.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$2d_{\\gamma ,\\nu } - \\ell \\leq 2d_{g,n} - k$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. This is because we must have \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline166.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"254\" height=\"22\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline166.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$k -2- \\ell \\leq 2(d_{g,n} - 1 - d_{\\gamma ,\\nu })$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, so that the degree of the other Künneth component does not exceed its real dimension. Now, suppose we are given \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline167.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"84\" height=\"20\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline167.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$(g',n',k')$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E that satisfy \u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"disp-formula\" data-magellan-destination=\"eqnU4\" id=\"eqnU4\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu4.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"587\" height=\"24\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu4.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$$\\begin{align*}(g', n') \\prec (\\gamma,\\nu), \\qquad 2d_{g',n'} - k' \\leq 2d_{\\gamma,\\nu} - \\ell \\qquad \\text{and} \\qquad k' \\leq \\ell-2.\\end{align*}$$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\u003Cp class=\"p continuation\"\u003EThen \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline168.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"84\" height=\"20\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline168.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$(g',n',k')$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E satisfies (\u003Ca class=\"xref disp-formula\" href=\"#eqn2\"\u003E2.2\u003C\u002Fa\u003E), so \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline169.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"202\" height=\"26\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline169.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$S^{\\ell }({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{\\gamma , \\nu }) = H^\\ell ({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{\\gamma ,\\nu })$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E by induction. This proves the claim.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E Next, by induction, we have \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline170.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"237\" height=\"26\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline170.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^k({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n-1}) = S^k({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n-1})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, so the image of \u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"disp-formula\" data-magellan-destination=\"eqnU5\" id=\"eqnU5\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu5.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"269\" height=\"27\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu5.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$$\\begin{align*}\\pi_i^*\\colon H^k({\\overline{\\mathcal{M}}}_{g,n-1}) \\to H^k({\\overline{\\mathcal{M}}}_{g,n})\\end{align*}$$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\u003Cp class=\"p continuation\"\u003Eis contained in \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline171.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"86\" height=\"26\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline171.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$S^k({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E for all \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003Ei\u003C\u002Fem\u003E. Hence, \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline172.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"39\" height=\"27\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline172.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\Phi ^k_{g,n}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E is contained in the image of \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline173.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"11\" height=\"18\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline173.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\phi $\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. The tautological classes \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline174.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"251\" height=\"25\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline174.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$RH^k({\\mathcal {M}}_{g,n}) \\subseteq W_k H^k({\\mathcal {M}}_{g,n})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E are also contained in the image of \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline175.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"11\" height=\"18\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline175.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\phi $\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E by definition. Thus, the surjectivity of \u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"disp-formula\" data-magellan-destination=\"eqnU6\" id=\"eqnU6\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu6.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"435\" height=\"37\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu6.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$$\\begin{align*}S^k({\\overline{\\mathcal{M}}}_{g,n}) \\to W_kH^k({\\mathcal{M}}_{g,n})\u002F\\left(\\Phi^k_{g,n} + RH^k({\\mathcal{M}}_{g,n})\\right)\\end{align*}$$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\u003Cp class=\"p continuation\"\u003Eimplies that \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline176.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"11\" height=\"18\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline176.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\phi $\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E is surjective. Hence, \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline177.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"13\" height=\"19\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline177.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\beta $\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E is also surjective, as desired.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E In order to apply Lemma \u003Ca class=\"xref statement\" href=\"#lemma1\"\u003E2.1\u003C\u002Fa\u003E, we need results that help us understand generators for \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline178.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"315\" height=\"37\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline178.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$W_kH^k({\\mathcal {M}}_{g,n})\u002F\\left (\\Phi ^k_{g,n} + RH^k({\\mathcal {M}}_{g,n})\\right )$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. This is the topic of Sections \u003Ca class=\"xref sec\" href=\"#sec7\"\u003E3\u003C\u002Fa\u003E and \u003Ca class=\"xref sec\" href=\"#sec8\"\u003E4\u003C\u002Fa\u003E.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003Cdiv class=\"sec\" data-magellan-destination=\"sec4\" id=\"sec4\"\u003E\n\n\u003Ch3 class=\"B\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003E2.2\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E Pure cohomology in genus 1 and 2\u003C\u002Fh3\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E On \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline179.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"47\" height=\"21\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline179.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n${\\mathcal {M}}_{0,n}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, the only nonvanishing pure cohomology is \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline180.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"113\" height=\"24\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline180.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$W_0 H^0({\\mathcal {M}}_{0,n})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. Below, we present the complete classification of pure cohomology in genus \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline181.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"7\" height=\"14\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline181.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$1$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, which is due to Getzler [\u003Ca class=\"xref bibr\" href=\"#r16\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"show-for-sr\"\u003EReference Getzler\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E16\u003C\u002Fa\u003E]. In genus \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline182.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline182.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$2$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, we present a classification in low cohomological degree, following Petersen [\u003Ca class=\"xref bibr\" href=\"#r27\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"show-for-sr\"\u003EReference Petersen\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E27\u003C\u002Fa\u003E].\u003C\u002Fp\u003E \n\u003Cdiv class=\"sec\" data-magellan-destination=\"sec5\" id=\"sec5\"\u003E\n\n\u003Ch4 class=\"C\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003E2.2.1\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E Genus 1\u003C\u002Fh4\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E The following statement appeared in [\u003Ca class=\"xref bibr\" href=\"#r23\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"show-for-sr\"\u003EReference Pandharipande, Zvonkine and Petersen\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E23\u003C\u002Fa\u003E, Proposition 7]; the proof there is omitted. Here, we include the proof (and corrected statement), which was explained to us by Petersen. Let \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline183.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline183.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n${\\mathsf {S}}_{k+1}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E denote the weight \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003Ek\u003C\u002Fem\u003E structure associated to the space of cusp forms of weight \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline184.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline184.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$k+1$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E for \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline185.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"59\" height=\"20\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline185.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\operatorname {\\mathrm {SL}}_2(\\mathbb {Z})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. Let \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline186.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"118\" height=\"21\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline186.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\pi \\colon E \\to {\\mathcal {M}}_{1,1}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E be the universal curve, and let \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline187.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline187.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\mathbb {V}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E be the local system \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline188.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"58\" height=\"22\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline188.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$R^1\\pi _*\\mathbb {Q}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. By the Eichler–Shimura correspondence, we have \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline189.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"238\" height=\"24\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline189.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n${\\mathsf {S}}_{k+1} = W_{k}H^1({\\mathcal {M}}_{1,1}, \\mathbb {V}^{\\otimes {k-1}})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. We will see that the latter is identified with \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline190.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"117\" height=\"24\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline190.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$W_k H^k({\\mathcal {M}}_{1,k})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. More generally, we have the following. Given a partition \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline191.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"11\" height=\"15\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline191.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\lambda $\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E of \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003En\u003C\u002Fem\u003E, let \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline192.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"20\" height=\"18\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline192.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$V_\\lambda $\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E be the associated Specht module representation of \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline193.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline193.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\mathbb {S}_n$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\"statement proposition\" data-magellan-destination=\"proposition1\" id=\"proposition1\"\u003E\n\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003EProposition 2.2.\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E For \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline194.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline194.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$n\\geq k,$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E a basis for \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline195.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"117\" height=\"24\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline195.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$W_kH^k({\\mathcal {M}}_{1,n})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E is given by the \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline196.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"37\" height=\"28\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline196.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\binom {n-1}{k-1}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E pullbacks from \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline197.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"119\" height=\"24\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline197.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$W_kH^k({\\mathcal {M}}_{1,A})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, where \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003EA\u003C\u002Fem\u003E runs over all subsets of \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline198.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"83\" height=\"19\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline198.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\{1,\\ldots ,n\\}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E of size \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003Ek\u003C\u002Fem\u003E, such that \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline199.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline199.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$1 \\in A$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. Consequently, there is an \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline200.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline200.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\mathbb {S}_n$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E-equivariant isomorphism \u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"disp-formula\" data-magellan-destination=\"eqnU7\" id=\"eqnU7\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu7.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"302\" height=\"27\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu7.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$$\\begin{align*}W_k H^k({\\mathcal{M}}_{1,n})\\cong {\\mathsf{S}}_{k+1}\\otimes V_{n-k+1,1^{k-1}}. \\end{align*}$$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\u003Cp class=\"p continuation\"\u003EFor \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline201.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"47\" height=\"15\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline201.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$n&lt;k$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, we have \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline202.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"152\" height=\"24\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline202.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$W_k H^k({\\mathcal {M}}_{1,n})=0$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003Cdiv class=\"statement other\" data-magellan-destination=\"proof2\" id=\"proof2\"\u003E\n\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003EProof.\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E Let \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline203.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"118\" height=\"21\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline203.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\pi \\colon E\\rightarrow {\\mathcal {M}}_{1,1}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E denote the universal elliptic curve, and \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline204.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"123\" height=\"21\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline204.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\sigma \\colon {\\mathcal {M}}_{1,1} \\to E$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E the section. Associated to the open embedding \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline205.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"124\" height=\"24\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline205.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n${\\mathcal {M}}_{1,n}\\hookrightarrow E^{n-1}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, we have a right exact sequence \u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"disp-formula\" data-magellan-destination=\"eqn4\" id=\"eqn4\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003E(2.4)\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn4.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"530\" height=\"32\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn4.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$$ \\begin{align} \\bigoplus W_{k-2}H^{k-2}(E^{n-2})\\rightarrow W_k H^k(E^{n-1})\\rightarrow W_k H^k({\\mathcal{M}}_{1,n})\\rightarrow 0. \\end{align} $$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\u003Cp class=\"p continuation\"\u003ESince \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline206.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"146\" height=\"24\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline206.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$f\\colon E^{n-1}\\rightarrow {\\mathcal {M}}_{1,1}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E is smooth and proper, the Leray spectral sequence degenerates at \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline207.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline207.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$E_2$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, and by [\u003Ca class=\"xref bibr\" href=\"#r12\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"show-for-sr\"\u003EReference Deligne\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E12\u003C\u002Fa\u003E, Proposition 2.16], we have a direct sum decomposition \u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"disp-formula\" data-magellan-destination=\"eqn5\" id=\"eqn5\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003E(2.5)\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn5.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"323\" height=\"49\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn5.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$$ \\begin{align} H^k(E^{n-1}) = \\bigoplus_{p+q = k} H^p({\\mathcal{M}}_{1,1}, R^qf_*\\mathbb{Q}). \\end{align} $$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\u003Cp class=\"p continuation\"\u003EBy the Künneth formula, we have \u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"disp-formula\" data-magellan-destination=\"eqnU8\" id=\"eqnU8\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu8.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"361\" height=\"48\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu8.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$$\\begin{align*}R^qf_*\\mathbb{Q}= \\bigoplus_{i_2 + \\cdots + i_{n} = q}R^{i_2}\\pi_*\\mathbb{Q} \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes R^{i_{n}}\\pi_*\\mathbb{Q}. \\end{align*}$$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\u003Cp class=\"p continuation\"\u003ELet \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline208.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"102\" height=\"22\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline208.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\mathbb {V}:=R^1\\pi _*\\mathbb {Q}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, and note that \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline209.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"97\" height=\"22\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline209.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$R^0\\pi _*\\mathbb {Q} = \\mathbb {Q}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E and \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline210.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"135\" height=\"23\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline210.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$R^2\\pi _*\\mathbb {Q} = \\mathbb {Q}(-1)$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E Fix some \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003Ep\u003C\u002Fem\u003E and \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline211.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"89\" height=\"20\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline211.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$(i_2, \\ldots , i_{n})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E with \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline212.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"165\" height=\"19\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline212.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$p + i_2 + \\cdots + i_{n} = k$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. If \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline213.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"48\" height=\"21\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline213.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$i_j = 2$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, then, we claim that \u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"disp-formula\" data-magellan-destination=\"eqn6\" id=\"eqn6\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003E(2.6)\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn6.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"461\" height=\"26\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn6.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$$ \\begin{align} W_kH^p({\\mathcal{M}}_{1,1}, R^{i_2}\\pi_*\\mathbb{Q} \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes R^{i_{n}}\\pi_*\\mathbb{Q}) \\subset W_kH^k(E^{n-1}) \\end{align} $$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\u003Cp class=\"p continuation\"\u003Elies in the image of the first map in (\u003Ca class=\"xref disp-formula\" href=\"#eqn4\"\u003E2.4\u003C\u002Fa\u003E). More precisely, let \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline214.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"151\" height=\"25\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline214.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\alpha _{j} \\colon E^{n-2} \\rightarrow E^{n-1}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E be the locus where the \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003Ej\u003C\u002Fem\u003Eth entry in \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline215.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"39\" height=\"18\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline215.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$E^{n-1}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E agrees with the section \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline216.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"123\" height=\"21\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline216.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\sigma \\colon {\\mathcal {M}}_{1,1} \\to E$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. In other words, \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline217.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline217.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\alpha _j$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E is defined by the fiber diagram \u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\"disp-formula\" data-magellan-destination=\"eqnU9\" id=\"eqnU9\"\u003E\n\u003Cdiv class=\"figure-thumb\"\u003E\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu9.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image\" width=\"159\" height=\"97\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu9.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E If \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline218.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"52\" height=\"21\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline218.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$i_j = 2,$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E we have \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline219.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"349\" height=\"21\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline219.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$p + i_2 + \\cdots + i_{j-1} + i_{j+1} + \\cdots + i_{n} = k-2$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. Therefore, using the Leray spectral sequence for \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline220.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"118\" height=\"24\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline220.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$E^{n-2} \\to {\\mathcal {M}}_{1,1}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, there is a corresponding term \u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"disp-formula\" data-magellan-destination=\"eqn7\" id=\"eqn7\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003E(2.7)\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn7.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"763\" height=\"26\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn7.png\" data-zoomable=\"true\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$$ \\begin{align} \\begin{aligned} W_{k-2} H^p({\\mathcal{M}}_{1,1}, R^{i_2}\\pi_*\\mathbb{Q} \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes R^{i_{j-1}}\\pi_*\\mathbb{Q} \\otimes R^{i_{j+1}}\\pi_*\\mathbb{Q} \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes R^{i_{n}}\\pi_*\\mathbb{Q}) \\subset W_{k-2} H^{k-2}(E^{n-2}). \\end{aligned} \\end{align} $$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\u003Cp class=\"p continuation\"\u003EThen the pushforward \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline221.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"264\" height=\"25\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline221.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\alpha _{j*}\\colon H^{k-2}(E^{n-2}) \\to H^k(E^{n-1})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E sends the subspace on the left of (\u003Ca class=\"xref disp-formula\" href=\"#eqn7\"\u003E2.7\u003C\u002Fa\u003E) isomorphically onto the subspace on the left of (\u003Ca class=\"xref disp-formula\" href=\"#eqn6\"\u003E2.6\u003C\u002Fa\u003E), which proves the claim.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E It follows that \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline222.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"117\" height=\"24\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline222.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$W_kH^k({\\mathcal {M}}_{1,n})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E is generated by the terms \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline223.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"322\" height=\"23\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline223.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$W_k H^p({\\mathcal {M}}_{1,1}, R^{i_2} \\pi _*\\mathbb {Q} \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes R^{i_{n}}\\pi _*\\mathbb {Q})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E in \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline224.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"111\" height=\"23\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline224.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$W_k H^k(E^{n-1})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, where all \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline225.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"49\" height=\"21\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline225.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$i_j \\leq 1$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. By [\u003Ca class=\"xref bibr\" href=\"#r26\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"show-for-sr\"\u003EReference Petersen\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E26\u003C\u002Fa\u003E, Section 2], we have \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline226.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"198\" height=\"22\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline226.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$W_k H^p({\\mathcal {M}}_{1,1}, \\mathbb {V}^{\\otimes q}) = 0$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E unless \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline227.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"46\" height=\"19\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline227.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$p = 1$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E and \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline228.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"78\" height=\"19\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline228.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$q = k-1$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, in which case \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline229.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"238\" height=\"24\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline229.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$W_k H^1({\\mathcal {M}}_{1,1}, \\mathbb {V}^{\\otimes k-1}) = {\\mathsf {S}}_{k+1}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E by Eichler–Shimura.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E There are \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline230.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"37\" height=\"28\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline230.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\binom {n-1}{k-1}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E terms of the form \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline231.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"149\" height=\"24\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline231.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^1({\\mathcal {M}}_{1,1}, \\mathbb {V}^{\\otimes k-1})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E in (\u003Ca class=\"xref disp-formula\" href=\"#eqn5\"\u003E2.5\u003C\u002Fa\u003E) coming from choosing which \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline232.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline232.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$k-1$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E of the \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline233.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline233.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$n-1$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E indices have \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline234.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"47\" height=\"21\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline234.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$i_j =1$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. Each of these terms is pulled back along the projection map \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline235.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"114\" height=\"18\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline235.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$E^{n-1} \\to E^{k-1}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, which remembers the \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline236.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline236.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$k-1$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E factors for which \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline237.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"47\" height=\"21\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline237.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$i_j = 1$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. Let \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003EA\u003C\u002Fem\u003E be the collection of indices \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003Ej\u003C\u002Fem\u003E, such that \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline238.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"47\" height=\"21\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline238.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$i_j = 1$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E together with \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline239.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"7\" height=\"14\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline239.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$1$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. There is a commutative diagram \u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\"disp-formula\" data-magellan-destination=\"eqnU10\" id=\"eqnU10\"\u003E\n\u003Cdiv class=\"figure-thumb\"\u003E\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu10.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image\" width=\"307\" height=\"101\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu10.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\u003Cp class=\"p continuation\"\u003EIt follows that \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline240.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"117\" height=\"24\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline240.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$W_kH^k({\\mathcal {M}}_{1,n})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E is generated by the pullbacks from \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline241.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"119\" height=\"24\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline241.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$W_kH^k({\\mathcal {M}}_{1,A})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E as \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003EA\u003C\u002Fem\u003E ranges over all subsets of size \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003Ek\u003C\u002Fem\u003E containing \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline242.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"7\" height=\"14\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline242.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$1$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. Finally, we note that there can be no relations among these \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline243.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"37\" height=\"28\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline243.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\binom {n-1}{k-1}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E copies of \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline244.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"238\" height=\"24\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline244.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$W_k H^1({\\mathcal {M}}_{1,1}, \\mathbb {V}^{\\otimes k-1}) = {\\mathsf {S}}_{k+1}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E since the image of the left-hand map of (\u003Ca class=\"xref disp-formula\" href=\"#eqn4\"\u003E2.4\u003C\u002Fa\u003E) lies in the subspace of type \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline245.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"76\" height=\"21\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline245.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\mathsf {L}^i {\\mathsf {S}}_{k+1-2i}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E for \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline246.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"40\" height=\"16\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline246.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$i \\geq 1$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E We have now shown that \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline247.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"220\" height=\"24\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline247.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$W_kH^k({\\mathcal {M}}_{1,n}) = {\\mathsf {S}}_{k+1} \\otimes U$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E for some \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline248.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"37\" height=\"28\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline248.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\binom {n-1}{k-1}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E-dimensional vector space \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003EU\u003C\u002Fem\u003E. From the discussion above, it is not difficult to identify \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003EU\u003C\u002Fem\u003E as an \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline249.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline249.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\mathbb {S}_n$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E-representation. When \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline250.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline250.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$n = k$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, the \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline251.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"20\" height=\"18\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline251.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\mathbb {S}_k$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E action on \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline252.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"117\" height=\"24\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline252.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$W_kH^k({\\mathcal {M}}_{1,k})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E is the sign representation. To identify \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003EU\u003C\u002Fem\u003E for \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline253.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"47\" height=\"15\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline253.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$n&gt; k$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, let \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline254.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline254.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\mathbb {S}_{n-1} \\subset \\mathbb {S}_n$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E be the subgroup that fixes \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline255.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"7\" height=\"14\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline255.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$1$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. Since \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline256.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"117\" height=\"24\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline256.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$W_kH^k({\\mathcal {M}}_{1,n})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E is freely generated by the pullbacks from \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline257.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"119\" height=\"24\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline257.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$W_kH^k({\\mathcal {M}}_{1,A})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E as \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003EA\u003C\u002Fem\u003E runs over subsets of size \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003Ek\u003C\u002Fem\u003E containing \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline258.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"7\" height=\"14\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline258.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$1$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, we have \u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"disp-formula\" data-magellan-destination=\"eqnU11\" id=\"eqnU11\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu11.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"285\" height=\"31\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu11.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{Res}^{\\mathbb{S}_n}_{\\mathbb{S}_{n-1}} U = \\mathrm{Ind}_{\\mathbb{S}_{k-1} \\times \\mathbb{S}_{n-k}}^{\\mathbb{S}_{n-1}}(\\mathrm{sgn}\\boxtimes \\mathbf{1}).\\end{align*}$$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\u003Cp class=\"p continuation\"\u003EBy the Pieri rule, we have \u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"disp-formula\" data-magellan-destination=\"eqn8\" id=\"eqn8\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003E(2.8)\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn8.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"641\" height=\"31\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn8.png\" data-zoomable=\"true\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$$ \\begin{align} \\mathrm{Ind}_{\\mathbb{S}_{k-1} \\times \\mathbb{S}_{n-k}}^{\\mathbb{S}_{n-1}}(\\mathrm{sgn}\\boxtimes \\mathbf{1}) = \\mathrm{Ind}_{\\mathbb{S}_{k-1} \\times \\mathbb{S}_{n-k}}^{\\mathbb{S}_{n-1}}(V_{1^{k-1}} \\boxtimes V_{n-k}) = V_{n-k+1,1^{k-2}} \\oplus V_{n-k,1^{k-1}}.\\end{align} $$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\u003Cp class=\"p continuation\"\u003EBy the branching rule, \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline259.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"88\" height=\"22\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline259.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$V_{n-k+1,1^{k-1}}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E is the unique \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline260.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline260.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\mathbb {S}_n$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E representation whose restriction to \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline261.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline261.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\mathbb {S}_{n-1}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E is the representation in (\u003Ca class=\"xref disp-formula\" href=\"#eqn8\"\u003E2.8\u003C\u002Fa\u003E).\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E Since \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline262.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline262.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n${\\mathsf {S}}_{14} = 0$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, we have the following.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\"statement corollary\" data-magellan-destination=\"corollary2\" id=\"corollary2\"\u003E\n\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003ECorollary 2.3.\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E \n\u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline263.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"96\" height=\"25\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline263.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^{13}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{1,n})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E lies in the STE generated by \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline264.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"101\" height=\"25\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline264.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^{11}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{1,11})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E for all \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003En\u003C\u002Fem\u003E.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E Let \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline265.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"24\" height=\"20\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline265.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$S^*_\\omega $\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E denote the STE generated by \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline266.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"101\" height=\"25\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline266.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^{11}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{1,11})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. Note that \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline267.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"24\" height=\"20\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline267.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$S^*_\\omega $\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E is the STE generated by the class \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline268.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"152\" height=\"25\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline268.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\omega \\in H^{11,0}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{1,11})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E associated to the weight \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline269.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline269.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$12$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E cusp form for \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline270.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"59\" height=\"20\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline270.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\operatorname {\\mathrm {SL}}_2(\\mathbb {Z})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E,that is, it is the smallest STE whose complexification contains \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline271.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"14\" height=\"11\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline271.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\omega $\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. In [\u003Ca class=\"xref bibr\" href=\"#r8\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"show-for-sr\"\u003EReference Canning, Larson and Payne\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E8\u003C\u002Fa\u003E], we showed that \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline272.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"25\" height=\"20\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline272.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$S^*_\\omega $\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E contains \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline273.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"98\" height=\"26\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline273.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^{11}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, and hence \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline274.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"96\" height=\"26\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline274.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H_{11}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, for all \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003Eg\u003C\u002Fem\u003E and \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003En\u003C\u002Fem\u003E. In this paper, we show that it also contains \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline275.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"97\" height=\"26\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline275.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H_{13}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E for all \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003Eg\u003C\u002Fem\u003E and \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003En\u003C\u002Fem\u003E (Theorem \u003Ca class=\"xref statement\" href=\"#theorem4\"\u003E1.6\u003C\u002Fa\u003E). In contrast with the system of tautological rings, an arbitrary STE need not be closed under pushforward along maps forgetting marked points or pullback to the boundary. Nevertheless, we have the following result for \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline276.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"90\" height=\"26\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline276.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$S_{\\omega }^*({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\"statement proposition\" data-magellan-destination=\"proposition2\" id=\"proposition2\"\u003E\n\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003EProposition 2.4.\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E The STE \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline277.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"24\" height=\"20\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline277.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$S_{\\omega }^*$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E is closed under the tautological operations induced by pushforward for forgetting marked points and pullback for gluing marked points.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003Cdiv class=\"statement other\" data-magellan-destination=\"proof3\" id=\"proof3\"\u003E\n\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003EProof.\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E By [\u003Ca class=\"xref bibr\" href=\"#r26\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"show-for-sr\"\u003EReference Petersen\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E26\u003C\u002Fa\u003E], all even cohomology in genus \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline278.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"7\" height=\"14\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline278.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$1$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E is represented by boundary strata. Therefore, any product of two odd degree classes can be written as a sum of boundary strata. It follows that every class in \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline279.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"90\" height=\"26\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline279.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$S_{\\omega }^*({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E can be represented as a linear combination of decorated graphs, all of whose nontautological decorations are \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline280.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline280.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^{11}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E-classes on genus 1 vertices.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E The pushforward of \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline281.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"96\" height=\"25\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline281.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^{11}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{1,n})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E along the maps forgetting marked points is zero. Since the tautological rings are closed under pushforward, it follows that \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline282.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"25\" height=\"20\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline282.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$S_{\\omega }^*$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E is closed under pushforward.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E By [\u003Ca class=\"xref bibr\" href=\"#r8\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"show-for-sr\"\u003EReference Canning, Larson and Payne\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E8\u003C\u002Fa\u003E, Lemma 2.2], the image of \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline283.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"96\" height=\"25\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline283.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^{11}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{1,n})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E under pullback to the boundary lies in \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline284.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"25\" height=\"20\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline284.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$S^*_{\\omega }$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. By the excess intersection formula, and using the fact that \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline285.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline285.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\psi $\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E-classes in genus 1 are boundary classes, it follows that the pullback of any such decorated graph in \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline286.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"25\" height=\"20\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline286.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$S_\\omega ^*$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E to any boundary stratum is a sum of decorated graphs of the same form. In particular, \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline287.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"24\" height=\"20\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline287.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$S_{\\omega }^*$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E is closed under pullback to the boundary, as required.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003Cdiv class=\"statement remark\" data-magellan-destination=\"remark1\" id=\"remark1\"\u003E\n\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003ERemark 2.5.\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E More generally, the Hodge groups \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline288.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"102\" height=\"25\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline288.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^{k,0}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{1,k})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E correspond to the space of cusp forms for \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline289.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"59\" height=\"20\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline289.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\operatorname {\\mathrm {SL}}_2(\\mathbb {Z})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E of weight \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline290.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline290.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$k+1$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. Essentially the same argument shows that the STE generated by any subset of these cusp form spaces is closed under all of the tautological operations.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003Cdiv class=\"sec\" data-magellan-destination=\"sec6\" id=\"sec6\"\u003E\n\n\u003Ch4 class=\"C\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003E2.2.2\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E Genus 2\u003C\u002Fh4\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E Here, we summarize what we need about the pure weight cohomology of \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline291.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"47\" height=\"21\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline291.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n${\\mathcal {M}}_{2,n}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E in low degrees, from [\u003Ca class=\"xref bibr\" href=\"#r28\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"show-for-sr\"\u003EReference Petersen\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E28\u003C\u002Fa\u003E, \u003Ca class=\"xref bibr\" href=\"#r30\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"show-for-sr\"\u003EReference Petersen and Tommasi\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E30\u003C\u002Fa\u003E].\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\"statement proposition\" data-magellan-destination=\"proposition3\" id=\"proposition3\"\u003E\n\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003EProposition 2.6.\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E Let \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline292.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"57\" height=\"16\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline292.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$k\\leq 10$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. Then \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline293.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"269\" height=\"24\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline293.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$W_{2k} H^{2k}({\\mathcal {M}}_{2,n})=RH^{2k}({\\mathcal {M}}_{2,n})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003Cdiv class=\"statement other\" data-magellan-destination=\"proof4\" id=\"proof4\"\u003E\n\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003EProof.\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E When \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline294.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"57\" height=\"15\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline294.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$n&lt;20$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, we have \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline295.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"235\" height=\"25\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline295.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^{2k}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{2,n})=RH^{2k}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{2,n})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E by [\u003Ca class=\"xref bibr\" href=\"#r28\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"show-for-sr\"\u003EReference Petersen\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E28\u003C\u002Fa\u003E, Theorem 3.8]. Hence, \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline296.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"269\" height=\"24\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline296.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$W_{2k} H^{2k}({\\mathcal {M}}_{2,n})=RH^{2k}({\\mathcal {M}}_{2,n})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E by restriction. For \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline297.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline297.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$n=20$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E and \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline298.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"57\" height=\"16\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline298.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$k\\leq 10$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, the same result holds (see [\u003Ca class=\"xref bibr\" href=\"#r28\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"show-for-sr\"\u003EReference Petersen\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E28\u003C\u002Fa\u003E, Remark 3.10]). For \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline299.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"57\" height=\"15\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline299.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$n&gt;20$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E and \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline300.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"57\" height=\"16\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline300.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$k \\leq 10$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, all of \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline301.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"132\" height=\"24\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline301.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$W_{2k} H^{2k}({\\mathcal {M}}_{2,n})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E is pulled back from \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline302.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"136\" height=\"24\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline302.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$W_{2k} H^{2k}({\\mathcal {M}}_{2,m})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E where \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline303.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline303.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$m\\leq 20$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E (see Lemma \u003Ca class=\"xref statement\" href=\"#lemma2\"\u003E3.1\u003C\u002Fa\u003E, below). Because the tautological ring is closed under forgetful pullbacks, the lemma follows.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E Applying Lemma \u003Ca class=\"xref statement\" href=\"#lemma1\"\u003E2.1\u003C\u002Fa\u003E to the STE \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline304.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline304.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$RH^*$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E immediately implies Conjecture \u003Ca class=\"xref statement\" href=\"#conjecture1\"\u003E1.8\u003C\u002Fa\u003E for \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline305.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"45\" height=\"19\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline305.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$g = 2$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\"statement corollary\" data-magellan-destination=\"corollary3\" id=\"corollary3\"\u003E\n\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003ECorollary 2.7.\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E If \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline306.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"57\" height=\"16\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline306.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$k \\leq 10$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, then \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline307.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"235\" height=\"25\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline307.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^{2k}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{2,n}) = RH^{2k}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{2,n})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E for all \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003En\u003C\u002Fem\u003E.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E In odd degrees, there are restrictions on the possible motivic structures coming from the cohomology of local systems on the moduli space of principally polarized abelian surfaces.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\"statement proposition\" data-magellan-destination=\"proposition4\" id=\"proposition4\"\u003E\n\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003EProposition 2.8.\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E In the category of Galois representations, the pure weight cohomology of \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline308.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"47\" height=\"21\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline308.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n${\\mathcal {M}}_{2,n}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E in degrees 13 and 15 is of the form \u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"disp-formula\" data-magellan-destination=\"eqnU12\" id=\"eqnU12\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu12.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"567\" height=\"32\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu12.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$$\\begin{align*}W_{13}H^{13}({\\mathcal{M}}_{2,n})^{\\mathrm{ss}} \\cong \\bigoplus \\mathsf{L}{\\mathsf{S}}_{12} \\ \\ \\mbox{and} \\ \\ W_{15}H^{15}({\\mathcal{M}}_{2,n})^{\\mathrm{ss}} \\cong \\bigoplus {\\mathsf{L}}^2{\\mathsf{S}}_{12}. \\end{align*}$$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003Cdiv class=\"statement other\" data-magellan-destination=\"proof5\" id=\"proof5\"\u003E\n\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003EProof.\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E For every \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003Ek\u003C\u002Fem\u003E, the surjection \u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"disp-formula\" data-magellan-destination=\"eqnU13\" id=\"eqnU13\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu13.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"242\" height=\"26\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu13.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$$\\begin{align*}H^k({\\overline{\\mathcal{M}}}_{2,n})\\rightarrow W_{k} H^k({\\mathcal{M}}_{2,n}) \\end{align*}$$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\u003Cp class=\"p continuation\"\u003Efactors through \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline309.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"117\" height=\"29\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline309.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$W_k H^k({\\mathcal {M}}_{2,n}^{\\operatorname {\\mathrm {ct}}})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. Here, \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline310.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"47\" height=\"27\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline310.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n${\\mathcal {M}}_{2,n}^{\\operatorname {\\mathrm {ct}}}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E is the moduli space of genus \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline311.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline311.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$2$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E curves of compact type with \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003En\u003C\u002Fem\u003E markings. By [\u003Ca class=\"xref bibr\" href=\"#r28\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"show-for-sr\"\u003EReference Petersen\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E28\u003C\u002Fa\u003E, Theorem 2.1(i) and (ii)], \u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"disp-formula\" data-magellan-destination=\"eqnU14\" id=\"eqnU14\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu14.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"487\" height=\"49\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu14.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$$\\begin{align*}H^k({\\mathcal{M}}_{2,n}^{\\operatorname{\\mathrm{ct}}})\\cong \\bigoplus_{p+q=k} H^p({\\mathcal{M}}_{2}^{\\operatorname{\\mathrm{ct}}},A^q)\\oplus H^p(\\operatorname{\\mathrm{Sym}}^2 {\\mathcal{M}}_{1,1}, B^q), \\end{align*}$$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\u003Cp class=\"p continuation\"\u003Ewhere \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline312.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"23\" height=\"14\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline312.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$A^q$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E and \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline313.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"23\" height=\"14\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline313.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$B^q$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E are local systems of weight \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003Eq\u003C\u002Fem\u003E, given by direct sums of Tate twists of symplectic local systems. Moreover, the terms \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline314.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"174\" height=\"25\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline314.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^p(\\operatorname {\\mathrm {Sym}}^2 {\\mathcal {M}}_{1,1},B^q)$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E map to zero under restriction to \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline315.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"90\" height=\"24\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline315.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^k({\\mathcal {M}}_{2,n})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E by [\u003Ca class=\"xref bibr\" href=\"#r28\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"show-for-sr\"\u003EReference Petersen\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E28\u003C\u002Fa\u003E, Lemma 3.3].\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E We now consider the terms \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline316.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"115\" height=\"24\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline316.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^p({\\mathcal {M}}_{2}^{\\operatorname {\\mathrm {ct}}},A^q)$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. Let \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline317.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline317.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\mathbb {V}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E be a Tate twist of a symplectic local system of weight \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003Eq\u003C\u002Fem\u003E on \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline318.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"37\" height=\"24\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline318.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n${\\mathcal {M}}_2^{\\operatorname {\\mathrm {ct}}}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. If \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003Eq\u003C\u002Fem\u003E is odd, then \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline319.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"104\" height=\"24\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline319.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^p({\\mathcal {M}}_{2}^{\\operatorname {\\mathrm {ct}}},\\mathbb {V})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E vanishes because the hyperelliptic involution acts on the fibers of \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline320.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline320.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\mathbb {V}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E by \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline321.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"48\" height=\"20\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline321.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$(-1)^q$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. When \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003Eq\u003C\u002Fem\u003E is even, the possible Galois representations appearing in \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline322.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"119\" height=\"24\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline322.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^p({\\mathcal {M}}_{2}^{\\operatorname {\\mathrm {ct}}},\\mathbb {V})^{\\mathrm {ss}}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E are determined by [\u003Ca class=\"xref bibr\" href=\"#r27\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"show-for-sr\"\u003EReference Petersen\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E27\u003C\u002Fa\u003E, Theorem 2.1]. When \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline323.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"88\" height=\"19\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline323.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$p+q=13$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E (respectively, \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline324.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"97\" height=\"20\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline324.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$p+q=15)$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, the only possibility of pure weight is \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline325.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"37\" height=\"17\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline325.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\mathsf {L}{\\mathsf {S}}_{12}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E (respectively, \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline326.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"53\" height=\"23\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline326.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n${\\mathsf {L}}^2{\\mathsf {S}}_{12})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003Cdiv class=\"statement corollary\" data-magellan-destination=\"corollary4\" id=\"corollary4\"\u003E\n\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003ECorollary 2.9.\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E On \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline327.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"47\" height=\"25\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline327.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n${\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{2,n}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, in the category of Galois representations, we have \u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"disp-formula\" data-magellan-destination=\"eqnU15\" id=\"eqnU15\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu15.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"502\" height=\"32\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu15.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$$\\begin{align*}H^{13}({\\overline{\\mathcal{M}}}_{2,n})^{\\mathrm{ss}} \\cong \\bigoplus \\mathsf{L}{\\mathsf{S}}_{12} \\ \\ \\mbox{and} \\ \\ H^{15}({\\overline{\\mathcal{M}}}_{2,n})^{\\mathrm{ss}} \\cong \\bigoplus {\\mathsf{L}}^2 {\\mathsf{S}}_{12}. \\end{align*}$$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003Cdiv class=\"statement other\" data-magellan-destination=\"proof6\" id=\"proof6\"\u003E\n\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003EProof.\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E For degree 13, consider the right exact sequence \u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"disp-formula\" data-magellan-destination=\"eqnU16\" id=\"eqnU16\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu16.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"451\" height=\"27\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu16.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$$\\begin{align*}H^{11}(\\widetilde{\\partial {\\mathcal{M}}_{2,n}}) \\rightarrow H^{13}({\\overline{\\mathcal{M}}}_{2,n})\\rightarrow W_{13}H^{13}({\\mathcal{M}}_{2,n})\\rightarrow 0. \\end{align*}$$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\u003Cp class=\"p continuation\"\u003EBy [\u003Ca class=\"xref bibr\" href=\"#r8\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"show-for-sr\"\u003EReference Canning, Larson and Payne\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E8\u003C\u002Fa\u003E], the semi-simplification of the left-hand side is a sum of terms \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline328.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline328.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n${\\mathsf {S}}_{12}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. Proposition \u003Ca class=\"xref statement\" href=\"#proposition4\"\u003E2.8\u003C\u002Fa\u003E shows that the semi-simplification of the right-hand side consists only of Tate twists of \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline329.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline329.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n${\\mathsf {S}}_{12}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. Thus, the semi-simplification of the middle term does, too.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E Similarly, for degree \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline330.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"17\" height=\"16\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline330.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$15$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, we consider the right exact sequence \u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"disp-formula\" data-magellan-destination=\"eqnU17\" id=\"eqnU17\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu17.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"451\" height=\"27\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu17.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$$\\begin{align*}H^{13}(\\widetilde{\\partial {\\mathcal{M}}_{2,n}}) \\rightarrow H^{15}({\\overline{\\mathcal{M}}}_{2,n})\\rightarrow W_{15}H^{15}({\\mathcal{M}}_{2,n})\\rightarrow 0. \\end{align*}$$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\u003Cp class=\"p continuation\"\u003EThe boundary divisors on \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline331.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"48\" height=\"25\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline331.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n${\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{2,n}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E are finite quotients of products of moduli spaces for genus at most \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline332.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline332.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$2$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. In particular, by the Künneth formula and vanishing of odd cohomology in degrees less than or equal to \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline333.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"10\" height=\"15\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline333.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$9$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, we see that the left-hand side is a sum of terms of the form \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline334.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"106\" height=\"26\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline334.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^{13}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{g',n'})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E or \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline335.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"238\" height=\"26\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline335.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^2({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{g_1,n_1}) \\otimes H^{11}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{g_2,n_2})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, where \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline336.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"110\" height=\"20\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline336.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$g', g_1, g_2 \\leq 2$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. By the degree 13 result just proved, the semi-simplification of terms of the first kind is a sum of \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline337.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"37\" height=\"17\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline337.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\mathsf {L}{\\mathsf {S}}_{12}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. Meanwhile, we know \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline338.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"102\" height=\"26\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline338.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^2({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{g_1,n_1})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E is pure Tate by [\u003Ca class=\"xref bibr\" href=\"#r1\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"show-for-sr\"\u003EReference Arbarello and Cornalba\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E1\u003C\u002Fa\u003E] and \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline339.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"124\" height=\"26\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline339.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^{11}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{g_2, n_2})^{\\mathrm {ss}}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E is a sum of terms \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline340.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline340.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n${\\mathsf {S}}_{12}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E by [\u003Ca class=\"xref bibr\" href=\"#r8\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"show-for-sr\"\u003EReference Canning, Larson and Payne\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E8\u003C\u002Fa\u003E]. Hence, the semi-simplification of terms of the second kind is also a sum of \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline341.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"37\" height=\"17\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline341.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\mathsf {L}{\\mathsf {S}}_{12}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. To conclude, note that Proposition \u003Ca class=\"xref statement\" href=\"#proposition4\"\u003E2.8\u003C\u002Fa\u003E shows that the semi-simplification of the right-hand side consists only of Tate twists of \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline342.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline342.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n${\\mathsf {S}}_{12}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, so the semi-simplification of the middle term does too.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003Cdiv class=\"statement remark\" data-magellan-destination=\"remark2\" id=\"remark2\"\u003E\n\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003ERemark 2.10.\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E See Lemma \u003Ca class=\"xref statement\" href=\"#lemma25\"\u003E8.1\u003C\u002Fa\u003E for an analogous result in the category of Hodge structures.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003Cdiv class=\"sec\" data-magellan-destination=\"sec7\" id=\"sec7\"\u003E\n\n\u003Ch2 class=\"A\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003E3\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E Finite generation\u003C\u002Fh2\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E Let \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline343.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline343.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$S^*$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E be an STE. By Lemma \u003Ca class=\"xref statement\" href=\"#lemma1\"\u003E2.1\u003C\u002Fa\u003E, \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline344.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"86\" height=\"26\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline344.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$S^k({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E contains \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline345.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"92\" height=\"26\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline345.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^k({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E for all \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003Eg\u003C\u002Fem\u003E and \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003En\u003C\u002Fem\u003E if and only if it surjects onto \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline346.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"312\" height=\"27\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline346.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$W_kH^k({\\mathcal {M}}_{g,n})\u002F \\big (\\Phi ^k_{g,n} + RH^k({\\mathcal {M}}_{g,n}) \\big )$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E for all \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003Eg\u003C\u002Fem\u003E and \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003En\u003C\u002Fem\u003E. Below we give a sufficient criterion for the vanishing of \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline347.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"174\" height=\"27\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline347.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$W_kH^k({\\mathcal {M}}_{g,n})\u002F \\Phi ^k_{g,n}.$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E The argument is similar to the proof of Proposition \u003Ca class=\"xref statement\" href=\"#proposition1\"\u003E2.2\u003C\u002Fa\u003E, using the Künneth decomposition of the Leray spectral sequence for the \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003En\u003C\u002Fem\u003E-fold fiber product of the universal curve \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline348.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"88\" height=\"22\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline348.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\mathcal {C}^n \\to {\\mathcal {M}}_g$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E We are grateful to Petersen for explaining how an earlier version of this lemma could be strengthened to the version presented here. This stronger version will also be useful for controlling some additional base cases in Section \u003Ca class=\"xref sec\" href=\"#sec19\"\u003E7\u003C\u002Fa\u003E. To state it, we define the subspace \u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"disp-formula\" data-magellan-destination=\"eqnU18\" id=\"eqnU18\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu18.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"417\" height=\"29\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu18.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Psi_{g,n}^k := \\psi_1\\Phi^{k-2}_{g,n} + \\cdots + \\psi_n \\Phi^{k-2}_{g,n} \\subset W_k H^k({\\mathcal{M}}_{g,n}).\\end{align*}$$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\u003Cp class=\"p continuation\"\u003EIn other words, \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline349.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"39\" height=\"27\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline349.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\Psi ^k_{g,n}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E is generated by pullbacks from moduli spaces with fewer markings multiplied with \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline350.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline350.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\psi $\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E-classes. Given a \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003Eg\u003C\u002Fem\u003E-tuple of integers \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline351.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"249\" height=\"22\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline351.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\lambda = (\\lambda _1 \\geq \\lambda _2 \\geq \\cdots \\geq \\lambda _g \\geq 0)$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, let \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline352.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline352.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\mathbb {V}_\\lambda $\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E be the associated symplectic local system on \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline353.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"33\" height=\"22\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline353.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n${\\mathcal {M}}_g$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, as in [\u003Ca class=\"xref bibr\" href=\"#r29\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"show-for-sr\"\u003EReference Petersen, Tavakol and Yin\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E29\u003C\u002Fa\u003E]. Let \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline354.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"150\" height=\"22\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline354.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$|\\lambda | = \\lambda _1 + \\cdots + \\lambda _g$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, which is the weight of the local system \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline355.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline355.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\mathbb {V}_\\lambda $\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. When \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline356.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"55\" height=\"19\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline356.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$|\\lambda | = n$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, as in the previous section, we write \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline357.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"20\" height=\"18\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline357.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$V_{\\lambda }$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E for the irreducible \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline358.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline358.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\mathbb {S}_n$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E representation corresponding to \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline359.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"11\" height=\"15\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline359.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\lambda $\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\"statement lemma\" data-magellan-destination=\"lemma2\" id=\"lemma2\"\u003E\n\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003ELemma 3.1.\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E \n\u003Cspan class=\"roman\"\u003E(a)\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E If \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline360.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"47\" height=\"19\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline360.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$g \\geq 2$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, then \u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"disp-formula\" data-magellan-destination=\"eqnU19\" id=\"eqnU19\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu19.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"532\" height=\"49\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu19.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$$\\begin{align*}W_kH^k({\\mathcal{M}}_{g,n})\u002F(\\Phi_{g,n}^k + \\Psi_{g,n}^k) \\cong \\bigoplus_{|\\lambda| = n} W_k H^{k - n} ({\\mathcal{M}}_g, \\mathbb{V}_{\\lambda}) \\otimes V_{\\lambda^T}.\\end{align*}$$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\u003Cp class=\"p continuation\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"roman\"\u003E(b)\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E Moreover, if \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline361.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline361.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$n&gt; 0$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E and \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline362.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"48\" height=\"16\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline362.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$n \\geq k$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, then \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline363.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"183\" height=\"27\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline363.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$W_kH^k({\\mathcal {M}}_{g,n}) = \\Phi ^k_{g,n}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003Cdiv class=\"statement other\" data-magellan-destination=\"proof7\" id=\"proof7\"\u003E\n\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003EProof.\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E (a) Let \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline364.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"104\" height=\"22\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline364.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\pi \\colon \\mathcal {C} \\to {\\mathcal {M}}_g$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E be the universal curve. There is an open inclusion \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline365.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"97\" height=\"22\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline365.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n${\\mathcal {M}}_{g,n} \\subset \\mathcal {C}^n$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, and hence restriction gives a surjection from \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline366.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"91\" height=\"23\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline366.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$W_kH^k(\\mathcal {C}^n)$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E to \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline367.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"118\" height=\"25\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline367.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$W_kH^k({\\mathcal {M}}_{g,n})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. Given a subset \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline368.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"124\" height=\"19\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline368.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$A \\subset \\{1, \\ldots , n\\}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, let \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline369.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"78\" height=\"19\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline369.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\mathcal {C}^n \\to \\mathcal {C}^A$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E be the projection onto the factors indexed by \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003EA\u003C\u002Fem\u003E. We consider the following three subspaces of \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline370.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"64\" height=\"23\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline370.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^k(\\mathcal {C}^n)$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E:\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E \n\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cul class=\"list nomark\"\u003E\n\u003Cli class=\"list-item\"\u003E\n\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003E•\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E \n\u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCw