\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1192.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"45\" height=\"19\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1192.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$g=2$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E and \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1193.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"54\" height=\"15\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1193.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$n=11$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, the result follows from hard Lefschetz and Lemma \u003Ca class=\"xref statement\" href=\"#lemma18\"\u003E7.1\u003C\u002Fa\u003E. When \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1194.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"45\" height=\"19\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1194.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$g=2$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E and \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1195.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"101\" height=\"16\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1195.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$12\\leq n\\leq 13$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, the result follows from Lemmas \u003Ca class=\"xref statement\" href=\"#lemma19\"\u003E7.3\u003C\u002Fa\u003E and \u003Ca class=\"xref statement\" href=\"#lemma24\"\u003E7.10\u003C\u002Fa\u003E. For \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1196.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"44\" height=\"19\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1196.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$g = 1$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, the claim follows from Proposition \u003Ca class=\"xref statement\" href=\"#proposition1\"\u003E2.2\u003C\u002Fa\u003E.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003Cdiv class=\"statement corollary\" data-magellan-destination=\"corollary9\" id=\"corollary9\"\u003E\n\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003ECorollary 7.11.\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E As Hodge structures or Galois representations, we have \u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"disp-formula\" data-magellan-destination=\"eqnU75\" id=\"eqnU75\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu75.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"475\" height=\"32\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu75.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$$\\begin{align*}H^{2d_{g,n}-15}({\\overline{\\mathcal{M}}}_{g,n})^{\\mathrm{ss}}\\cong \\bigoplus\\mathsf{L}^{d_{g,n}-13}{\\mathsf{S}}_{12}\\oplus \\bigoplus \\mathsf{L}^{d_{g,n}-15}{\\mathsf{S}}_{16} \\end{align*}$$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\u003Cp class=\"p continuation\"\u003Efor all \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003Eg\u003C\u002Fem\u003E and \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003En\u003C\u002Fem\u003E.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003Cdiv class=\"statement other\" data-magellan-destination=\"proof30\" id=\"proof30\"\u003E\n\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003EProof.\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E The proof is similar to that of Corollary \u003Ca class=\"xref statement\" href=\"#corollary8\"\u003E7.2\u003C\u002Fa\u003E, using the additional input that \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1197.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"307\" height=\"25\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1197.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^{15}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{1,15})^{\\mathrm {ss}} \\cong {\\mathsf {S}}_{16} \\oplus 186263\\, {\\mathsf {L}}^2{\\mathsf {S}}_{12}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E by [\u003Ca class=\"xref bibr\" href=\"#r16\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"show-for-sr\"\u003EReference Getzler\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E16\u003C\u002Fa\u003E, p. 491].\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E We expect that Theorem \u003Ca class=\"xref statement\" href=\"#theorem5\"\u003E1.7\u003C\u002Fa\u003E can be improved as follows.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\"statement conjecture\" data-magellan-destination=\"conjecture2\" id=\"conjecture2\"\u003E\n\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003EConjecture 7.12.\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E The STE generated by \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1198.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"102\" height=\"25\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1198.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^{11}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{1,11})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E contains \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1199.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"97\" height=\"26\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1199.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^{15}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E for \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1200.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"47\" height=\"19\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1200.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$g \\geq 2$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E The proof of Theorem \u003Ca class=\"xref statement\" href=\"#theorem1\"\u003E1.1\u003C\u002Fa\u003E in the next section shows that for \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1201.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"47\" height=\"19\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1201.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$g\\geq 2$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1202.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"112\" height=\"26\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1202.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^{15}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})^{\\mathrm {ss}}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E contains no copies of \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1203.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1203.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n${\\mathsf {S}}_{16}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. Conjecture \u003Ca class=\"xref statement\" href=\"#conjecture2\"\u003E7.12\u003C\u002Fa\u003E is, therefore, equivalent to the assertion that the STE generated by \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1204.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"102\" height=\"25\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1204.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^{11}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{1,11})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E and \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1205.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"101\" height=\"25\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1205.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^{15}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{1,15})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E contains \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1206.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"98\" height=\"26\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1206.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^{15}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E for all \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003Eg\u003C\u002Fem\u003E and \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003En\u003C\u002Fem\u003E.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003Cdiv class=\"sec\" data-magellan-destination=\"sec22\" id=\"sec22\"\u003E\n\n\u003Ch2 class=\"A\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003E8\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E Proof of Theorem \u003Ca class=\"xref statement\" href=\"#theorem1\"\u003E1.1\u003C\u002Fa\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fh2\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E The first two statements of Theorem \u003Ca class=\"xref statement\" href=\"#theorem1\"\u003E1.1\u003C\u002Fa\u003E follow immediately from Corollaries \u003Ca class=\"xref statement\" href=\"#corollary7\"\u003E6.2\u003C\u002Fa\u003E and \u003Ca class=\"xref statement\" href=\"#corollary8\"\u003E7.2\u003C\u002Fa\u003E by Poincaré duality. From Corollary \u003Ca class=\"xref statement\" href=\"#corollary9\"\u003E7.11\u003C\u002Fa\u003E, we can similarly conclude that \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1207.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"111\" height=\"26\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1207.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^{15}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})^{\\mathrm {ss}}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E is a direct sum of copies of \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1208.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"46\" height=\"21\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1208.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n${\\mathsf {L}}^2 {\\mathsf {S}}_{12}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E and \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1209.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1209.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n${\\mathsf {S}}_{16}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. To finish, it suffices to show that when \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1210.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"47\" height=\"19\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1210.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$g\\geq 2$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, no copies of \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1211.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1211.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n${\\mathsf {S}}_{16}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E appear.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\"statement lemma\" data-magellan-destination=\"lemma25\" id=\"lemma25\"\u003E\n\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003ELemma 8.1.\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E The STE generated by \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1212.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"102\" height=\"25\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1212.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^{11}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{1,11})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E contains \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1213.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"94\" height=\"25\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1213.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H_{15}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{2,n})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E for all \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003En\u003C\u002Fem\u003E. Hence, \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1214.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"214\" height=\"26\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1214.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^{15}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{2,n})^{\\mathrm {ss}} \\cong \\bigoplus {\\mathsf {L}}^2{\\mathsf {S}}_{12}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, as Galois representations or Hodge structures.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003Cdiv class=\"statement other\" data-magellan-destination=\"proof31\" id=\"proof31\"\u003E\n\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003EProof.\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E When \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1215.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"45\" height=\"19\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1215.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$g=2$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, as Galois representations, there are no copies of \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1216.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1216.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n${\\mathsf {S}}_{16}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E in \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1217.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"109\" height=\"25\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1217.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^{15}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{2,n})^{\\mathrm {ss}}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E by Corollary \u003Ca class=\"xref statement\" href=\"#corollary4\"\u003E2.9\u003C\u002Fa\u003E. This shows that \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1218.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"109\" height=\"25\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1218.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H_{15}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{2,n})^{\\mathrm {ss}}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E is a direct sum of copies of \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1219.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"91\" height=\"21\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1219.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\mathsf {L}^{d_{2,n} - 13} {\\mathsf {S}}_{12}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E in the category of Galois representations. But we know that \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1220.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"97\" height=\"26\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1220.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H_{15}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E lies in the STE generated by \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1221.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"101\" height=\"25\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1221.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^{11}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{1,11})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E and \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1222.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"102\" height=\"25\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1222.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^{15}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{1,15})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E by Theorem \u003Ca class=\"xref statement\" href=\"#theorem5\"\u003E1.7\u003C\u002Fa\u003E. By considering the Galois representations involved, it follows that \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1223.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"94\" height=\"25\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1223.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H_{15}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{2,n})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E lies in the STE generated by \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1224.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"102\" height=\"25\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1224.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^{11}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{1,11})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. In particular, \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1225.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"108\" height=\"25\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1225.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H_{15}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{2,n})^{\\mathrm {ss}}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E is a direct sum of copies of \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1226.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"91\" height=\"21\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1226.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\mathsf {L}^{d_{2,n} - 13} {\\mathsf {S}}_{12}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, either as Galois representations or Hodge structures. The second statement follows by Poincaré duality.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E To show there are no copies of \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1227.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1227.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n${\\mathsf {S}}_{16}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E when \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1228.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"46\" height=\"19\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1228.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$g\\geq 3$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, we will use a similar strategy to that of [\u003Ca class=\"xref bibr\" href=\"#r8\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"show-for-sr\"\u003EReference Canning, Larson and Payne\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E8\u003C\u002Fa\u003E]. We study the first two maps in the weight \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1229.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"17\" height=\"16\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1229.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$15$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E complex: \u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"disp-formula\" data-magellan-destination=\"eqn30\" id=\"eqn30\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003E(8.1)\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn30.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"675\" height=\"49\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn30.png\" data-zoomable=\"true\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$$ \\begin{align} H^{15}({\\overline{\\mathcal{M}}}_{g,n})\\xrightarrow{\\alpha} \\bigoplus_{|E(\\Gamma)| = 1} H^{15}({\\overline{\\mathcal{M}}}_{\\Gamma})^{\\operatorname{\\mathrm{Aut}}(\\Gamma)} \\rightarrow \\bigoplus_{|E(\\Gamma)| = 2} (H^{15}\\big({\\overline{\\mathcal{M}}}_{\\Gamma}) \\otimes \\det E(\\Gamma)\\big)^{\\operatorname{\\mathrm{Aut}}(\\Gamma)}. \\end{align} $$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\u003Cp class=\"p continuation\"\u003EHere, \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1230.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1230.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\Gamma $\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E is a stable graph of genus \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003Eg\u003C\u002Fem\u003E with \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003En\u003C\u002Fem\u003E legs. The first map is the pullback to the normalization of the boundary \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1231.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"61\" height=\"28\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1231.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\widetilde {\\partial {\\mathcal {M}}_{g,n}}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. The second map is explicitly described in [\u003Ca class=\"xref bibr\" href=\"#r8\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"show-for-sr\"\u003EReference Canning, Larson and Payne\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E8\u003C\u002Fa\u003E, Section 4.1].\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\"statement lemma\" data-magellan-destination=\"lemma26\" id=\"lemma26\"\u003E\n\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003ELemma 8.2.\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E If \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1232.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"46\" height=\"19\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1232.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$g\\geq 3$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, then the pullback map \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1233.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"12\" height=\"11\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1233.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\alpha $\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E in (\u003Ca class=\"xref disp-formula\" href=\"#eqn30\"\u003E8.1\u003C\u002Fa\u003E) is injective.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003Cdiv class=\"statement other\" data-magellan-destination=\"proof32\" id=\"proof32\"\u003E\n\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003EProof.\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E The map \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1234.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"12\" height=\"11\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1234.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\alpha $\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E is injective when \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1235.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"169\" height=\"27\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1235.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\mathrm {gr}^W_{15}H^{15}_c({\\mathcal {M}}_{g,n})=0$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. By [\u003Ca class=\"xref bibr\" href=\"#r4\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"show-for-sr\"\u003EReference Bergström, Faber and Payne\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E4\u003C\u002Fa\u003E, Proposition 2.1], this holds whenever \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1236.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"131\" height=\"20\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1236.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$2g-2+n&gt;15$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. When \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1237.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"131\" height=\"20\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1237.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$2g-2+n\\leq 15$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1238.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"49\" height=\"22\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1238.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n${\\mathcal {M}}_{g,n}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E has the CKgP (see Table \u003Ca class=\"xref table\" href=\"#tab1\"\u003E1\u003C\u002Fa\u003E). The result follows from Proposition \u003Ca class=\"xref statement\" href=\"#proposition6\"\u003E4.5\u003C\u002Fa\u003E.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E We now assume \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1239.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"46\" height=\"19\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1239.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$g\\geq 3$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, and we study the second map in (\u003Ca class=\"xref disp-formula\" href=\"#eqn30\"\u003E8.1\u003C\u002Fa\u003E) as a morphism of Hodge structures. In particular, we consider the \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1240.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1240.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^{15,0}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E part: \u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"disp-formula\" data-magellan-destination=\"eqn31\" id=\"eqn31\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003E(8.2)\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn31.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"578\" height=\"53\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn31.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$$ \\begin{align} \\bigoplus_{|E(\\Gamma)| = 1} H^{15,0}({\\overline{\\mathcal{M}}}_{\\Gamma})^{\\operatorname{\\mathrm{Aut}}(\\Gamma)} \\xrightarrow{ \\ \\beta \\ } \\bigoplus_{|E(\\Gamma)| = 2} \\big(H^{15,0}({\\overline{\\mathcal{M}}}_{\\Gamma}) \\otimes \\det E(\\Gamma)\\big)^{\\operatorname{\\mathrm{Aut}}(\\Gamma)}. \\end{align} $$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E By Lemma \u003Ca class=\"xref statement\" href=\"#lemma26\"\u003E8.2\u003C\u002Fa\u003E, to prove the theorem in the category of Hodge structures, it suffices to show that \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1241.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"13\" height=\"19\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1241.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\beta $\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E is injective. The domain is a direct sum over graphs with one edge. If \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1242.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1242.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\Gamma $\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E has one vertex and a loop, then \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1243.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"300\" height=\"26\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1243.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^{15,0}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{\\Gamma })=H^{15,0}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{g-1,n+2})=0$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E by induction on \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003Eg\u003C\u002Fem\u003E. If \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1244.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1244.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\Gamma $\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E has two vertices with an edge connecting them, then by the Künneth formula, we have \u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"disp-formula\" data-magellan-destination=\"eqnU76\" id=\"eqnU76\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu76.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"427\" height=\"26\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu76.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$$\\begin{align*}H^{15,0}({\\overline{\\mathcal{M}}}_{\\Gamma})=H^{15,0}({\\overline{\\mathcal{M}}}_{a,A\\cup p})\\oplus H^{15,0}({\\overline{\\mathcal{M}}}_{b,A^c\\cup q}). \\end{align*}$$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\u003Cp class=\"p continuation\"\u003EAssume \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1245.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"48\" height=\"16\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1245.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$a\\geq b$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. By induction, the above is nonvanishing only if \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1246.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1246.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$b=1$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E and \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1247.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"80\" height=\"19\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1247.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$|A^c|\\geq 14$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. Because \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1248.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"46\" height=\"19\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1248.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$g\\geq 3$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, it follows that \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1249.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"260\" height=\"25\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1249.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^{15,0}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{\\Gamma })=H^{15,0}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{1,A^c\\cup q})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E in this case. Let \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1250.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1250.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\Gamma '$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E be the graph obtained from \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1251.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1251.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\Gamma $\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E by adding a loop on the genus \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1252.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"43\" height=\"19\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1252.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$g-1$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E vertex and decreasing the genus accordingly, as in Figure \u003Ca class=\"xref fig\" href=\"#fig3\"\u003E3\u003C\u002Fa\u003E. Then \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1253.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"101\" height=\"24\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1253.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^{15,0}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{\\Gamma '})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E has a summand \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1254.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"138\" height=\"25\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1254.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^{15,0}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{1,A^c\\cup q})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, and the map \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1255.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"232\" height=\"24\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1255.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^{15,0}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{\\Gamma })\\rightarrow H^{15,0}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{\\Gamma '})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E injects into that summand. This completes the proof of Theorem \u003Ca class=\"xref statement\" href=\"#theorem1\"\u003E1.1\u003C\u002Fa\u003E in the category of Hodge structures.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Csection\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\"fig-ada\" data-magellan-destination=\"fig3\" id=\"fig3\"\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\"caption\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003EFigure 3\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003EThe graph \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1256.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1256.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\Gamma $\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E on the left and \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1257.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1257.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\Gamma '$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E on the right.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\n\n\u003Cdiv class=\"figure-thumb\"\u003E\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_fig3.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image\" width=\"955\" height=\"228\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_fig3.png\" data-zoomable=\"true\"\u003E\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\u003C\u002Fsection\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E Finally, we explain how to deduce the result in the category of Galois representations from the result in the category of Hodge structures. To do so, we need one more lemma.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\"statement lemma\" data-magellan-destination=\"lemma27\" id=\"lemma27\"\u003E\n\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003ELemma 8.3.\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E Let \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1258.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"141\" height=\"25\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1258.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$V \\subset H^{15}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{1,15})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E be the subspace of classes pushed forward from the boundary, and let \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1259.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"146\" height=\"25\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1259.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$W \\subset H^{15}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{1,15})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E be the image of \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1260.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"238\" height=\"25\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1260.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^{15}_c({\\mathcal {M}}_{1,15}) \\to H^{15}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{1,15})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. Then there is a direct sum decomposition \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1261.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"184\" height=\"25\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1261.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^{15}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{1,15}) = V \\oplus W$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, as Hodge structures or as Galois representations. Moreover, we have \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1262.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1262.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$W \\cong {\\mathsf {S}}_{16}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E and \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1263.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"165\" height=\"21\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1263.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$V^{\\mathrm {ss}} \\cong 186263\\, {\\mathsf {L}}^2{\\mathsf {S}}_{12}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003Cdiv class=\"statement other\" data-magellan-destination=\"proof33\" id=\"proof33\"\u003E\n\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003EProof.\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E There is an exact sequence \u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"disp-formula\" data-magellan-destination=\"eqnU77\" id=\"eqnU77\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu77.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"409\" height=\"26\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu77.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$$\\begin{align*}0 \\rightarrow V \\rightarrow H^{15}({\\overline{\\mathcal{M}}}_{1,15}) \\rightarrow W_{15}H^{15}({\\mathcal{M}}_{1,15}) \\rightarrow 0.\\end{align*}$$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\u003Cp class=\"p continuation\"\u003EIt thus suffices to show that the composition \u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"disp-formula\" data-magellan-destination=\"eqn32\" id=\"eqn32\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003E(8.3)\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn32.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"378\" height=\"26\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn32.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$$ \\begin{align} W \\to H^{15}({\\overline{\\mathcal{M}}}_{1,15}) \\to W_{15} H^{15}({\\mathcal{M}}_{1,15}) \\cong {\\mathsf{S}}_{16} \\end{align} $$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\u003Cp class=\"p continuation\"\u003Eis an isomorphism. The pairing \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1264.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"277\" height=\"25\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1264.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^{15}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{1,15}) \\times H^{15}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{1,15}) \\to \\mathbb {Q}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E equips \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1265.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"102\" height=\"25\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1265.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^{15}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{1,15})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E with a nondegenerate bilinear form, under which the inclusion of \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003EW\u003C\u002Fem\u003E is dual to the quotient \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1266.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"271\" height=\"25\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1266.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^{15}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{1,15}) \\to W_{15} H^{15}({\\mathcal {M}}_{1,15})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. To show (\u003Ca class=\"xref disp-formula\" href=\"#eqn32\"\u003E8.3\u003C\u002Fa\u003E) is an isomorphism is, therefore, equivalent to showing that the restriction of the pairing to \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003EW\u003C\u002Fem\u003E with itself is full rank. This becomes clear in the category of Hodge structures: Since \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003EV\u003C\u002Fem\u003E has type \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1267.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"114\" height=\"19\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1267.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^{13,2} \\oplus H^{2,13}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E and \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003EW\u003C\u002Fem\u003E has type \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1268.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"113\" height=\"19\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1268.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^{15,0} \\oplus H^{0,15}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, the pairing between \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003EV\u003C\u002Fem\u003E and \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003EW\u003C\u002Fem\u003E is trivial, so \u003Cem class=\"italic\"\u003EW\u003C\u002Fem\u003E must be full rank on itself. This claim holds at the level of \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1269.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"15\" height=\"18\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1269.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\mathbb {Q}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E-vector spaces. Since all the maps above are also maps of Galois representations, we have a direct sum decomposition as Galois representations too.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E The identification of the remainder \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1270.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"163\" height=\"21\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1270.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$V^{\\mathrm {ss}} = 186263\\, {\\mathsf {L}}^2{\\mathsf {S}}_{12}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E follows from [\u003Ca class=\"xref bibr\" href=\"#r16\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"show-for-sr\"\u003EReference Getzler\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E16\u003C\u002Fa\u003E, p. 491].\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E By Poincaré duality, to prove Theorem \u003Ca class=\"xref statement\" href=\"#theorem1\"\u003E1.1\u003C\u002Fa\u003E, it suffices to show that when \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1271.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"47\" height=\"19\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1271.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$g \\geq 2$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, there are no copies of \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1272.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"93\" height=\"22\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1272.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\mathsf {L}^{d_{g,n}-15} {\\mathsf {S}}_{16}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E in the right-hand side of Corollary \u003Ca class=\"xref statement\" href=\"#corollary9\"\u003E7.11\u003C\u002Fa\u003E. The proof of Theorem \u003Ca class=\"xref statement\" href=\"#theorem5\"\u003E1.7\u003C\u002Fa\u003E exhibits \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1273.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"145\" height=\"26\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1273.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$H^{2d_{g,n} - 15}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E as a quotient of a direct sum of the form \u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"disp-formula\" data-magellan-destination=\"eqnU78\" id=\"eqnU78\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu78.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"668\" height=\"32\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqnu78.png\" data-zoomable=\"true\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$$\\begin{align*}\\bigoplus \\mathsf{L}^{d_{g,n}-13} \\otimes H^{11}({\\overline{\\mathcal{M}}}_{1,11})\\oplus \\bigoplus \\mathsf{L}^{d_{g,n}-15} \\otimes H^{15}({\\overline{\\mathcal{M}}}_{1,15}) \\twoheadrightarrow H^{2d_{g,n} - 15}({\\overline{\\mathcal{M}}}_{g,n}), \\end{align*}$$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\u003Cp class=\"p continuation\"\u003Ewhere the map from each summand on the left is a composition of a forgetful pullback with a gluing pushforward. By Lemma \u003Ca class=\"xref statement\" href=\"#lemma27\"\u003E8.3\u003C\u002Fa\u003E, it suffices to show that, for each of these maps, the composition with the inclusion of \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1274.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"146\" height=\"25\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1274.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$W \\subset H^{15}({\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{1,15})$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, \u003C\u002Fp\u003E\u003Cdiv data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"disp-formula\" data-magellan-destination=\"eqn33\" id=\"eqn33\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"label\"\u003E(8.4)\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn33.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"516\" height=\"27\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_eqn33.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$$ \\begin{align} \\mathsf{L}^{d_{g,n}-15} \\otimes W \\rightarrow \\mathsf{L}^{d_{g,n}-15} \\otimes H^{15}({\\overline{\\mathcal{M}}}_{1,15}) \\to H^{2d_{g,n} - 15}({\\overline{\\mathcal{M}}}_{g,n}), \\end{align} $$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\u003Cp class=\"p continuation\"\u003Evanishes. When we view (\u003Ca class=\"xref disp-formula\" href=\"#eqn33\"\u003E8.4\u003C\u002Fa\u003E) as a map of Hodge structures, we see that it vanishes, since we have already proved Theorem \u003Ca class=\"xref statement\" href=\"#theorem1\"\u003E1.1\u003C\u002Fa\u003E in the category of Hodge structures. Thus, (\u003Ca class=\"xref disp-formula\" href=\"#eqn33\"\u003E8.4\u003C\u002Fa\u003E) vanishes as a map of \u003Cspan data-mathjax-status=\"texmath alt-graphic\" class=\"inline-formula\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\n\u003Cimg src=\"data:image\u002Fgif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAMLCwgAAACH5BAAAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw==\" data-src=\"https:\u002F\u002Fstatic.cambridge.org\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1275.png?pub-status=live\" class=\"aop-lazy-load-image mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" width=\"15\" height=\"18\" data-original-image=\"\u002Fbinary\u002Fversion\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:binary:20241118052945671-0407:S2050508624000246:S2050508624000246_inline1275.png\" data-zoomable=\"false\"\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E\n$\\mathbb {Q}$\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E-vector spaces, and so also as a map of Galois representations.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003Cdiv class=\"back\"\u003E\n\u003Cdiv class=\"ack\"\u003E\n\u003Ch2 class=\"A\"\u003E Acknowledgements\u003C\u002Fh2\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E We thank Jonas Bergström, Carel Faber, Rahul Pandharipande, Dan Petersen, Kartik Prasanna, Burt Totaro and Thomas Willwacher for helpful conversations related to this work. We especially thank Dan Petersen for his comments that led to an improved version of Lemma \u003Ca class=\"xref statement\" href=\"#lemma2\"\u003E3.1\u003C\u002Fa\u003E. S.C. was supported by a Hermann-Weyl-Instructorship from the Forschungsinstitut für Mathematik at ETH Zürich. This research was partially conducted during the period H.L. served as a Clay Research Fellow and as a guest of the Forschungsinstitut für Mathematik at ETH Zürich. S.P. was supported in part by National Science Foundation grants DMS–2302475 and DMS–2053261.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003Cdiv class=\"sec coi-statement\" data-magellan-destination=\"sec23\" id=\"sec23\"\u003E\n\u003Ch2 class=\"A\"\u003E Competing interests\u003C\u002Fh2\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\"p\"\u003E The authors have no competing interest to declare.\u003C\u002Fp\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E\n\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E",tableOfContent:[{level:h,current:a,title:"\u003Cdiv class=\"toc-title\"\u003EIntroduction\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E",url:"sec1"},{level:h,current:a,title:"\u003Cdiv class=\"toc-title\"\u003EPreliminaries\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E",url:"sec2"},{level:h,current:a,title:"\u003Cdiv class=\"toc-title\"\u003EFinite generation\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E",url:"sec7"},{level:h,current:a,title:"\u003Cdiv class=\"toc-title\"\u003EThe Chow–Künneth generation Property\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E",url:"sec8"},{level:h,current:a,title:"\u003Cdiv class=\"toc-title\"\u003EThe CKgP in genus 7 with at most three marked points\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E",url:"sec9"},{level:h,current:a,title:"\u003Cdiv class=\"toc-title\"\u003EApplications to even cohomology\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E",url:"sec16"},{level:h,current:a,title:"\u003Cdiv class=\"toc-title\"\u003EThe 13th and 15th homology of \u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\u003Cimg class=\"inline-graphic mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" data-mimesubtype=\"png\" data-type=\"\" src=\"${staticDomain}\u002Fcontent\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:article:S2050508624000246\u002Fresource\u002Fname\u002FS2050508624000246_inline1023.png?pub-status=live\"\u002F\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E${\\overline {\\mathcal {M}}}_{g,n}$\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E",url:"sec19"},{level:h,current:a,title:"\u003Cdiv class=\"toc-title\"\u003EProof of Theorem \u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E",url:"sec22"},{level:h,current:a,title:"\u003Cdiv class=\"toc-title\"\u003ECompeting interests\u003C\u002Fdiv\u003E",url:"sec23"}],footnotes:[],fulltextNotes:[],references:[{id:"r1",displayNumber:"[1]",existInContent:b,content:"\u003Cspan class=\"string-name\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"surname\"\u003EArbarello\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, \u003Cspan class=\"given-names\"\u003EE.\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E and \u003Cspan class=\"string-name\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"surname\"\u003ECornalba\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, \u003Cspan class=\"given-names\"\u003EM.\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, ‘\u003Cspan class=\"article-title\"\u003ECalculating cohomology groups of moduli spaces of curves via algebraic geometry\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E’, \u003Cspan class=\"source\"\u003EInst. Hautes Études Sci. Publ. Math.\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E (\u003Cspan class=\"volume\"\u003E88\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E) (\u003Cspan class=\"year\"\u003E1998\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E), \u003Cspan class=\"fpage\"\u003E97\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E–\u003Cspan class=\"lpage\"\u003E127\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E. MR 1733327\u003Ca class='ref-link' target='_blank' aria-label='CrossRef link for Calculating cohomology groups of moduli spaces of curves via algebraic geometry' href=https:\u002F\u002Fdx.doi.org\u002F10.1007\u002FBF02701767\u003ECrossRef\u003C\u002Fa\u003E\u003Ca class='ref-link' target='_blank' aria-label='Google Scholar link for Calculating cohomology groups of moduli spaces of curves via algebraic geometry' href=https:\u002F\u002Fscholar.google.com\u002Fscholar_lookup?title=Calculating+cohomology+groups+of+moduli+spaces+of+curves+via+algebraic+geometry&author=Arbarello+E.&author=Cornalba+M.&publication+year=1998&journal=Inst.+Hautes+%C3%89tudes+Sci.+Publ.+Math.&volume=88&doi=10.1007%2FBF02701767&pages=97-127\u003EGoogle Scholar\u003C\u002Fa\u003E",item:[{googleScholarLink:"https:\u002F\u002Fscholar.google.com\u002Fscholar_lookup?title=Calculating+cohomology+groups+of+moduli+spaces+of+curves+via+algebraic+geometry&author=Arbarello+E.&author=Cornalba+M.&publication+year=1998&journal=Inst.+Hautes+%C3%89tudes+Sci.+Publ.+Math.&volume=88&doi=10.1007%2FBF02701767&pages=97-127",openUrlParams:{genre:g,atitle:K,jtitle:l,title:l,volume:"88",artnum:"673ad0ff21c8183ee4e89e50",spage:"97",epage:"127",date:L,sid:e,aulast:c,aufirst:c,doi:M,au:c},innerRefId:"ref1",title:K,doi:M,crossRefLink:"https:\u002F\u002Fdx.doi.org\u002F10.1007\u002FBF02701767",pubMedLink:c}]},{id:"r2",displayNumber:"[2]",existInContent:b,content:"\u003Cspan class=\"string-name\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"surname\"\u003EBergström\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, \u003Cspan class=\"given-names\"\u003EJ.\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, ‘Cohomology of moduli spaces of curves’, (\u003Cspan class=\"year\"\u003E2024\u003C\u002Fs