46\u002Fresource\u002Fname\u002FS2050508624000246_inline440.png?pub-status=live\" \u002F\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E$(g,n)$\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E outside the gray shaded region. Note that this quotient does \u003Cspan class=\"italic\"\u003Enot\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E vanish for \u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\u003Cimg class=\"inline-graphic mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" data-mimesubtype=\"png\" data-type src=\"${staticDomain}\u002Fcontent\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:article:S2050508624000246\u002Fresource\u002Fname\u002FS2050508624000246_inline441.png?pub-status=live\" \u002F\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E$(g,n)$\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E equal to \u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\u003Cimg class=\"inline-graphic mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" data-mimesubtype=\"png\" data-type src=\"${staticDomain}\u002Fcontent\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:article:S2050508624000246\u002Fresource\u002Fname\u002FS2050508624000246_inline442.png?pub-status=live\" \u002F\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E$(1,17)$\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E and \u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\u003Cimg class=\"inline-graphic mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" data-mimesubtype=\"png\" data-type src=\"${staticDomain}\u002Fcontent\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:article:S2050508624000246\u002Fresource\u002Fname\u002FS2050508624000246_inline443.png?pub-status=live\" \u002F\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E$(2,14)$\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, which are pictured by purple dots.\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E",thumbnailSrc:ba,enlargedSrc:ba,attrib:[]},{contentId:"tab1",label:"Table 1",description:"\u003Cspan class=\"p\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\u003Cimg class=\"inline-graphic mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" data-mimesubtype=\"png\" data-type src=\"${staticDomain}\u002Fcontent\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:article:S2050508624000246\u002Fresource\u002Fname\u002FS2050508624000246_inline505.png?pub-status=live\" \u002F\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E${\\mathcal {M}}_{g,n}$\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E has the CKgP and \u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\u003Cimg class=\"inline-graphic mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" data-mimesubtype=\"png\" data-type src=\"${staticDomain}\u002Fcontent\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:article:S2050508624000246\u002Fresource\u002Fname\u002FS2050508624000246_inline506.png?pub-status=live\" \u002F\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E$A^*({\\mathcal {M}}_{g,n})=R^*({\\mathcal {M}}_{g,n})$\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, for \u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\u003Cimg class=\"inline-graphic mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" data-mimesubtype=\"png\" data-type src=\"${staticDomain}\u002Fcontent\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:article:S2050508624000246\u002Fresource\u002Fname\u002FS2050508624000246_inline507.png?pub-status=live\" \u002F\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E$n \\leq c(g)$\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E, by [5, Theorem 1.4] and Theorem 1.10.\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E",thumbnailSrc:bb,enlargedSrc:bb,attrib:[]},{contentId:"fig2",label:"Figure 2",description:"\u003Cspan class=\"p\"\u003ESelected Künneth components of pullbacks of the \u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\u003Cimg class=\"inline-graphic mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" data-mimesubtype=\"png\" data-type src=\"${staticDomain}\u002Fcontent\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:article:S2050508624000246\u002Fresource\u002Fname\u002FS2050508624000246_inline1092.png?pub-status=live\" \u002F\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E$891$\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E classes to boundary divisors. In the chart, each row represents several rows of a block matrix. The number of rows in each group is listed to its left. The two half-edges glued to make a boundary divisor (pictured across the top) are labeled \u003Cspan class=\"italic\"\u003Eq\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E on the left vertex and \u003Cspan class=\"italic\"\u003Ep\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E on the right vertex.\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E",thumbnailSrc:bc,enlargedSrc:bc,attrib:[]},{contentId:"fig3",label:"Figure 3",description:"\u003Cspan class=\"p\"\u003EThe graph \u003Cspan class=\"alternatives\"\u003E\u003Cimg class=\"inline-graphic mathjax-alternative mathjax-alt-graphic mathjax-off\" data-mimesubtype=\"png\" data-type src=\"${staticDomain}\u002Fcontent\u002Fid\u002Furn:cambridge.org:id:article:S2050508624000246\u002Fresource\u002Fname\u002FS2050508624000246_inline1256.png?pub-status=live\" \u002F\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"mathjax-tex-wrapper\" data-mathjax-type=\"texmath\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"tex-math mathjax-tex-math mathjax-on\"\u003E$\\Gamma $\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E\u003C\u002Fspan\u003E on the left and 